TURATH_CHUNK(25,[{"num":5000,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَمَلَ مِنَ الْحَجَرِ الْأَسْوَدِ حَتَّى انْتَهَى إِلَيْهِ ثَلَاثَةَ أَطْوَافٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الحج (107) عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره. ومن طريقه رواه مسلم في الحج (1263)","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (107) and Muslim (1263).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform brisk walking from the Black Stone until he returned to it for three circuits."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (107)، ومسلم (1263)."},{"num":5001,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، قال: قَدِمَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ مَكَّةَ وَقَدْ وَهَنَتْهُمْ حُمَّى يَثْرِبَ. قَالَ المُشْرِكُونَ: إِنَّهُ يَقْدَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ غَدًا قَوْمٌ قَدْ وَهَنَتْهُمْ الحُمَّى، وَلَقُوا مِنْهَا شِدَّةً، فَجَلَسُوا مِمَّا يَلِي الحِجْرَ وَأَمَرَهُمْ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يَرْمُلُوا ثَلاثَةَ أَشْوَاطٍ وَيَمْشُوا مَا بَيْنَ الرُّكْنَيْنِ لِيَرَى المُشْرِكُونَ جَلَدَهُمْ. فَقَالَ المُشْرِكُونَ: هَؤُلاءِ الَّذِينَ زَعَمْتُمْ أَنَّ الحُمَّى قَدْ وَهَنَتْهُمْ؟ هَؤُلاءِ أَجْلَدُ مِنْ كَذَا وَكَذَا!!. قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: وَلَمْ يَمْنَعْهُ أَنْ يَأْمُرَهُمْ أَنْ يَرْمُلُوا الأَشْوَاطَ كُلَّهَا إِلا الإِبْقَاءُ عَلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1602)، ومسلم في الحج (1266) كلاهما من طريق حماد بن زيد، عن أيوب، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس، فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1602) and Muslim (1266). This is the wording of Muslim.","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions came to Mecca after the fever of Yathrib had weakened them. The idolaters said: Tomorrow there will come to you people whom the fever has weakened, and they have suffered severely from it. So they sat on the side near the enclosure. The Prophet ﷺ ordered his Companions to perform brisk walking in three circuits and to walk between the two corners, so that the idolaters might see their strength. The idolaters then said: Are these the ones about whom you claimed that the fever had weakened them? These are stronger than this and that. Ibn ‘Abbas said: What prevented him from ordering them to perform brisk walking in all the circuits was his mercy toward them."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “and walk between the two corners,” means in the place where the eyes of the idolaters would not fall upon them, because they were not positioned on that side."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9103,13331],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1602)، ومسلم (1266)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5002,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي الطّفيل، قال: قُلْتُ لابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: أَرَأَيْتَ هَذَا الرَّمَلَ بِالْبَيْتِ ثَلاثَةَ أَطْوَافٍ وَمَشْيَ أَرْبَعَةِ أَطْوَافٍ أَسُنَّةٌ هُوَ، فَإِنَّ قَوْمَكَ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّهُ سُنَّةٌ؟ قَالَ: فَقَال: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا!. قَال: قُلْتُ مَا قَوْلُكَ: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا؟ قَال: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ فَقَالَ المُشْرِكُونَ: إِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا وَأَصْحَابَهُ لا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ أَنْ يَطُوفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ مِنْ الهُزَالِ، وَكَانُوا يَحْسُدُونَهُ. قَالَ: فَأَمَرَهُمْ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يَرْمُلُوا ثَلاثًا وَيَمْشُوا أَرْبَعًا. قَال: قُلْتُ لَهُ: أَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ الطَّوَافِ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ رَاكِبًا أَسُنَّةٌ هُوَ، فَإِنَّ قَوْمَكَ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّهُ سُنَّةٌ؟ قَال: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا!. قَال: قُلْتُ: وَمَا قَوْلُكَ صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا؟ قَال: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَثُرَ عَلَيْهِ النَّاسُ، يَقُولُونَ: هَذَا مُحَمَّدٌ، هَذَا مُحَمَّدٌ، حَتَّى خَرَجَ الْعَوَاتِقُ مِنْ الْبُيُوتِ.","قَالَ: وَكَانَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لا يُضْرَبُ النَّاسُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا كَثُرَ عَلَيْهِ رَكِبَ، وَالمَشْيُ وَالسَّعْيُ أَفْضَلُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1264) من حديث سعيد بن إياس الجريريّ، وعبدالله بن أبي حسين، وعبدالملك بن سعيد بن الأبحر، كلّهم من حديث أبي الطفيل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1264).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu al-Tufayl said: I said to Ibn ‘Abbas, “Tell me about this brisk walking around the House for three circuits and walking for four circuits — is it a Sunnah? Your people claim that it is a Sunnah.” He said, “They are right and they are wrong.” I said, “What do you mean by: they are right and they are wrong?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Mecca, and the polytheists said: Muhammad and his companions are too weakened by emaciation to circle the House. They envied him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to walk briskly for three circuits and walk normally for four.” I said to him, “Tell me about going between al-Safa and al-Marwah while riding — is that a Sunnah? Your people claim that it is a Sunnah.” He said, “They are right and they are wrong.” I said, “What do you mean by: they are right and they are wrong?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was surrounded by many people, saying: This is Muhammad, this is Muhammad, until even young women came out from the houses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have the people struck away from in front of him, so when the crowd became too great, he rode. Walking and sa‘y are better.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “They are right and they are wrong,” means: they are right that the Prophet ﷺ did perform brisk walking around the House for three circuits, and they are wrong in claiming that it is a specifically intended and strongly emphasized Sunnah in itself, because the Prophet ﷺ did not establish it as a constantly intended practice repeated every year. Rather, he ordered it that year to show strength before the disbelievers, and that reason later ceased. This is the meaning of Ibn ‘Abbas’s statement, and it was his view that brisk walking was not a Sunnah. The majority of the Companions, the Followers, and those after them held that brisk walking is a recommended Sunnah; the circumambulation is valid without it, but its virtue is missed and no compensatory sacrifice is due.","This is also indicated by the saying of ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: “It is something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did, and we do not like to leave it.” A contrary report also came from Ibn ‘Abbas stating that brisk walking is a Sunnah, and that is what comes next."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1264)."},{"num":5003,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا نَزَلَ مَرَّ الظَّهْرَانِ فِي عُمْرَتِهِ، بَلَغَ أَصْحَابَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّ قُرَيْشًا تَقُولُ: مَا يَتَبَاعَثُونَ مِنَ العَجَفِ. فَقَالَ أَصْحَابُهُ: لَوِ انْتَحَرْنَا مِنْ ظَهْرِنَا، فَأَكَلْنَا مِنْ لَحْمِهِ، وَحَسَوْنَا مِنْ مَرَقِهِ، أَصْبَحْنَا غَدًا حِينَ نَدْخُلُ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ وَبِنَا جَمَامَةٌ؟ قَالَ: لَا تَفْعَلُوا، وَلَكِنِ اجْمَعُوا لِي مِنْ أَزْوَادِكُمْ، فَجَمَعُوا لَهُ، وَبَسَطُوا الْأَنْطَاعَ، فَأَكَلُوا حَتَّى تَوَلَّوْا، وَحَثَا كُلُّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمْ فِي جِرَابِهِ، ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى دَخَلَ الْمَسْجِدَ، وَقَعَدَتْ قُرَيْشٌ نَحْوَ الْحِجْرِ، فَاضْطَبَعَ بِرِدَائِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: لَا يَرَى الْقَوْمُ فِيكُمْ غَمِيزَةً. فَاسْتَلَمَ الرُّكْنَ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ حَتَّى إِذَا تَغَيَّبَ بِالرُّكْنِ الْيَمَانِي، مَشَى إِلَى الرُّكْنِ الْأَسْوَدِ، فَقَالَتْ قُرَيْشٌ: مَا يَرْضَوْنَ بِالْمَشْيِ، أَنَّهُمْ لَيَنْقُزُونَ نَقْزَ الظِّبَاءِ، فَفَعَلَ ذَلِكَ ثَلاثَةَ أَطْوَافٍ، فَكَانَتْ سُنَّةً.","قَالَ أَبُو الطُّفَيْلِ: وَأَخْبَرَنِي ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2782) عن محمد بن الصباح، حدّثنا إسماعيل ـ يعني ابن زكريا ـ ، عن عبدالله ـ يعني ابن عثمان ـ، عن أبي الطفيل، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (2782).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down at Marr al-Zahran during his ‘Umrah, the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned that Quraysh was saying: They can hardly move from weakness. His companions said: If we slaughtered some of our riding animals and ate from their meat and drank from their broth, then tomorrow when we enter upon the people we would have strength and fullness. He said: “Do not do that, but gather for me from your provisions.” So they gathered them for him and spread out leather cloths, and they ate until they were satisfied, and each one of them then scooped some back into his bag. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward until he entered the mosque, while Quraysh sat near the enclosure. He tucked his cloak under one arm and over the other shoulder, then said: “Let the people not see any weakness in you.” He touched the Corner, then proceeded, and when he was hidden at the Yemeni Corner he walked until the Black Stone. Quraysh said: They are not content just to walk; they are springing like gazelles. He did that for three circuits, and it became a Sunnah.","Abu al-Tufayl said: Ibn ‘Abbas also told me that the Prophet ﷺ did that in the Farewell Pilgrimage."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “and it became a Sunnah,” may indicate that he later revised his first view after the matter became clear to him. Abu al-Tufayl heard from him first the disapproval, then later heard the affirmation, so he narrated both forms, and Allah knows best. Also, the incident reported by Ibn ‘Abbas was during the Compensatory ‘Umrah, while the reports of Jabir, Ibn ‘Umar, and others were from the Farewell Pilgrimage, which came later.","His earlier words, “except out of mercy toward them,” mean that the Prophet ﷺ only refrained from commanding them to do brisk walking in all the circuits in order to preserve their strength, while still continuing what he and his companions had done in the Compensatory ‘Umrah. This explanation agrees with his statement, “and it became a Sunnah.” Abu al-Tufayl’s words, “Ibn ‘Abbas told me that the Prophet ﷺ did that in the Farewell Pilgrimage as well,” mean that the Prophet ﷺ repeated the brisk walking in the Farewell Pilgrimage too. This indicates its continuance even though the original reason for it had ended. This second statement from Ibn ‘Abbas agrees with the majority of the scholars that brisk walking in the first three circuits is a Sunnah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2782)."},{"num":5004,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أسلم مولى عمر، أنّ عمر بن الخطاب رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قال لِلرُّكْنِ: أَمَا وَالله إِنِّي لأَعْلَمُ أَنَّكَ حَجَرٌ لا تَضُرُّ وَلا تَنْفَعُ، وَلَوْلا أَنِّي رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ اسْتَلَمَكَ مَا اسْتَلَمْتُكَ، فَاسْتَلَمَهُ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: فَمَا لَنَا وَلِلرَّمَلِ إِنَّمَا كُنَّا رَاءَيْنَا بِهِ المُشْرِكِينَ وَقَدْ أَهْلَكَهُمْ الله. ثُمَّ قَالَ: شَيْءٌ صَنَعَهُ النَّبِيُّصَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَلا نُحِبُّ أَنْ نَتْرُكَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1605) عن سعيد بن أبي مريم، أخبرنا محمد بن جعفر، أخبرني زيد بن أسلم، عن أبيه، به، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1605).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Aslam, the freed servant of ‘Umar, narrated that ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Corner: By Allah, I know that you are only a stone; you neither harm nor benefit. Had I not seen the Prophet ﷺ touch you, I would not have touched you. Then he touched it and said: What have we to do with brisk walking? We only used to display strength by it before the polytheists, and Allah has destroyed them. Then he said: It is something the Prophet ﷺ did, and we do not like to leave it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1605)."},{"num":5005,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمر بن الخطاب، قال: فِيمَ الرَّمَلانُ الْيَوْمَ، وَالْكَشْفُ عَن المَنَاكِبِ، وَقَدْ أَطَّأَ الله الإِسْلامَ وَنَفَى الْكُفْرَ وَأَهْلَهُ؟! مَعَ ذَلِكَ لا نَدَعُ شَيْئًا كُنَّا نَفْعَلُهُ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1887) عن أحمد بن حنبل ـ وهو في مسنده (317) ـ، وابن ماجه (2952) كلّهم من حديث هشام بن سعد، عن زيد ابن أسلم، عن أبيه، قال: سمعت عمر يقول (فذكره).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرَّمَل في الأشواط الثلاثة الأولى في طواف العمرة، وفي الطواف الأول في الحجّ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1887), Ahmad in his Musnad (317), and Ibn Majah (2952). Ibn Khuzaymah graded it authentic (2708).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of brisk walking in the first three circuits of the lesser pilgrimage circumambulation and in the first circumambulation of the pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Why should there still be brisk walking today and uncovering of the shoulders, when Allah has firmly established Islam and removed disbelief and its people? Even so, we do not leave anything that we used to do during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Khuzaymah said: A Sunnah may be established by the Prophet ﷺ for a particular cause, then the cause disappears while the Sunnah remains forever. The Prophet ﷺ first performed brisk walking and uncovered his shoulder to show the polytheists his strength and the strength of his companions, and so the practices of uncovering the shoulder and brisk walking remained as enduring Sunnahs."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1887)، وأحمد في مسنده (317)، وابن ماجه (2952)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2708)."},{"num":5006,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ اضْطَبَعَ، فَاسْتَلَمَ وَكَبَّرَ، ثُمَّ رَمَلَ ثَلاثَةَ أَطْوَافٍ، وَكَانُوا إِذَا بَلَغُوا الرُّكْنَ الْيَمَانِيَ وَتَغَيَّبُوا مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ مَشَوْا، ثُمَّ يَطْلُعُونَ عَلَيْهِمْ يَرْمُلُونَ، تَقُولُ قُرَيْشٌ: كَأَنَّهُمْ الْغِزْلانُ. قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: فَكَانَتْ سُنَّةً."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1889)، وابن ماجه (2953) كلاهما من حديث ابن خثيم، عن أبي الطفيل، عن ابن عباس، فذكر الحديث، واللّفظ لأبي داود.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الاضطباع في الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1889) and Ibn Majah (2953), and the wording is that of Abu Dawud. In the wording of Ibn Majah, the Prophet ﷺ said to his companions when they intended to enter Mecca in his ‘Umrah after al-Hudaybiyah: “Your people will see you tomorrow, so let them see strength in you.”","chapter_en":"What has been narrated about uncovering the shoulder during circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Prophet ﷺ uncovered his shoulder, touched the Stone, said the takbir, then performed brisk walking for three circuits. When they reached the Yemeni Corner and were hidden from Quraysh, they walked normally, then when they came back into view they again performed brisk walking. Quraysh would then say: They are like gazelles. Ibn ‘Abbas said: So it became a Sunnah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1889)، وابن ماجه (2953)، واللفظ لأبي داود. وفي لفظ لابن ماجه: قال النبي ﷺ لأصحابه حين أرادوا دخول مكة في عمرته بعد الحديبية: (( إن قومكم غدا سيرونكم، فليرونكم جلدا ))."},{"num":5007,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَعْلَى، قَالَ: طَافَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُضْطَبِعًا بِبُرْدٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1883)، والترمذيّ (859)، وابن ماجه (2954) كلّهم من طريق سفيان، عن ابن جريج، عن عبد الحميد، عن ابن يعلى بن أمية، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الاضطباع في الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1883), al-Tirmidhi (859), and Ibn Majah (2954). Al-Tirmidhi said: It is a Hasan hadith.","chapter_en":"What has been narrated about uncovering the shoulder during circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ya‘la ibn Umayyah said: The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated while having one shoulder uncovered with a cloak wrapped in that manner."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1883)، والترمذي (859)، وابن ماجه (2954). قال الترمذي: حديث حسن."},{"num":5008,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أمِّ سلمة زوج النبيّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أنها قالت: شَكَوْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنِّي أَشْتَكِي، فَقَالَ: طُوفِي مِنْ وَرَاءِ النَّاسِ وَأَنْتِ رَاكِبَةٌ. قَالَتْ: فَطُفْتُ رَاكِبَةً بَعِيرِي وَرَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَئِذٍ يُصَلِّي إِلَى جَانِبِ الْبَيْتِ وَهُوَ يَقْرَأُ بِالطُّورِ (1) وَكِتَابٍ مَسْطُورٍ (2)."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (123) عن أبي الأسود محمد بن عبدالرحمن ابن نوفل، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن زينب بنت أبي سلمة، عن أم سلمة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (123), al-Bukhari (1633), and Muslim (1276).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was unwell, so he said: “Circumambulate behind the people while you are riding.” She said: So I circumambulated while riding my camel, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time was praying beside the House, reciting: “By the Mount, and by a written Book.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5019,13403],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (123)، والبخاري (1633)، ومسلم (1276)."},{"num":5009,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ طَافَ فِي حجّة الْوَدَاعِ عَلَى بَعِيرٍ، يَسْتَلِمُ الرُّكن بمِحْجَن."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1607)، ومسلم في الحج (1272) كلاهما من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني يونس، عن ابن شهاب، عن عبيدالله بن عبدالله بن عتبة، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1607) and Muslim (1272). Al-Bukhari also narrated it (1632) with the addition: “and he said the takbir.”","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated during the Farewell Pilgrimage while on a camel, touching the Corner with a crook."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “with a crook,” means a stick with a curved end."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1607)، ومسلم (1272). ورواه البخاري (1632) وزاد: (( وكبر ))."},{"num":5010,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر، قال: طَافَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْبَيْتِ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ يَسْتَلِمُ الحَجَرَ بِمِحْجَنِهِ لأَنْ يَرَاهُ النَّاسُ وَلِيُشْرِفَ وَلِيَسْأَلُوهُ فَإِنَّ النَّاسَ غَشُوهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1273) من طرق عن ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله، يقول (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1273).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House during the Farewell Pilgrimage while riding his mount, touching the Stone with his crook, so that the people could see him, so that he would be visible above them, and so that they could ask him, because the people had crowded around him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1273)."},{"num":5011,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الطُّفَيْلِ عامر بن وَاثِلَةَ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَطُوفُ بِالْبَيْتِ وَيَسْتَلِمُ الرُّكنَ بِمِحْجَنٍ مَعَهُ، ويقبِّلُ الْمِحْجَنَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1275) عن محمد بن المثنى، حدّثنا سليمان بن داود، حدثنا معروف بن خرّبوذ، قال: سمعت أبا الطفيل، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1275).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu al-Tufayl ‘Amir ibn Wathilah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulating the House and touching the Corner with a crook he had with him, and then kissing the crook."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1275)."},{"num":5012,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ،  طَافَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ حَوْلَ الْكَعْبَةِ عَلَى بَعِيرِهِ، يَسْتَلِمُ الرُّكْنَ كَرَاهِيَةَ أَنْ يُضْرَبَ عَنْهُ النَّاسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1274) عن الحكم بن موسى القنطريّ، حدّثنا شعيب بن إسحاق، عن هشام بن عروة، عن عروة، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1274).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the Ka‘bah during the Farewell Pilgrimage on his camel, touching the Corner, because he disliked that the people should be pushed away from him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1274)."},{"num":5013,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ صَفِيَّةَ بِنْتِ شَيْبَةَ، قَالَتْ: لَمَّا اطْمَأَنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمَكَّةَ عَامَ الْفَتْحِ طَافَ عَلَى بَعِيرٍ يَسْتَلِمُ الرُّكْنَ بِمِحْجَنٍ فِي يَدِهِ. قَالَتْ: وَأَنَا أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1878)، وابن ماجه (2947) كلاهما من حديث يونس بن بكير، حدثنا ابن إسحاق، حدثني محمد بن جعفر بن الزبير، عن عبيدالله بن عبدالله بن أبي ثور، عن صفية بنت شيبة، فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1878) and Ibn Majah (2947).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Safiyyah bint Shaybah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had settled in Mecca in the year of the Conquest, he circumambulated on a camel, touching the Corner with a crook in his hand. She said: And I was looking at him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9159],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1878)، وابن ماجه (2947)."},{"num":5014,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قُدَامَةَ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى نَاقَةٍ يَسْتَلِمُ الْحَجَرَ بِمِحْجَنِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15412)، وأبو يعلى (928)، والطبراني في الكبير (19/ح 78)، وفي \"الأوسط\" (8024) كلهم من طريق محرز بن عون، عن قرّان بن تمام الأسدي، عن أيمن بن نابل، عن قدامة بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (15414), Abu Ya‘la (928), al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (19/80), and in al-Awsat (8024).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qudamah ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a she-camel touching the Stone with his crook."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[4971],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (15412)، وأبو يعلى (928)، والطبراني في الكبير (19/80)، وفي الأوسط (8024)."},{"num":5015,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: طَافَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ الْقَصْوَاءِ يَوْمَ الْفَتْحِ، وَاسْتَلَمَ الرُّكْنَ بِمِحْجَنِهِ وَمَا وَجَدَ لَهَا مُنَاخًا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ حَتَّى أُخْرِجَتْ إِلَى بَطْنِ الْوَادِي فَأُنِيخَتْ، ثُمَّ حَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَمَا بَعْدُ، أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَذْهَبَ عَنْكُمْ عُبِّيَّةَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، إِنَّمَا النَّاسُ رَجُلَانِ: بَرٌّ تَقِيٌّ كَرِيمٌ عَلَى رَبِّهِ، وَفَاجِرٌ شَقِيٌّ هَيِّنٌ عَلَى رَبِّهِ، ثُمَّ تَلَا: ﴿يَاأَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنَّا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ وَأُنْثَى وَجَعَلْنَاكُمْ شُعُوبًا وَقَبَائِلَ لِتَعَارَفُوا﴾ [الحجرات: ١٣]، حَتَّى قَرَأَ الآيَةَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَقُولُ قَوْلِي هَذَا وَأَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ لِي وَلَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (3828) ـ واللّفظ له ـ، وابن خزيمة (2781) كلاهما من حديث محمد بن عبدالله بن يزيد المقرئ، ثنا عبدالله بن رجاء، عن موسى بن عقبة، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الطواف راكبًا لمرض أو عذر، واستلام الحجر بمحجن وغيره، وتقبيله أو الإشارة إليه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (3828) — and this is his wording — and Ibn Khuzaymah (2781).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of circumambulating while riding due to illness or an excuse, and touching the Stone with a crook or something similar, then kissing it or pointing to it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated on his she-camel al-Qaswa’ on the day of the Conquest, and touched the Corner with his crook. He did not find a place for it to kneel in the mosque until it was taken out to the bottom of the valley and made to kneel there. Then he praised Allah and extolled Him and said: “To proceed: O people, Allah has removed from you the arrogance of the age of ignorance. O people, mankind are only of two kinds: a righteous, Allah-fearing person who is noble before his Lord, and a wicked, miserable person who is insignificant before his Lord.” Then he recited: “O mankind, We created you from a male and a female and made you peoples and tribes so that you may know one another” [49:13], until he completed the verse, then said: “I say this and seek Allah’s forgiveness for me and for you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (3828) - واللفظ له -، وابن خزيمة (2781)."},{"num":5016,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَرَّ وَهُوَ يَطُوفُ بِالْكَعْبَةِ بِإِنْسَانٍ رَبَطَ يَدَهُ إِلَى إِنْسَانٍ بِسَيْرٍ أَوْ بِخَيْطٍ أَوْ بِشَيْءٍ غَيْرِ ذَلِكَ، فَقَطَعَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ ثُمَّ قَالَ: قُدْهُ بِيَدِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1620)، عن إبراهيم بن موسى، حدّثنا هشام، أن ابن جريج أخبرهم قال: أخبرني سليمان الأحول، أنّ طاوساً أخبره، عن ابن عباس، فذكره كما مضى.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الكلام المباح والأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر في الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1620). He also narrated it (6703), in which it says: “He was leading a man by a nose-rope placed in his nose.”","chapter_en":"The permissibility of lawful speech, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong during circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Prophet ﷺ passed by, while circumambulating the Ka‘bah, a man whose hand had been tied to another man with a strap, a string, or something else. The Prophet ﷺ cut it with his own hand and then said: “Lead him by his hand.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["A khizamah is a ring-like loop made of hair or wool placed in the partition between a camel’s nostrils, in which the rein is tied so that it can be led easily."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14768],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1620). ورواه أيضا bukhari(6703)، وفيه: (( يقود إنسانا بخزامة في أنفه ))."},{"num":5017,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، أنّ النبيّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قال:الطَّوَافُ حَوْلَ الْبَيْتِ مِثْلُ الصَّلاةِ إِلا أَنَّكُمْ تَتَكَلَّمُونَ فِيهِ، فَمَنْ تَكَلَّمَ فِيهِ فَلا يَتَكَلَّمَنَّ إِلا بِخَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (960) عن قتيبة، حدّثنا جرير، عن عطاء بن السائب، عن طاوس، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الكلام المباح والأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر في الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (960), and Ibn Khuzaymah graded it authentic (2739).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of lawful speech, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong during circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Circumambulation around the House is like prayer, except that you speak in it. So whoever speaks in it should speak only good.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (960)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2739)."},{"num":5018,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن جريج، قال: أخبرني عطاء إِذْ مَنَعَ ابْنُ هِشَامٍ النِّسَاءَ الطَّوَافَ مَعَ الرِّجَالِ. قَال: كَيْفَ يَمْنَعُهُنَّ وَقَدْ طَافَ نِسَاءُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَ الرِّجَالِ؟! قُلْتُ: أَبَعْدَ الحِجَابِ أَوْ قَبْلُ؟ قَال: إِي لَعَمْرِي لَقَدْ أَدْرَكْتُهُ بَعْدَ الحِجَابِ. قُلْتُ: كَيْفَ يُخَالِطْنَ الرِّجَالَ؟ قَالَ: لَمْ يَكُنَّ يُخَالِطْنَ، كَانَتْ عَائِشَةُ رَضِيَ الله عَنْهَا تَطُوفُ حَجْرَةً مِنْ الرِّجَالِ لا تُخَالِطُهُمْ، فَقَالَتْ امْرَأَةٌ: انْطَلِقِي نَسْتَلِمْ يَا أُمَّ المُؤْمِنِينَ. قَالَتْ: انْطَلِقِي عَنْكِ، وَأَبَتْ. يَخْرُجْنَ مُتَنَكِّرَاتٍ بِاللَّيْلِ فَيَطُفْنَ مَعَ الرِّجَالِ، وَلَكِنَّهُنَّ كُنَّ إِذَا دَخَلْنَ الْبَيْتَ قُمْنَ حَتَّى يَدْخُلْنَ وَأُخْرِجَ الرِّجَالُ، وَكُنْتُ آتِي عَائِشَةَ أَنَا وَعُبَيْدُ بْنُ عُمَيْرٍ وَهِيَ مُجَاوِرَةٌ فِي جَوْفِ ثَبِيرٍ. قُلْتُ: وَمَا حِجَابُهَا؟ قَالَ: هِيَ فِي قُبَّةٍ تُرْكِيَّةٍ لَهَا غِشَاءٌ، وَمَا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهَا غَيْرُ ذَلِكَ، وَرَأَيْتُ عَلَيْهَا دِرْعًا مُوَرَّدًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1618) عن عمرو بن علي، حدّثنا أبو عاصم، عن ابن جريج، به، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب طواف النساء مع الرجال من غير اختلاط ما أمكن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1618).","chapter_en":"Women circumambulating with men without mixing, as much as possible","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Jurayj said: ‘Ata’ informed me that when Ibn Hisham prevented women from circumambulating with men, he said: How can he prevent them when the wives of the Prophet ﷺ circumambulated with men? I said: Was that after the command of veiling or before it? He said: Yes, by my life, I witnessed it after veiling. I said: How did they mix with men? He said: They did not mix. ‘A’ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, would circumambulate separately from the men and would not mix with them. A woman said to her: Let us go touch the Stone, O Mother of the Believers. She said: Go yourself, and she refused. They would go out disguised at night and circumambulate with the men, but when they intended to enter the House, they would wait until the men had entered and been taken out. I used to come to ‘A’ishah with ‘Ubayd ibn ‘Umayr while she was staying in devotion in the interior of Thabir. I said: What was her screen? He said: She was in a Turkish tent with a covering, and there was nothing between us and her except that. And I saw a pink cover on her."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “Ibn Hisham,” refers to Ibrahim or his brother Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, and that occurred during the caliphate of Hisham ibn ‘Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan.","The word hajrah here means a side or separate area.","In another narration it is read as hajzah with a zay instead of a ra’, meaning that a cloth barrier separated her from the men."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1618)."},{"num":5019,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أمِّ سلمة زوج النبيّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أنها قالت: شَكَوْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنِّي أَشْتَكِي، فَقَالَ: طُوفِي مِنْ وَرَاءِ النَّاسِ وَأَنْتِ رَاكِبَةٌ. قَالَتْ: فَطُفْتُ رَاكِبَةً بَعِيرِي وَرَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَئِذٍ يُصَلِّي إِلَى جَانِبِ الْبَيْتِ وَهُوَ يَقْرَأُ بِالطُّورِ وَكِتَابٍ مَسْطُور."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (123) عن أبي الأسود محمد بن","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز طواف المرأة عند إقامة الصلاة لعذر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (123), al-Bukhari (1626), and Muslim (1276).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of a woman performing tawaf when the prayer is established due to an excuse","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was ill, so he said: “Perform tawaf behind the people while you are riding.” She said: So I performed tawaf riding my camel, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying beside the House and reciting: “By the Mount, and by a written Book.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration: “When the dawn prayer is established, then perform tawaf on your camel while the people are praying.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5008,13403],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (123)، والبخاري (1626)، ومسلم (1276)."},{"num":5020,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة، قالت: قَدِمْتُ مَكَّةَ وَأَنَا حَائِضٌ وَلَمْ أَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ وَلا بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ. قَالَتْ: فَشَكَوْتُ ذَلِكَ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: افْعَلِي كَمَا يَفْعَلُ الحَاجُّ غَيْرَ أَنْ لا تَطُوفِي بِالْبَيْتِ حَتَّى تَطْهُرِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1650) عن عبدالله بن يوسف، أخبرنا مالك، عن عبدالرحمن بن القاسم، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحائض تفعل كلَّ ما يفعله الحاج غير أنها لا تطوف بالبيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1650) and Muslim (1211:119).","chapter_en":"A menstruating woman does everything that the pilgrim does except that she does not circumambulate the House","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Aisha said: I arrived in Mecca while menstruating, and I did not circumambulate the House nor go between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Do as the pilgrim does, except that you must not circumambulate the House until you become pure.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Aisha also said, in a narration recorded by al-Bukhari (294) and Muslim (1211:119): “We set out considering only Hajj. When we were at Sarif, I menstruated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was crying and said: ‘What is the matter? Have you begun menstruating?’ I said: Yes. He said: ‘This is something Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Adam, so do what the pilgrim does, except that you do not circumambulate the House.’” She said: “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered cattle on behalf of his wives.”","Al-Bukhari (305) and Muslim (1211:120) also narrated in it: “So do what the pilgrim does, except that you do not circumambulate the House until you become pure.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1650)، ومسلم (119: 1211)."},{"num":5021,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حفصة، قالت: كُنَّا نَمْنَعُ عَوَاتِقَنَا أَنْ يَخْرُجْنَ، فَقَدِمَتْ امْرَأَةٌ فَنَزَلَتْ قَصْرَ بَنِي خَلَفٍ فَحَدَّثَتْ أَنَّ أُخْتَهَا كَانَتْ تَحْتَ رَجُلٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ غَزَا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ثِنْتَيْ عَشْرَةَ غَزْوَةً، وَكَانَتْ أُخْتِي مَعَهُ فِي سِتِّ غَزَوَاتٍ، قَالَتْ: كُنَّا نُدَاوِي الْكَلْمَى وَنَقُومُ عَلَى المَرْضَى، فَسَأَلَتْ أُخْتِي رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَتْ: هَلْ عَلَى إِحْدَانَا بَأْسٌ إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهَا جِلْبَابٌ أَنْ لا تَخْرُجَ؟ قَال: لِتُلْبِسْهَا صَاحِبَتُهَا مِنْ جِلْبَابِهَا، وَلْتَشْهَدْ الخَيْرَ وَدَعْوَةَ المُؤْمِنِينَ. فَلَمَّا قَدِمَتْ أُمُّ عَطِيَّةَ رَضِيَ الله عَنْهَا سَأَلْنَهَا - أَوْ قَالَتْ سَأَلْنَاهَا- فَقَــــالَتْ - وَكَانَتْ لا تَذْكُرُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبَدًا إِلا قَالَتْ: بِأَبِي -. فَقُلْنَا: أَسَمِعْتِ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ كَذَا وَكَذَا؟ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ بِأَبِي، فَقَالَ: لِتَخْرُج الْعَوَاتِقُ ذَوَاتُ الخُدُورِ - أَوْ الْعَوَاتِقُ وَذَوَاتُ الخُدُورِ – الحيَّضُ، فَيَشْهَدْنَ الخَيْرَ وَدَعْوَةَ المُسْلِمِينَ وَيَعْتَزِلُ الحُيَّضُ المُصَلَّى.","فَقُلْتُ: الحَائِضُ؟ فَقَالَتْ: أَوَلَيْسَ تَشْهَدُ عَرَفَةَ، وَتَشْهَدُ كَذَا وَتَشْهَدُ كَذَا؟!."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1652) من طريق أيوب، عن حفصة (هي بنت سيرين)، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحائض تفعل كلَّ ما يفعله الحاج غير أنها لا تطوف بالبيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1652) and Muslim (890).","chapter_en":"A menstruating woman does everything that the pilgrim does except that she does not circumambulate the House","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hafsah said: We used to keep our young women from going out. Then a woman came and stayed at the palace of Banu Khalaf, and she related that her sister had been married to one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who had gone out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in twelve military expeditions, and my sister had gone with him in six expeditions. She said: We used to tend the wounded and care for the sick. My sister asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: Is there any blame upon one of us if she does not have a jilbab and therefore does not go out? He said: “Let her companion lend her one of her jilbabs so that she may witness the good and the supplication of the believers.” Then when Umm ‘Atiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, came, we asked her — or she said: we asked her — and she said — and she would never mention the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that she would say, “May my father be sacrificed for him” — so we said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say such-and-such? She said: Yes, may my father be sacrificed for him. He said: “Let the young women in seclusion, and the women in their private quarters, and the menstruating women go out so that they may witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims, but the menstruating women must keep away from the prayer area.” I said: Even the menstruating woman? She said: Does she not attend ‘Arafah, and attend such-and-such, and attend such-and-such?"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1652)، ومسلم (890)."},{"num":5022,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: أَهَلَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هُوَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ بِالحَج...وَحَاضَتْ عَائِشَةُ رَضِيَ الله عَنْهَا فَنَسَكَت المَنَاسِكَ كُلَّهَا غَيْرَ أَنَّهَا لَمْ تَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ، فَلَمَّا طَهُرَتْ طَافَتْ بِالْبَيْتِ قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ الله، تَنْطَلِقُونَ بِحَجَّةٍ وَعُمْرَةٍ وَأَنْطَلِقُ بِحَجٍّ؟! فَأَمَرَ عبدالرحمن بْنَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ أَنْ يَخْرُجَ مَعَهَا إِلَى التَّنْعِيمِ فَاعْتَمَرَتْ بَعْدَ الحَجِّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1651) عن محمد بن المثنى، حدّثنا عبد الوهاب ـ قال: وقال لي خليفة:حدّثنا عبد الوهاب، حدّثنا حبيب المعلِّم، عن عطاء، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحائض تفعل كلَّ ما يفعله الحاج غير أنها لا تطوف بالبيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1651).","chapter_en":"A menstruating woman does everything that the pilgrim does except that she does not circumambulate the House","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: The Prophet ﷺ and his companions entered into ihram for Hajj … and Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, menstruated, so she performed all the rites except that she did not circumambulate the House. When she became pure, she circumambulated the House. She said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you are returning with Hajj and ‘Umrah while I return with only Hajj? So he ordered ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr to go out with her to al-Tan‘im, and she performed ‘Umrah after Hajj."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1651)."},{"num":5023,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: أَقْبَلْنَا مُهِلِّينَ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِحَجٍّ مُفْرَدٍ...ثُمَّ دَخَلَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ الله عَنْهَا فَوَجَدَهَا تَبْكِي فَقَالَ: مَا شَأْنُكِ؟. قَالَتْ: شَأْنِي أَنِّي قَدْ حِضْتُ، وَقَدْ حَلَّ النَّاسُ وَلَمْ أَحْلِلْ، وَلَمْ أَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ وَالنَّاسُ يَذْهَبُونَ إِلَى الحَجِّ الآنَ؟ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ هَذَا أَمْرٌ كَتَبَهُ الله عَلَى بَنَاتِ آدَمَ، فَاغْتَسِلِي، ثُمَّ أَهِلِّي بِالحَجِّ. فَفَعَلَتْ وَوَقَفَتْ المَوَاقِفَ حَتَّى إِذَا طَهَرَتْ طَافَتْ بِالْكَعْبَةِ وَالصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ. ثُمَّ قَال: قَدْ حَلَلْتِ مِنْ حَجِّكِ وَعُمْرَتِكِ جَمِيعًا. فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ الله، إِنِّي أَجِدُ فِي نَفْسِي أَنِّي لَمْ أَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ حَتَّى حَجَجْتُ. قَال: فَاذْهَبْ بِهَا يَا عبدالرحمن فَأَعْمِرْهَا مِنْ التَّنْعِيمِ. وَذَلِكَ لَيْلَةَ الحَصْبَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1213) من طريق الليث بن سعد، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحائض تفعل كلَّ ما يفعله الحاج غير أنها لا تطوف بالبيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1213).","chapter_en":"A menstruating woman does everything that the pilgrim does except that she does not circumambulate the House","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: We came entering ihram with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for Hajj alone. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and found her crying. He said: “What is the matter with you?” She said: My situation is that I have menstruated, while the people have exited ihram and I have not exited ihram, and I have not circumambulated the House, while the people are now heading to Hajj. He said: “This is something Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Adam, so bathe and then enter ihram for Hajj.” So she did that and stood at the standing places, until when she became pure, she circumambulated the Ka‘bah and al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said: “You have now exited from both your Hajj and your ‘Umrah together.” She said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I still feel uneasy that I did not circumambulate the House until after I had done Hajj. He said: “Take her, O ‘Abd al-Rahman, and let her perform ‘Umrah from al-Tan‘im.” And that was on the night of al-Hasbah."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His words, “until when she became pure, she circumambulated the Ka‘bah and al-Safa and al-Marwah,” indicate that Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, did not perform sa‘y until after she had performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah. She herself explicitly stated: “I arrived in Mecca while menstruating, and I did not circumambulate the House nor go between al-Safa and al-Marwah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1213)."},{"num":5024,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر، قال: قال رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الاسْتِجْمَارُ تَوٌّ، وَرَمْيُ الجِمَارِ تَوٌّ، وَالسَّعْيُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ تَوٌّ، وَالطَّوَافُ تَوٌّ، وَإِذَا اسْتَجْمَرَ أَحَدُكُمْ فَلْيَسْتَجْمِرْ بِتَوٍّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1300) عن سلمة بن شبيب، حدّثنا الحسن بن أعين، حدّثنا معقل (وهو ابن عبيدالله الجزريّ)، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الطواف وتر والسعي وتر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1300).","chapter_en":"What has been narrated that tawaf is an odd-numbered rite and sa‘y is an odd-numbered rite","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":48,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cleaning oneself with stones is done in odd numbers, the stoning of the pillars is in odd numbers, sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah and tawaf are in odd numbers, and when one of you cleans himself with stones, let him do so in an odd number.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “witr,” means an odd number."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1382],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1300)."},{"num":5025,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر: أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا طَافَ فِي الحَجِّ وَالْعُمْرَةِ أَوَّلَ مَا يَقْدَمُ فَإِنَّهُ يَسْعَى ثَلاثَةَ أَطْوَافٍ بِالْبَيْتِ، ثُمَّ يَمْشِي أَرْبَعَةً، ثُمَّ يُصَلِّي سَجْدَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ يَطُوفُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1616)، ومسلم في الحج (1261: 231) كلاهما من طريق موسى بن عقبة، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لكل سبعة أشواط ركعتان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1616) and Muslim (1261:231), and the wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"For every seven circuits there are two rak‘ahs","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf in Hajj or ‘Umrah on first arriving, he would walk briskly for three circuits around the House, then walk normally for four, then pray two rak‘ahs, then go between al-Safa and al-Marwah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1616)، ومسلم (1261: 231)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5026,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر، قال: قَدِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَطَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ سَبْعًا وَصَلَّى خَلْفَ المَقَامِ رَكْعَتَيْنِ ثُمَّ خَرَجَ إِلَى الصَّفَا وَقَدْ قَالَ الله تَعَالَى: لَقَدْ ﴿كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 21]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1627) عن آدم، حدّثنا شعبة، حدّثنا عمرو بن دينار، قال: سمعت ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب صلاة ركعتي الطواف خلف المقام، والقراءة فيهما بـ {قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ} و{قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ}","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1627), also (1644, 1623), and Muslim (1234:189) through Sufyan ibn ‘Uyaynah, from ‘Amr ibn Dinar, who said: We asked Ibn ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, about a man who circumambulated the House in ‘Umrah but did not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah — may he go to his wife? So he mentioned this hadith. Al-Bukhari added: We also asked Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he said: “He must not go near her until he has gone between al-Safa and al-Marwah.”","chapter_en":"The recommendation of praying the two rak‘ahs of tawaf behind the Maqam, and reciting in them “Say: He is Allah, One” and “Say: O disbelievers”","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ arrived, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak‘ahs behind the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa. Allah Most High has said: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have an excellent example.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1627، 1644، 1623)، ومسلم (189: 1234). وزاد البخاري: وسألنا جابر بن عبد الله رضي الله عنهما، فقال: (( لا يقربنها حتى يطوف بين الصفا والمروة ))."},{"num":5027,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: ثُمَّ نَفَذَ (يعني رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ) إِلَى مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلام فَقَرَأَ: ﴿وَاتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى﴾، [سورة البقرة: 125]، فَجَعَلَ المَقَامَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ الْبَيْتِ - فَكَانَ أَبِي يَقُولُ: وَلا أَعْلَمُهُ ذَكَرَهُ إِلا عَنْ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَانَ يَقْرَأُ فِي الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ ، و قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ ، ثُمَّ رَجَعَ إِلَى الرُّكْنِ فَاسْتَلَمَه."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره بطوله في صفة حجّة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب صلاة ركعتي الطواف خلف المقام، والقراءة فيهما بـ {قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ} و{قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ}","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of praying the two rak‘ahs of tawaf behind the Maqam, and reciting in them “Say: He is Allah, One” and “Say: O disbelievers”","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: Then he went forward — meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — to the Maqam of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and recited: “And take the standing place of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.” He placed the Maqam between himself and the House — and my father used to say, and I only know that he mentioned it from the Prophet ﷺ — that he used to recite in the two rak‘ahs: “Say: He is Allah, One” and “Say: O disbelievers.” Then he returned to the Corner and touched it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5028,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جبير بن مطعم، قال: قال رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا بَنِي عَبْدِ مَنَافٍ، لا تَمْنَعُوا أَحَدًا يَطُوفُ بِهَذَا الْبَيْتِ وَيُصَلِّي أَيَّ سَاعَةٍ شَاءَ مِنْ لَيْلٍ أَوْ نَهَارٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1894)، والترمذيّ (868)، والنسائي (2924)، وابن ماجه (1254) كلّهم من حديث سفيان بن عيينة، عن أبي الزبير، عن عبدالله بن باباه، عن جبير بن مطعم، فذكر الحديث. وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (1280)، وابن حبان (1552)، والحاكم (1643) وقال: صحيح على شرط مسلم. وقد روي أيضاً من أوجه أخرى تقوّيه.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الطواف بعد الصبح والعصر، وأداء ركعتي الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1894), al-Tirmidhi (868), al-Nasa’i (2924), and Ibn Majah (1254). It was graded authentic by Ibn Khuzaymah (1280), Ibn Hibban (1552), and al-Hakim (1/448). Al-Tirmidhi said: “A Hasan Sahih hadith.”","chapter_en":"Performing tawaf after dawn and after ‘Asr, and praying the two rak‘ahs of tawaf","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Banu ‘Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House and prays at any hour he wishes, by night or by day.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10611],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1894)، والترمذي (868)، والنسائي (2924)، وابن ماجه (1254)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (1280)، وابن حبان (1552)، والحاكم (1643). وقال الترمذي: (( حديث حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5029,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أمِّ سَلَمَةَ زَوْجِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهَا قَالَتْ: شَكَوتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنِّي أشْتَكِي، فَقَالَ: طُوفِي مِنْ وَرَاءِ النَّاس وَأَنْتِ رَاكِبَةٌ.","وفي رواية: إذا أقميت صلاةُ الصُّبح فطوفي على بعيرك والنّاسُ يصلّون. ففعلتْ ذلك، فلم تصلِّ حتى خرجتْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (123) عن أبي الأسود محمد بن عبدالرحمن بن نوفل، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن زينب بنت أبي سلمة، عن أم سلمة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من طاف بعد الصبح ولم يصل ركعتي الطواف حتى طلعت الشمس وأداؤهما خارج المسجد الحرام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (123), al-Bukhari (1633), and Muslim (1276). The second narration was narrated by al-Bukhari (1626).","chapter_en":"Whoever performs tawaf after dawn and does not pray its two rak‘ahs until the sun rises, and praying them outside al-Masjid al-Haram","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was ill, so he said: “Perform tawaf behind the people while you are riding.” In another narration: “When the dawn prayer is established, then perform tawaf on your camel while the people are praying.” So she did that, and she did not pray until she had gone out."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (123)، والبخاري (1633)، ومسلم (1276). والرواية الثانية: رواها البخاري (1626)."},{"num":5030,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: فَجَعَلَ (يعني النبيّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ) المَقَامَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ الْبَيْتِ - فَكَانَ أَبِي يَقُولُ وَلا أَعْلَمُهُ ذَكَرَهُ إِلا عَنْ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقْرَأُ فِي الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ: قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ ، و قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ ، ثُمَّ رَجَعَ إِلَى الرُّكْنِ فَاسْتَلَمَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الرجوع إلى الحجر الأسود لاستلامه بعد ركعتي الطواف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of returning to the Black Stone to touch it after the two rak‘ahs of tawaf","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":53,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: He — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — placed the Maqam between himself and the House. My father used to say — and I only know that he mentioned it from the Prophet ﷺ — that he used to recite in the two rak‘ahs: “Say: He is Allah, One” and “Say: O disbelievers,” then he returned to the Corner and touched it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5031,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عروة، قال: قلتُ لِعَائِشَةَ أُمِّ المُؤْمِنِينَ - وَأَنَا يَوْمَئِذٍ حَدِيثُ السِّنِّ -: أَرَأَيْتِ قَوْلَ الله تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى: ﴿إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا﴾ [البقرة: 158]، فَمَا عَلَى الرَّجُلِ شَيْءٌ أَنْ لا يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا؟ فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: كَلا! لَوْ كَانَ كَمَا تَقُولُ، لَكَانَتْ فَلا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ لا يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا؛ إِنَّمَا أُنْزِلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ فِي الأَنْصَارِ كَانُوا يُهِلُّونَ لمَنَاةَ، وَكَانَتْ مَنَاةُ حَذْوَ قُدَيْدٍ، وَكَانُوا يَتَحَرَّجُونَ أَنْ يَطُوفُوا بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ، فَلَمَّا جَاءَ الإِسْلامُ سَأَلُوا رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنْ ذَلِكَ فَأَنْزَلَ الله تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى: ﴿إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا﴾. [سورة البقرة: 158]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (129) عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، قال (فذكره). ورواه البخاريّ في الحج (1790) من طريق مالك، به، مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب السعي بين الصفا والمروة في الحج والعمرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (129), al-Bukhari (1790), and Muslim (1277:259).","chapter_en":"The obligation of sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah in Hajj and ‘Umrah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":54,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Urwah said: I said to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers — and I was young at that time — “What do you think about the statement of Allah, Blessed and Most High: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj of the House or performs ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him that he goes between them’ — does that mean there is no issue if a person does not go between them?” Aisha said: No. If it were as you say, then it would have said: ‘there is no blame upon him if he does not go between them.’ Rather, this verse was revealed concerning the Ansar. They used to enter ihram for Manat, and Manat was near Qudayd, and they used to feel uneasy about going between al-Safa and al-Marwah. So when Islam came, they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and Allah, Blessed and Most High, revealed: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj of the House or performs ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him that he goes between them.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Khuzaymah also narrated it (2769), in which Aisha said: By my life, Allah has not completed the Hajj of the one who does not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah, because Allah Most High says: “Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,” and they are among the symbols of Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (129)، والبخاري (1790)، ومسلم (259: 1277)."},{"num":5032,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عاصم، قال: قلت لأنس بن مالك: أَكُنْتُمْ تَكْرَهُونَ السَّعْيَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ؟ قَال: نَعَمْ لِأَنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ الجَاهِلِيَّةِ حَتَّى أَنْزَلَ الله: ﴿إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا﴾. [سورة البقرة: 158]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1648)، ومسلم في الحجّ (1278) كلاهما من طريق عاصم (هو ابن سليمان الأحول)، به، واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب السعي بين الصفا والمروة في الحج والعمرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1648) and Muslim (1278), and the wording is that of al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"The obligation of sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah in Hajj and ‘Umrah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":54,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Asim said: I said to Anas ibn Malik, “Did you use to dislike sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah?” He said: “Yes, because it had been among the rites of the age of ignorance, until Allah revealed: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj of the House or performs ‘Umrah, there is no blame upon him that he goes between them.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement of Allah Most High, “Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,” indicates that going between them is a binding rite that cannot be omitted, because the symbols of Allah are great matters that must not be treated lightly."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1648)، ومسلم (1278)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":5033,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ بن أبي طالب: أَنَّهُ رَأَى رَسُولَ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَسْعَى بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ فِي الْمَسْعَى كَاشِفًا عَنْ ثَوْبِهِ، قَدْ بَلَغَ إِلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه عبدالله أحمد من زياداته على المسند (597) عن أبي عبدالرحمن عبدالله بن أبي زياد القطوانيّ، حدّثنا زيد بن الحباب، أخبرني حرب أبو سفيان المنقريّ، حدّثنا محمد بن علي أبو جعفر، حدّثني عمّي، عن أبي، أنه رأى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب كيف السعي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by ‘Abdullah ibn Ahmad in his additions to al-Musnad (597), and al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1117).","chapter_en":"How the sa‘y is performed","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib reported that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah in the place of sa‘y, with his garment lifted, reaching up to his knees."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد من زياداته على المسند (597)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1117)."},{"num":5034,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حبيبة بنت أبي تَجراة، قالت: دَخَلْنَا دَارَ أَبِي حُسَيْنٍ فِي نِسْوَةٍ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ وَالنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَطُوفَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ، قَالَتْ: وَهُوَ يَسْعَى يَدُورُ بِهِ إِزَارُهُ مِنْ شِدَّةِ السَّعْيِ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ لأَصْحَابِهِ: اسْعَوْا فَإِنَّ الله كَتَبَ عَلَيْكُمْ السَّعْيَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: وله طرق منها:","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب كيف السعي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (27367) — and this is his wording — al-Tabarani (24/227), and al-Daraqutni (2584).","chapter_en":"How the sa‘y is performed","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Habibah bint Abi Tajrah said: We entered the house of Abu Husayn along with some women of Quraysh while the Prophet ﷺ was going between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: He was moving quickly, and his lower garment was turning about him because of the intensity of his sa‘y, and he was saying to his companions: “Perform sa‘y, for Allah has prescribed sa‘y upon you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27367) - واللفظ له -، والطبراني (24/227)، والدارقطني (2584)."},{"num":5035,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعِيدِ بْنِ جُبَيْرٍ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ ابْنَ عُمَرَ يَمْشِي بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنْ مَشَيْتُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمْشِي، وَإِنْ سَعَيْتُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَسْعَى."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النّسائيّ (2977)، والإمام أحمد (6393) كلاهما من حديث عبدالرزاق- وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (2772) ورواه من طريق الضّحّاك ـ كلاهما عن سفيان الثوريّ، عن عبد الكريم الجزريّ، عن سعيد بن جبير، فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كيف السعي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (2977) and Imam Ahmad (6393).","chapter_en":"How the sa‘y is performed","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":55,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sa‘id ibn Jubayr said: I saw Ibn ‘Umar walking between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walk; and if I move quickly, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ move quickly."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (2977)، والإمام أحمد (6393)."},{"num":5036,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر: أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا طَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ الطَّوَافَ الأَوَّلَ خَبَّ ثَلاثًا وَمَشَى أَرْبَعًا، وَكَانَ يَسْعَى بِبَطْنِ المَسِيلِ إِذَا طَافَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ.","وَكَانَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ يَفْعَلُ ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحج (1617)، ومسلم في الحج (1261: 230) كلاهما من حديث عبيدالله بن عمر، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السعي في بطن المسيل بشدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1617) and Muslim (1261/230).","chapter_en":"Moving quickly in the bottom of the valley","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":56,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the first tawaf around the House, he would move briskly for three circuits and walk for four, and he would move quickly in the bottom of the valley when he went between al-Safa and al-Marwah.","And Ibn ‘Umar used to do that."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “the bottom of the valley,” means the place where the floodwater gathers, and it is now known as the area between the two green markers."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1617)، ومسلم (1261: 230)."},{"num":5037,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، قال: إِنَّمَا سَعَى رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْبَيْتِ وَبَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ لِيُرِيَ المُشْرِكِينَ قُوَّتَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1649)، ومسلم في الحج (1265: 241) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن عمرو (هو ابن دينار)، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السعي في بطن المسيل بشدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1649) and Muslim (1265/241).","chapter_en":"Moving quickly in the bottom of the valley","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":56,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only moved quickly around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah in order to show the idolaters his strength."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1649)، ومسلم (1265: 241)."},{"num":5038,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله: أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا نَزَلَ مِن الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ مَشَى، حَتَّى إِذَا انْصَبَّتْ قَدَمَاهُ فِي بَطْنِ الْوَادِي سَعَى حَتَّى يَخْرُجَ مِنْهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الحج (131) عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره. ورواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طرق عن حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، قال: ... ثم نزل إلى المروة، حتى إذا انصبَّتْ قدماه في بطن الوادي سعى، حتّى إذا صعدتا مشى، حتى أتى المروة الحديث في صفة حجة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السعي في بطن المسيل بشدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (131) and Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Moving quickly in the bottom of the valley","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":56,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from al-Safa toward al-Marwah, he would walk until his feet reached the bottom of the valley, then he would move quickly until he came out of it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (131)، ومسلم (1218)."},{"num":5039,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن صفية بنت شيبة، عن امرأة قالت: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَسْعَى فِي بَطْنِ المَسِيلِ، وَيَقُولُ: لا يُقْطَعُ الْوَادِي إِلا شَدًّا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائيّ (2980)، والإمام أحمد (27281)، والبيهقيّ (9368) كلّهم من حديث حماد بن زيد، عن بُديل بن ميسرة، عن المغيرة بن حكيم، عن صفية بنت شيبة، عن امرأة، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السعي في بطن المسيل بشدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (2980), Imam Ahmad (27281), and al-Bayhaqi (5/98).","chapter_en":"Moving quickly in the bottom of the valley","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":56,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrated from a woman, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing sa‘y in the bottom of the valley and saying: “The valley is not crossed except with vigorous movement.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This applies specifically to men and not to women."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (2980)، والإمام أحمد (27281)، والبيهقي (9368)."},{"num":5040,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: ثُمَّ خَرَجَ مِن الْبَابِ إِلَى الصَّفَا فَلَمَّا دَنَا مِنْ الصَّفَا قَرَأَ: ﴿إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ﴾ [البقرة: 158] أَبْدَأُ بِمَا بَدَأَ الله بِهِ، فَبَدَأَ بِالصَّفَا فَرَقِيَ عَلَيْهِ ... حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ آخِرُ طَوَافِهِ عَلَى المَرْوَة...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره في الحديث الطّويل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن السعي سبعة أشواط يبدأ بالصفا وينتهي بالمروة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The sa‘y is seven circuits, beginning at al-Safa and ending at al-Marwah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":57,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: … Then he went out through the door to al-Safa, and when he came near al-Safa he recited: “Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,” and said: “I begin with what Allah began with.” So he began with al-Safa and climbed it … until when his final circuit ended at al-Marwah, he said: “If I had known beforehand what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animals, and I would have made it an ‘Umrah. So whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it an ‘Umrah.” … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5041,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَدِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَكَّةَ، فَطَافَ وَسَعَى بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ، وَلَمْ يَقْرَبِ الْكَعْبَةَ بَعْدَ طَوَافِهِ بِهَا حَتَّى رَجَعَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1625) عن محمد بن أبي بكر، حدّثنا فضيل، حدّثنا موسى بن عقبة، أخبرني كريب، عن عبدالله بن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بقي النبي في منزله بعد الطواف والسعي ولم يرجع إلى الكعبة إلا لطواف الإفاضة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1625).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ remained at his lodging after tawaf and sa‘y and did not return to the Ka‘bah except for Tawaf al-Ifadah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":58,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ came to Mecca, performed tawaf and sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and did not approach the Ka‘bah again after that tawaf until he returned from ‘Arafah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[9302],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1625)."},{"num":5042,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّمَا جُعِلَ رَمْىُ الْجِمَارِ وَالسَّعْىُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ لإِقَامَةِ ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1888)، والترمذي (902) كلاهما من حديث عيسى بن يونس، عن عبيدالله بن أبي زياد، عن القاسم بن محمد، عن عائشة، فذكرته. قال الترمذيّ: حديث حسن صحيح.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما شُرِعَ رمي الجمار والسعي إلا لإقامة ذكر الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1888) and al-Tirmidhi (902), who said: “A Hasan Sahih hadith.”","chapter_en":"The stoning of the pillars and the sa‘y were only prescribed for the establishment of the remembrance of Allah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":59,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Aishah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The stoning of the pillars and the sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah were only prescribed for the establishment of the remembrance of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1888)، والترمذي (902) وقال: (( حديث حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5043,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عباس، قال: ... وَجَعَلَتْ أُمُّ إِسْمَاعِيلَ تُرْضِعُ إِسْمَاعِيلَ وَتَشْرَبُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ المَاءِ، حَتَّى إِذَا نَفِدَ مَا فِي السِّقَاءِ عَطِشَتْ وَعَطِشَ ابْنُهَا وَجَعَلَتْ تَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِ يَتَلَوَّى - أَوْ قَالَ يَتَلَبَّطُ - فَانْطَلَقَتْ كَرَاهِيَةَ أَنْ تَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهِ فَوَجَدَت الصَّفَا أَقْرَبَ جَبَلٍ فِي الأَرْضِ يَلِيهَا فَقَامَتْ عَلَيْهِ ثُمَّ اسْتَقْبَلَت الْوَادِيَ تَنْظُرُ هَلْ تَرَى أَحَدًا؟ فَلَمْ تَرَ أَحَدًا فَهَبَطَتْ مِنْ الصَّفَا حَتَّى إِذَا بَلَغَت الْوَادِيَ رَفَعَتْ طَرَفَ دِرْعِهَا، ثُمَّ سَعَتْ سَعْيَ الإِنْسَانِ المَجْهُودِ حَتَّى جَاوَزَتْ الْوَادِيَ ثُمَّ أَتَت المَرْوَةَ فَقَامَتْ عَلَيْهَا وَنَظَرَتْ هَلْ تَرَى أَحَدًا؟ فَلَمْ تَرَ أَحَدًا، فَفَعَلَتْ ذَلِكَ سَبْعَ مَرَّاتٍ.","قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاس: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَذَلِكَ سَعْيُ النَّاسِ بَيْنَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في أحاديث الأنبياء (3364) عن عبدالله بن محمد (هو الجعفيّ المسنديّ)، حدّثنا عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن أيوب السّختيانيّ، وكثير بن كثير بن المطّلب بن أبي وداعة ـ يزيد أحدهما على الآخر ـ، عن سعيد بن جبير، قال ابن عباس، فذكر الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في بيان سبب السعي بين الصفا والمروة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (3364).","chapter_en":"Clarifying the reason for sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":60,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas said: “… The mother of Isma‘il began nursing Isma‘il and drinking from that water, until when what was in the waterskin was exhausted, she became thirsty and her son became thirsty. She began looking at him writhing — or he said: tossing — so she went off, disliking to keep looking at him. She found al-Safa to be the nearest hill on the land beside her, so she stood upon it, then faced the valley to see whether she could see anyone, but she saw no one. Then she came down from al-Safa until when she reached the valley, she lifted the edge of her garment and ran with the running of an exhausted person until she crossed the valley. Then she came to al-Marwah and stood upon it and looked whether she could see anyone, but she saw no one. She did that seven times.”","Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is the sa‘y of the people between them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3364)."},{"num":5044,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جَابِرَ بْنَ عبدالله قال: طَافَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ بِالْبَيْتِ وَبِالصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ؛ لِيَرَاهُ النَّاسُ وَلِيُشْرِفَ وَلِيَسْأَلُوهُ فَإِنَّ النَّاسَ غَشُوهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1273: 255) من طرق عن ابن جريج، قال: أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في جواز السعي بين الصفا والمروة راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1273/255).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of performing sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah riding or walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":61,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: The Prophet ﷺ performed tawaf in the Farewell Pilgrimage on his mount around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, so that the people could see him, and so that he could be elevated above them, and so that they could ask him, for the people had crowded around him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1273: 255)."},{"num":5045,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا نَزَلَ مِن الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ مَشَى، حَتَّى إِذَا انْصَبَّتْ قَدَمَاهُ فِي بَطْنِ الْوَادِي سَعَى حَتَّى يَخْرُجَ مِنْهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الحج (131) عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره. وأصله في صحيح مسلم في صفة حجة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في جواز السعي بين الصفا والمروة راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (131). In a narration of al-Nasa’i (2974): “Then he descended walking until his feet sloped into the bottom of the watercourse.”","chapter_en":"The permissibility of performing sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah riding or walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":61,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from al-Safa toward al-Marwah, he would walk, and when his feet sloped down into the bottom of the valley he would move quickly until he came out of it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (131). وفي رواية للنسائي nasai(2974): (( ثم نزل ماشيا حتى تصوبت قدماه في بطن المسيل ))."},{"num":5046,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي الطفيل، قال: قلت لابن عباس: أَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ الطَّوَافِ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ رَاكِبًا، أَسُنَّةٌ هُوَ؟ فَإِنَّ قَوْمَكَ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّهُ سُنَّةٌ؟ قَالَ: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا! قَال: قُلْتُ: وَمَا قَوْلُكَ صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا؟ قَال: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَثُرَ عَلَيْهِ النَّاسُ يَقُولُونَ: هَذَا مُحَمَّدٌ، هَذَا مُحَمَّدٌ، حَتَّى خَرَجَ الْعَوَاتِقُ مِنْ الْبُيُوتِ، قَال: وَكَانَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لا يُضْرَبُ النَّاسُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا كَثُرَ عَلَيْهِ رَكِبَ، وَالمَشْيُ وَالسَّعْيُ أَفْضَلُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1264) عن أبي كامل فضيل بن حسين الجحدريّ، حدّثنا عبد الواحد بن زياد، حدّثنا الجريريّ، عن أبي الطفيل فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في جواز السعي بين الصفا والمروة راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1264).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of performing sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah riding or walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":61,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu al-Tufayl said: I said to Ibn ‘Abbas: Tell me about going between al-Safa and al-Marwah while riding — is that a Sunnah? For your people claim that it is a Sunnah. He said: They are right and they are wrong. I said: What do you mean by saying they are right and they are wrong? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had many people crowd around him, saying: This is Muhammad, this is Muhammad, until even the young women came out from the houses. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not one before whom people were struck aside. So when the crowd increased around him, he rode, while walking and moving quickly on foot is better."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “They are right and they are wrong,” was explained by al-Nawawi as meaning: they are right that he performed it while riding, and wrong in claiming that riding is better; rather, walking is better."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1264)."},{"num":5047,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي الطفيل، قال: قُلْتُ لابنِ عَبَّاس: أُرَانِي قَدْ رَأَيْتُ.","رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَال: فَصِفْهُ لِي. قَال: قُلْتُ: رَأَيْتُهُ عِنْدَ المَرْوَةِ عَلَى نَاقَةٍ وَقَدْ كَثُرَ النَّاسُ عَلَيْهِ. قَال: فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: ذَاكَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا لا يُدَعُّونَ عَنْهُ وَلا يُكْهَرُونَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1265) عن محمد بن رافع، حدّثنا يحيى بن آدم، حدّثنا زهير بن عبدالملك بن سعيد بن الأبجر، عن أبي الطفيل، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في جواز السعي بين الصفا والمروة راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1265).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of performing sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah riding or walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":61,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu al-Tufayl said: I said to Ibn ‘Abbas: I think I may have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Then describe him to me. He said: I said: I saw him at al-Marwah on a she-camel, while many people had gathered around him. Ibn ‘Abbas then said: “That was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They did not drive people away from him, nor were they harsh with them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["He first walked, then when the crowd around him increased, he rode, as is found in the narrations of Muslim.","What is understood from the hadiths of this chapter is that the Prophet ﷺ combined both walking and riding in his sa‘y during the Farewell Pilgrimage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1265)."},{"num":5048,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، قال: وَأَقْبَلَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى أَقْبَلَ إِلَى الحَجَرِ فَاسْتَلَمَهُ، ثُمَّ طَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ، قَال: فَأَتَى عَلَى صَنَمٍ إِلَى جَنْبِ الْبَيْتِ كَانُوا يَعْبُدُونَهُ. قَال: وَفِي يَدِ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَوْسٌ وَهُوَ آخِذٌ بِسِيَةِ الْقَوْسِ فَلَمَّا أَتَى عَلَى الصَّنَمِ جَعَلَ يَطْعُنُهُ فِي عَيْنِهِ وَيَقُولُ: جَاءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُ، فَلَمَّا فَرَغَ مِنْ طَوَافِهِ أَتَى الصَّفَا فَعَلا عَلَيْهِ حَتَّى نَظَرَ إِلَى الْبَيْتِ وَرَفَعَ يَدَيْهِ فَجَعَلَ يَحْمَدُ الله وَيَدْعُو بِمَا شَاءَ أَنْ يَدْعُوَ... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فتح مكة (1780) عن شيبان بن فرّوخ، حدّثنا سليمان بن المغيرة، حدّثنا ثابت البنانيّ، عن عبدالله بن رباح، عن أبي هريرة في حديث طويل في قصّة فتح مكة، وسيأتي بكامله في موضعه.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الصعود على الصفا والمروة واستقبال الكعبة والتكبير والتهليل والدعاء عليهما مع رفع اليدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1780).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of ascending al-Safa and al-Marwah, facing the Ka‘bah, saying takbir and tahlil, and making supplication upon them while raising the hands","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":62,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: … The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he came to the Black Stone and touched it, then he circumambulated the House. He then came upon an idol beside the House which they used to worship. In the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a bow, and he was holding it by its curved end. When he came to the idol, he began striking at its eye and saying: “Truth has come, and falsehood has vanished.” Then when he finished his tawaf, he went to al-Safa and climbed it until he looked toward the House, and he raised his hands and began praising Allah and supplicating … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1780)."},{"num":5049,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: فَلَمَّا دَنَا مِنْ الصَّفَا قَرَأَ: ﴿إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ﴾ [البقرة: 158]، أَبْدَأُ بِمَا بَدَأَ الله بِهِ، فَبَدَأَ بِالصَّفَا فَرَقِيَ عَلَيْهِ حَتَّى رَأَى الْبَيْتَ، فَاسْتَقْبَلَ الْقِبْلَةَ، فَوَحَّدَ الله وَكَبَّرَهُ، وَقَال: لا إِلَهَ إِلا الله وَحْدَهُ لا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ المُلْكُ وَلَهُ الحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، لا إِلَهَ إِلا الله وَحْدَهُ، أَنْجَزَ وَعْدَهُ، وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَهُ، وَهَزَمَ الْأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهُ. ثُمَّ دَعَا بَيْنَ ذَلِكَ قَالَ مِثْلَ هَذَا ثَلاثَ مَرَّاتٍ، ثُمَّ نَزَلَ إِلَى المَرْوَةِ حَتَّى إِذَا انْصَبَّتْ قَدَمَاهُ فِي بَطْنِ الْوَادِي سَعَى، حَتَّى إِذَا صَعِدَتَا مَشَى، حَتَّى أَتَى المَرْوَةَ فَفَعَلَ عَلَى المَرْوَةِ كَمَا فَعَلَ عَلَى الصَّفَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر الحديث بطوله في حجّة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الصعود على الصفا والمروة واستقبال الكعبة والتكبير والتهليل والدعاء عليهما مع رفع اليدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of ascending al-Safa and al-Marwah, facing the Ka‘bah, saying takbir and tahlil, and making supplication upon them while raising the hands","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":62,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: When he came near al-Safa, he recited: “Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,” and said: “I begin with what Allah began with.” So he began with al-Safa and climbed it until he could see the House. He then faced the qiblah, declared Allah’s oneness, magnified Him, and said: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs all dominion and all praise, and He has power over all things. There is no god but Allah alone. He fulfilled His promise, granted victory to His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.” Then he supplicated between that. He said this same statement three times. Then he descended toward al-Marwah, and when his feet went down into the bottom of the valley, he moved quickly; when they rose, he walked, until he came to al-Marwah and did upon al-Marwah as he had done upon al-Safa."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11129],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5050,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر، قال: تَمَتَّعَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الحَجِّ وَأَهْدَى فَسَاقَ مَعَهُ الهَدْيَ مِنْ ذِي الحُلَيْفَةِ وَبَدَأَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَهَلَّ بِالْعُمْرَةِ، ثُمَّ أَهَـلَّ بِالحَجِّ فَتَمَتَّعَ النّـَاسُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الحَجِّ فَكَانَ مِن النَّاسِ مَنْ أَهْدَى فَسَاقَ الهَدْيَ، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ لَمْ يُهْدِ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَكَّةَ قَالَ لِلنَّاسِ: مَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ أَهْدَى فَإِنَّهُ لا يَحِلُّ لِشَيْءٍ حَرُمَ مِنْهُ حَتَّى يَقْضِيَ حَجَّهُ، وَمَنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ أَهْدَى فَلْيَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ وَبِالصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ وَلْيُقَصِّرْ وَلْيَحْلِلْ، ثم ليُهلَّ بالحج، فمن لم يجـدْ هديا فليصمْ ثلاثـــة أيام في الحج، وسبعــــة إذا رجع إلى أهله."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1691)- واللفظ له-، ومسلم في الحج (1227) كلاهما من طريق الليث بن سعد، حدثني عُقيل بن خالد، عن ابن شهاب، عن سالم بن عبدالله، أنّ عبدالله بن عمر، فذكره بتمامه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن المتمتع يتحلل من عمرته بتقصير شعره وعليه هدي التمتع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1691) — and this is his wording — and Muslim (1227).","chapter_en":"The one performing tamattu‘ exits from his ‘Umrah by shortening his hair, and the sacrificial offering of tamattu‘ is due upon him","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":63,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tamattu‘ in the Farewell Pilgrimage by doing ‘Umrah before Hajj, and he brought a sacrificial offering and drove it with him from Dhu al-Hulayfah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began by entering ihram for ‘Umrah, then entered ihram for Hajj. The people also performed tamattu‘ with the Prophet ﷺ from ‘Umrah into Hajj. Among the people were those who had sacrificial animals and drove them along, and among them were those who did not. When the Prophet ﷺ came to Mecca, he said to the people: “Whoever among you has brought a sacrificial animal, then nothing that he entered into prohibition becomes lawful for him until he completes his Hajj. And whoever among you has not brought a sacrificial animal, let him circumambulate the House and go between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then shorten his hair and exit ihram, then enter ihram for Hajj. And whoever cannot find a sacrificial animal must fast three days during Hajj and seven when he returns to his family.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “let him shorten,” means from his hair. They were instructed to shorten because they were close to entering ihram for Hajj again, so that they would still be able to shave their heads during Hajj, and shaving is better than shortening."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1691) - واللفظ له -، ومسلم (1227)."},{"num":5051,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، أَنَّهُ حَجَّ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ سَاقَ الْبُدْنَ مَعَهُ وَقَدْ أَهَلُّوا بِالحَجِّ مُفْرَدًا، فَقَالَ لهُم: أَحِلُّوا مِنْ إِحْرَامِكُمْ بِطَوَافِ الْبَيْتِ وَبَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ، وَقَصِّرُوا، ثُمَّ أَقِيمُوا حَلالا حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ فَأَهِلُّوا بِالحَجِّ وَاجْعَلُوا الَّتِي قَدِمْتُمْ بِهَا مُتْعَةً، فقالوا: كيف نجعلها متعة وقد سمينا الحج؟ فقال: افعلوا ما أمرتكم، فلولا أني سقت الهدي لفعلت مثل الذي أمرتكم، ولكن لا يحل مني حرام حتى يبلغ الهدي محله ففعلوا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1568) ومسلم في الحج (1216/143) كلاهما من حديث أبي نعيم (هو الفضل ابن دكين)، حدّثنا أبو شهاب، قال: قدمت مكة بعمرة فدخلنا قبل التروية بثلاثة أيام، فقال لي أناسٌ من أهل مكة: تصير حجّتُك مكيّة!، فدخلتُ على عطاء أستفتيه، فقال: حدثني جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره بتمامه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن المتمتع يتحلل من عمرته بتقصير شعره وعليه هدي التمتع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1568) and Muslim (1216/143). In another narration in al-Bukhari (1651): “The Prophet ﷺ ordered his companions to make it an ‘Umrah, to perform tawaf, then shorten their hair and exit ihram, except those who had a sacrificial animal with them…”","chapter_en":"The one performing tamattu‘ exits from his ‘Umrah by shortening his hair, and the sacrificial offering of tamattu‘ is due upon him","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":63,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah reported that he performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ on the day he had brought the sacrificial camels with him, while they had entered ihram for Hajj alone. So he said to them: “Exit from your ihram by circumambulating the House and going between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and shorten your hair, then remain in a lawful state until, when the Day of Tarwiyah comes, enter ihram for Hajj, and make what you first came with into tamattu‘.” They said: How can we make it tamattu‘ when we have named Hajj? He said: “Do what I have commanded you. If I had not brought the sacrificial animal, I would have done as I commanded you. But nothing prohibited in ihram becomes lawful for me until the sacrificial animal reaches its place.” So they did that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1568)، ومسلم (1216/143). وفي رواية أخرى عند البخاري (1651) بلفظ: (( فأمر النبي ﷺ أصحابه أن يجعلوها عمرة ويطوفوا، ثم يقصروا ويحلوا إلا من كان معه الهدي… ))."},{"num":5052,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: ...حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ آخِرُ طَوَافِهِ عَلَى المَرْوَةِ فَقَال: لَوْ أَنِّي اسْتَقْبَلْتُ مِنْ أَمْرِي مَا اسْتَدْبَرْتُ لَمْ أَسُق الهَدْيَ وَجَعَلْتُهَا عُمْرَةً، فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ لَيْسَ مَعَهُ هَدْيٌ فَلْيَحِلَّ وَلْيَجْعَلْهَا عُمْرَةً... قَالَ فَحَلَّ النَّاسُ كُلُّهُمْ وَقَصَّرُوا إِلا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَنْ كَانَ مَعَهُ هَدْيٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طرق عن حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن المتمتع يتحلل من عمرته بتقصير شعره وعليه هدي التمتع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The one performing tamattu‘ exits from his ‘Umrah by shortening his hair, and the sacrificial offering of tamattu‘ is due upon him","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":63,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: When his final circuit ended at al-Marwah, he said: “If I had known beforehand what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal, and I would have made it an ‘Umrah. So whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it an ‘Umrah.” … He said: So all the people exited ihram and shortened their hair except the Prophet ﷺ and those who had a sacrificial animal with them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5053,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمرو بن دينار، قال: سَأَلْنَا ابْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عن رَجُلٍ قدم بعمرة فطَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ وَلَمْ يَطُفْ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ أَيَأْتِي امْرَأَتَهُ فَقَال:قَدِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَطَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ سَبْعًا وَصَلَّى خَلْفَ المَقَامِ رَكْعَتَيْنِ ثُمَّ خَرَجَ إِلَى الصَّفَا وَقَدْ قَالَ الله تَعَالَى: ﴿لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 21]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ أيضاً في الحج (1623، 1644)، ومسلم في الحج (1234: 189) من طريق سفيان ابن عيينة، عن عمرو بن دينار، به، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن التحلل من العمرة لا يكون إلا بعد السعي بين الصفا والمروة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1644, 1623) and Muslim (1234/189). Al-Bukhari added (1624, 1645): We also asked Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he said: “He must not go near her until he has gone between al-Safa and al-Marwah.”","chapter_en":"Exiting ihram from ‘Umrah does not occur until after sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":64,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Amr ibn Dinar said: We asked Ibn ‘Umar about a man who arrived for ‘Umrah, circumambulated the House, but did not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah — may he go to his wife? He said: The Prophet ﷺ arrived and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak‘ahs behind the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa. Allah Most High has said: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1644، 1623)، ومسلم (1234: 189). وزاد البخاري (1624، 1645): وسألنا جابر بن عبد الله رضي الله عنهما، فقال: (( لا يقربنها حتى يطوف بين الصفا والمروة ))."},{"num":5054,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة، قالت: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِخَمْسٍ بَقِينَ مِنْ ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ لا نُرَى إِلا الحَجَّ، فَلَمَّا دَنَوْنَا مِنْ مَكَّةَ أَمَرَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ مَعَهُ هَدْيٌ إِذَا طَافَ وَسَعَى بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ أَنْ يَحِلَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1709)، ومسلم في الحج (1211: 125) كلاهما من طريق يحيى بن سعيد (هو الأنصاريّ)، عن عمرة بنت عبدالرحمن، قال: سمعت عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن التحلل من العمرة لا يكون إلا بعد السعي بين الصفا والمروة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1709) and Muslim (1211/125).","chapter_en":"Exiting ihram from ‘Umrah does not occur until after sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":64,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Aishah said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with five nights remaining in Dhu al-Qa‘dah, seeing nothing but Hajj. When we drew near to Mecca, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered those who did not have a sacrificial animal with them to exit ihram once they had performed tawaf and sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1709)، ومسلم (1211: 125)."},{"num":5055,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، أَنَّهُ سُئِلَ عَنْ مُتْعَةِ الحَجِّ؟ فَقَال: أَهَلَّ المُهَاجِرُونَ وَالأَنْصَارُ وَأَزْوَاجُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ، وَأَهْلَلْنَا، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا مَكَّةَ، قَالَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اجْعَلُوا إِهْلالَكُمْ بِالحَجِّ عُمْرَةً إِلا مَنْ قَلَّدَ الهَدْيَ. فَطُفْنَا بِالْبَيْتِ وَبِالصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ وَأَتَيْنَا النِّسَاءَ وَلَبِسْنَا الثِّيَاب... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: علقه البخاريّ في الحج (1572) عن أبي كامل فضيل بن حسين البصريّ، حدّثنا أبو معشر (هو يوسف بن يزيد البرّاء)، حدّثنا عثمان ابن غياث، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس، فذكر الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن التحلل من العمرة لا يكون إلا بعد السعي بين الصفا والمروة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Al-Bukhari mentioned it in suspended form in the Book of Hajj (1572). Al-Hafiz said in al-Fath (3/434): “Al-Isma‘ili connected its chain.”","chapter_en":"Exiting ihram from ‘Umrah does not occur until after sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":64,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas was asked about tamattu‘ in Hajj, so he said: The Muhajirun, the Ansar, and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we also entered ihram. When we came to Mecca, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Make your ihram for Hajj into an ‘Umrah, except for the one who has garlanded the sacrificial animal.” So we circumambulated the House, went between al-Safa and al-Marwah, approached our wives, and wore clothes … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: علقه البخاري (1572). قال الحافظ في “الفتح” (3/434): (( وصله الإسماعيلي ))."},{"num":5056,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة أنها قالت: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ فَأَهْلَلْنَا بِعُمْرَةٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ كَانَ مَعَهُ هَدْيٌ فَلْيُهِلَّ بِالحَجِّ مَعَ الْعُمْرَةِ، ثُمَّ لا يَحِلَّ حَتَّى يَحِلَّ مِنْهُمَا جَمِيعًا. قالت: فَقَدِمْتُ مَكَّةَ وَأَنَا حَائِضٌ وَلَمْ أَطُفْ بِالْبَيْتِ وَلا بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ فَشَكَوْتُ ذَلِكَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَال: انْقُضِي رَأْسَكِ وَامْتَشِطِي وَأَهِلِّي بِالحَجِّ وَدَعِي الْعُمْرَةَ. قالت: فَفَعَلْتُ فَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا الحَجَّ أَرْسَلَنِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَ عبدالرحمن بْنِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ إِلَى التَّنْعِيمِ فَاعْتَمَرْتُ فَقَال: هَذِهِ مَكَانَ عُمْرَتِكِ. قَالَتْ: فَطَافَ الَّذِينَ أَهَلُّوا بِالْعُمْرَةِ بِالْبَيْتِ وَبَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ ثُمَّ حَلُّوا، ثُمَّ طَافُوا طَوَافًا آخَرَ بَعْدَ أَنْ رَجَعُوا مِنْ مِنًى لحجّهم. وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ جَمَعُوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ فَإِنَّمَا طَافُوا طَوَافًا وَاحِدًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1556) عن عبدالله بن يوسف، ومسلم في الحج (1211: 111) عن يحيى بن يحيى التميميّ، كلاهما عن مالك، عن ابن شهاب، عن عروة، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب هل على القارن سعي واحد أو سعيان؟","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1556) and Muslim (1211/111).","chapter_en":"Is one saʿy sufficient for the qarin, or are two required?","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":65,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Aishah said: We went out with the Prophet ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage and entered ihram for ‘Umrah. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him should enter ihram for Hajj along with ‘Umrah, then he should not exit ihram until he exits from both of them together.” She said: I came to Mecca while menstruating, so I did not circumambulate the House nor go between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I complained of that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Undo your hair, comb it, enter ihram for Hajj, and leave the ‘Umrah.” She said: So I did that. When we completed the Hajj, the Prophet ﷺ sent me with ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr to al-Tan‘im, and I performed ‘Umrah. He then said: “This is in place of your ‘Umrah.” She said: Those who had entered ihram for ‘Umrah circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then exited ihram. Then they performed another tawaf after returning from Mina for their Hajj. But those who combined Hajj and ‘Umrah performed only one tawaf."]},"buhuth":{"en":["I say: What is intended by “one tawaf” here is the sa‘y that occurred before Hajj, as was explained by al-Bayhaqi and others, as in the hadith of Jabir."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1556)، ومسلم (1211: 111)."},{"num":5057,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة، أَنَّهَا حَاضَتْ بِسَرِفَ فَتَطَهَّرَتْ بِعَرَفَةَ فَقَالَ لَهَا رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يُجْزِئُ عَنْكِ طَوَافُكِ بِالصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ عَنْ حَجِّكِ وَعُمْرَتِك."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1211: 133) عن حسن بن علي الحلوانيّ، حدّثنا زيد بن الحباب، حدّثني إبراهيم بن نافع، حدثني عبدالله بن أبي نجيح، عن مجاهد، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب هل على القارن سعي واحد أو سعيان؟","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1211/133). In another narration with him, the Prophet ﷺ said to her: “This is something Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Adam, so bathe and then enter ihram for Hajj.” So she did that, and she stood at the standing places until, when she became pure, she circumambulated the Ka‘bah and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said to her: “You have now exited from both your Hajj and your ‘Umrah together.” And in another narration with him: “Your tawaf is sufficient for your Hajj and your ‘Umrah.”","chapter_en":"Is one saʿy sufficient for the qarin, or are two required?","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":65,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Aishah menstruated at Sarif, then became pure at ‘Arafah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah will suffice for both your Hajj and your ‘Umrah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1211: 133). وفي رواية عنده: قال لها النبي ﷺ: (( إن هذا أمر كتبه الله على بنات آدم، فاغتسلي ثم أهلي بالحج )). ففعلت، ووقفت المواقف حتى إذا طهرت طافت بالكعبة والصفا والمروة، ثم قال لها: (( قد حللت من حجك وعمرتك جميعا )). وفي رواية عنده: (( يسعك طوافك لحجك وعمرتك ))."},{"num":5058,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر، أنه قال حِينَ خَرَجَ إِلَى مَكَّةَ مُعْتَمِرًا فِي الْفِتْنَةِ: إِنْ صُدِدْتُ عَنْ الْبَيْتِ صَنَعْنَا كَمَا صَنَعْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَهَلَّ بِعُمْرَةٍ مِنْ أَجْلِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أهلّ بِعُمْرَةٍ عَامَ الحُدَيْبِيَةِ، ثُمَّ إِنَّ عبدالله نَظَرَ فِي أَمْرِهِ فَقَالَ: مَا أَمْرُهُمَا إِلا وَاحِدٌ، ثُمَّ الْتَفَتَ إِلَى أَصْحَابِهِ، فَقَالَ: مَا أَمْرُهُمَا إِلا وَاحِدٌ، أُشْهِدُكُمْ أَنِّي قَدْ أَوْجَبْتُ الحَجَّ مَعَ الْعُمْرَةِ، ثُمَّ نَفَذَ حَتَّى جَاءَ الْبَيْتَ، فَطَافَ طَوَافًا وَاحِدًا، وَرَأَى ذَلِكَ مُجْزِيًا عَنْهُ وَأَهْدَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (99) عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (99), al-Bukhari (1813), and Muslim (1230:180). In the wording of Muslim: “He went on until he came to the House, then he circumambulated it seven times, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven times, without adding anything to that, and he considered that sufficient for himself…”","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said, when he set out for Mecca to perform the lesser pilgrimage during the time of turmoil: “If I am prevented from reaching the House, we will do as we did with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So he entered ihram for a lesser pilgrimage because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had entered ihram for a lesser pilgrimage in the year of al-Hudaybiyah. Then ‘Abd Allah reflected on the matter and said: “The ruling of both is only one.” Then he turned to his companions and said: “The ruling of both is only one. Bear witness that I have now made pilgrimage obligatory upon myself together with the lesser pilgrimage.” Then he continued until he came to the House and made one circumambulation, and he considered that sufficient for himself, and he offered a sacrificial animal."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (99) والبخاري (1813)، ومسلم (1230 : 180). وفي لفظ مسلم: (( فخرج حتى إذا جاء البيت طاف به سبعا، وبين الصفا والمروة سبعا لم يزد عليه، ورأى أنه مجزئ عنه… ))."},{"num":5059,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن نافع: أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ أَرَادَ الحَجَّ عَامَ نَزَلَ الحَجَّاجُ بِابْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ فَقِيلَ لَهُ إِنَّ النَّاسَ كَائِنٌ بَيْنَهُمْ قِتَالٌ وَإِنَّا نَخَافُ أَنْ يَصُدُّوكَ فَقَالَ: ﴿لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ﴾ [الأحزاب: 21] أَصْنَعُ كَمَا صَنَعَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِنِّي أُشْهِدُكُمْ أَنِّي قَدْ أَوْجَبْتُ عُمْرَةً ثُمَّ خَرَجَ حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ بِظَاهِرِ الْبَيْدَاءِ قَالَ: مَا شَأْنُ الحَجِّ وَالْعُمْرَةِ إِلا وَاحِدٌ، اشْهَدُوا -قَالَ ابْنُ رُمْحٍ: أُشْهِدُكُمْ- أَنِّي قَدْ أَوْجَبْتُ حَجًّا مَعَ عُمْرَتِي. وَأَهْدَى هَدْيًا اشْتَرَاهُ بِقُدَيْدٍ، ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَ يُهِلُّ بِهِمَا جَمِيعًا حَتَّى قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ فَطَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ وَبِالصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ وَلَمْ يَزِدْ عَلَى ذَلِكَ، وَلَمْ يَنْحَرْ، وَلَمْ يَحْلِقْ، وَلَمْ يُقَصِّرْ، وَلَمْ يَحْلِلْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ حَرُمَ مِنْهُ حَتَّى كَانَ يَوْمُ النَّحْرِ، فَنَحَرَ وَحَلَقَ وَرَأَى أَنْ قَدْ قَضَى طَوَافَ الحَجِّ وَالْعُمْرَةِ بِطَوَافِهِ الأَوَّلِ.","وَقَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: كَذَلِكَ فَعَلَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1640)، ومسلم في الحج (1230: 182) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدّثنا الليث، عن نافع، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1640) and Muslim (1230:182), and this is Muslim’s wording. Ibn ‘Umar’s statement, “This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did,” shows that what Ibn ‘Umar did is attributed back to the Prophet ﷺ, namely that the one combining both rites only has one sa‘y.","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Nafi‘ reported that Ibn ‘Umar intended to perform pilgrimage in the year when al-Hajjaj besieged Ibn al-Zubayr. It was said to him: “There will be fighting among the people, and we fear they may prevent you.” He replied: “Indeed, you have in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ an excellent example.” He then said: “I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did. I call you to witness that I have made a lesser pilgrimage obligatory upon myself.” Then he set out, and when he reached the outer part of al-Bayda’, he said: “The matter of pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage is only one. Bear witness” — Ibn Rumh said: “I call you to witness” — “that I have made pilgrimage obligatory upon myself together with my lesser pilgrimage.” He offered a sacrificial animal that he had bought at Qudayd, then proceeded entering into both together until he came to Mecca. He circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and did not add anything beyond that. He did not slaughter, shave, trim, or exit from any of the restrictions of ihram until the Day of Sacrifice, when he slaughtered and shaved. He held that he had fulfilled the circumambulation of both pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage with his first circumambulation. And Ibn ‘Umar said: “This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1640)، ومسلم (1230 : 182) واللفظ له. وقول ابن عمر: (( كذلك فعل رسول الله ﷺ )) دليل على رفع ما فعله ابن عمر إلى النبي ﷺ بأن ليس على القارن إلا سعي واحد."},{"num":5060,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمر، قال: قال رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ أَحْرَمَ بِالحَجِّ وَالْعُمْرَةِ أَجْزَأَهُ طَوَافٌ وَاحِدٌ وَسَعْيٌ وَاحِدٌ عَنْهُمَا حَتَّى يَحِلَّ مِنْهُمَا جَمِيعًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (948)، وابن ماجه (2975) كلاهما من حديث عبد العزيز بن محمد (وهو الدراورديّ) عن عبيدالله، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (948), Ibn Majah (2975), and Ahmad (5350). Al-Tirmidhi said: “Hasan Sahih Gharib.”","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever enters ihram for pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage together, one circumambulation and one sa‘y are sufficient for both until he exits from them together.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (948)، وابن ماجه (2975)، وأحمد (5350)، قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح غريب ))."},{"num":5061,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: لَمْ يَطُفِ النبيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَلَا أَصْحَابُهُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ إلاّ طَوَافًا وَاحِدًا، طوافَهُ الْأَوَّلَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1279، 1215) من طريق ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1279) and (1215). His statement, “their first going,” means their first sa‘y, which took place after the arrival circumambulation.","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions did not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah except once, their first going."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1279)، وmuslim(1215). قوله: (( طوافه الأول )) يعني سعيه الأول الذي كان عقب طواف القدوم."},{"num":5062,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ طَافَ طَوَافًا وَاحِدًا لِحَجَّتِهِ وَعُمْرَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الدارقطني (2619) عن عبدالله بن محمد بن عبد العزيز البغويّ، حدّثنا داود بن عمرو المسَيَّبي، حدّثنا منصور بن أبي الأسود، عن عبد الملك، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Daraqutni (2619).","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made one circumambulation for his pilgrimage and his lesser pilgrimage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الدارقطني (2619)."},{"num":5063,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن محمد بن عبدالرحمن، أَنَّ رَجُلا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْعِرَاقِ قَالَ لَهُ: سَلْ لِي عُرْوَةَ بْنَ الزُّبَيْرِ عَنْ رَجُلٍ يُهِلُّ بِالحَجِّ فَإِذَا طَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ أَيَحِلُّ أَمْ لا؟ فَإِنْ قَالَ لَكَ: لا يَحِلُّ، فَقُلْ لَهُ إِنَّ رَجُلا يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ.","قَال: فَسَأَلْتُهُ، فَقَالَ: لا يَحِلُّ مَنْ أَهَلَّ بِالحَجِّ إِلا بِالحَجِّ. قُلْتُ: فَإِنَّ رَجُلا كَانَ يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ. قَالَ: بِئْسَ مَا قَالَ!. فَتَصَدَّانِي الرَّجُلُ فَسَأَلَنِي فَحَدَّثْتُهُ، فَقَال: فَقُلْ لَهُ: فَإِنَّ رَجُلا كَانَ يُخْبِرُ أَنَّ رَسُـولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ، وَمَا شَأْنُ أَسْمَاءَ وَالزُّبَيْرِ قَدْ فَعَلا ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ: فَجِئْتُهُ فَذَكَرْتُ لَهُ ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقُلْتُ: لا أَدْرِي. قَال: فَمَا بَالُهُ لا يَأْتِينِي بِنَفْسِهِ يَسْأَلُنِي أَظُنُّهُ عِرَاقِيًّا؟! قُلْتُ: لا أَدْرِي! قَالَ: فَإِنَّهُ قَدْ كَذَبَ قَدْ حَجَّ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرَتْنِي عَائِشَةُ رَضِيَ الله عَنْهَا أَنَّ أَوَّلَ شَيْءٍ بَدَأَ بِهِ حِينَ قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ أَنَّهُ تَوَضَّأَ ثُمَّ طَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ، ثُمَّ حَجَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ شَيْءٍ بَدَأَ بِهِ الطَّوَافُ بِالْبَيْتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَكُنْ غَيْرُهُ، ثُمَّ عُمَرُ مِثْلُ ذَلِكَ، ثُمَّ حَجَّ عُثْمَانُ فَرَأَيْتُهُ أَوَّلُ شَيْءٍ بَدَأَ بِهِ الطَّوَافُ بِالْبَيْتِ، ثُمَّ لَمْ يَكُنْ غَيْرُهُ، ثُمَّ مُعَاوِيَةُ وَعبدالله بْنُ عُمَرَ، ثُمَّ حَجَجْتُ مَعَ أَبِي: الزُّبَيْرِ بْنِ الْعَوَّامِ فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ شَيْءٍ بَدَأَ بِهِ الطَّوَافُ بِالْبَيْتِ، ثُمَّ لَمْ يَكُنْ غَيْرُهُ، ثُمَّ رَأَيْتُ المُهَاجِرِينَ وَالأَنْصَارَ يَفْعَلُونَ ذَلِكَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَكُنْ غَيْرُهُ، ثُمَّ آخِرُ مَنْ رَأَيْتُ فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُضْهَا بِعُمْرَةٍ وَهَذَا ابْنُ عُمَرَ عِنْدَهُمْ أَفَلا يَسْأَلُونَهُ؟ وَلا أَحَدٌ مِمَّنْ مَضَى مَا كَانُوا يَبْدَؤونَ بِشَيْءٍ حِينَ يَضَعُونَ أَقْدَامَهُمْ أَوَّلَ مِنْ الطَّوَافِ بِالْبَيْتِ، ثُمَّ لا يَحِلُّونَ وَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ أُمِّي وَخَالَتِي حِينَ تَقْدَمَانِ لا تَبْدَآنِ بِشَيْءٍ أَوَّلَ مِنْ الْبَيْتِ تَطُوفَانِ بِهِ ثُمَّ لا تَحِلاّنِ، وَقَدْ أَخْبَرَتْنِي أُمِّي أَنَّهَا أَقْبَلَتْ هِيَ وَأُخْتُهَا وَالزُّبَيْرُ وَفُلانٌ وَفُلانٌ بِعُمْرَةٍ قَطُّ فَلَمَّا مَسَحُوا الرُّكْنَ حَلُّوا وَقَدْ كَذَبَ فِيمَا ذَكَرَ مِنْ ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1641)، ومسلم في الحج (1235) كلاهما من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث، عن محمد ابن عبدالرحمن بن نوفل القرشيّ، فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن والمفرد لا يتحللان بعد طوافهما الأوّل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1641) and Muslim (1235), and this is Muslim’s wording.","chapter_en":"The one combining pilgrimage and lesser pilgrimage, and the one performing pilgrimage alone, do not exit ihram after their first circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":67,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman reported that a man from Iraq said to him: “Ask ‘Urwah ibn al-Zubayr for me about a man who enters ihram for pilgrimage, then when he circumambulates the House, does he become lawful or not? If he says to you, ‘He does not become lawful,’ then tell him that a man says otherwise.” He said: So I asked him, and he said: “The one who enters ihram for pilgrimage does not become lawful except by completing pilgrimage.” I said: “But there is a man who says that.” He replied: “What a bad thing he said!” He said: Then that man came to me and asked me, so I informed him. He said: “Then tell him that a man used to report that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done that, and what about Asma’ and al-Zubayr, who also did that?” He said: So I came back to him and mentioned that to him. He said: “Who is this?” I said: “I do not know.” He said: “Why does he not come to me himself and ask me? I think he is Iraqi!” I said: “I do not know.” He said: “Then he has lied. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed pilgrimage, and ‘Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed me that the first thing he did when he came to Mecca was to perform ablution, then circumambulate the House. Then Abu Bakr performed pilgrimage, and the first thing he did was circumambulate the House, and there was nothing else after that. Then ‘Umar did the same. Then ‘Uthman performed pilgrimage, and I saw that the first thing he did was circumambulate the House, and there was nothing else after that. Then Mu‘awiyah and ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar. Then I performed pilgrimage with al-Zubayr ibn al-‘Awwam, and the first thing he did was circumambulate the House, and there was nothing else after that. Then I saw the Emigrants and the Helpers doing that, and there was nothing else after that. Then the last person I saw doing that was Ibn ‘Umar, yet he did not turn it into a lesser pilgrimage. And here is Ibn ‘Umar among them — will they not ask him? And no one from those before used to begin with anything when they set foot there before circumambulating the House, and then they would not exit ihram. And I saw my mother and my aunt when they arrived: they began with nothing before the House, circumambulating it, and then they would not exit ihram. My mother also informed me that she, her sister, al-Zubayr, and so-and-so and so-and-so came for a lesser pilgrimage only, and when they had touched the corner, they exited ihram. So he has lied in what he mentioned of that.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “then they would not exit ihram,” means whether their ihram was for pilgrimage alone or for combining both rites, contrary to those who said that whoever entered ihram for pilgrimage alone and then circumambulated became lawful, as is narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas. See al-Fath (3/497)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1641)، ومسلم (1235)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5064,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عطاء قال: كَانَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ يَقُولُ: لا يَطُوفُ بِالْبَيْتِ حَاجٌّ وَلا غَيْرُ حَاجٍّ إِلا حَلَّ.","قُلْتُ لِعَطَاءٍ: مِنْ أَيْنَ يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ: مِنْ قَوْلِ الله تَعَالَى: ﴿ثُمَّ مَحِلُّهَا إِلَى الْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ﴾ [سورة الحج: 33]. قَالَ: قُلْتُ: فَإِنَّ ذَلِكَ بَعْدَ المُعَرَّفِ. فَقَالَ: كَانَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ يَقُولُ: هُوَ بَعْدَ المُعَرَّفِ وَقَبْلَهُ، وَكَانَ يَأْخُذُ ذَلِكَ مِنْ أَمْرِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ أَمَرَهُمْ أَنْ يَحِلُّوا فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازي (4396)، ومسلم في الحج (1245) كلاهما من طريق ابن جريج، حدثني عطاء، فذكره. واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من قال: إن الحاج المفرد يتحلل إذا طاف بالبيت للقدوم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4396) and Muslim (1245), and this is Muslim’s wording.","chapter_en":"Those who said that the pilgrim performing pilgrimage alone exits ihram after the arrival circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":68,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ata’ said: Ibn ‘Abbas used to say: “No pilgrim or non-pilgrim circumambulates the House except that he becomes lawful.” I said to ‘Ata’: “From where did he say that?” He said: “From the statement of Allah Most High: ‘Then their place of sacrifice is at the Ancient House.’” I said: “But that is after standing at ‘Arafah.” He replied: Ibn ‘Abbas used to say: “It is after standing at ‘Arafah and before it.” And he took that from the command of the Prophet ﷺ when he ordered them to exit ihram during the Farewell Pilgrimage."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “after standing at ‘Arafah,” means after the standing at ‘Arafah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4396)، ومسلم (1245)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5065,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي حسّان الأعرج، قال: قَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي الهُجَيْمِ لابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ مَا هَذَه الْفُتْيَا الَّتِي قَدْ تَشَغَّفَتْ أَوْ تَشَغَّبَتْ بِالنَّاسِ أَنَّ مَنْ طَافَ بِالْبَيْتِ فَقَدْ حَلَّ!؟ فَقَال: سُنَّةُ نَبِيِّكُمْ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَإِنْ رَغِمْتُم."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1244) من طريق قتادة، قال: سمعت أبا حسّان الأعرج، به، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من قال: إن الحاج المفرد يتحلل إذا طاف بالبيت للقدوم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1244).","chapter_en":"Those who said that the pilgrim performing pilgrimage alone exits ihram after the arrival circumambulation","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":68,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hassan al-A‘raj said: A man from Banu al-Hujaym said to Ibn ‘Abbas: “What is this legal opinion that has taken hold of — or spread among — the people, that whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram?” He replied: “It is the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, even if you dislike it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “has taken hold,” means that it became attached to the hearts of the people and they became drawn to it. And his statement, “has spread among the people,” means that it confused the matter for them. It is also narrated as “has branched out,” meaning that it divided people into differing views and caused disagreement among them.","The scholars said: What Ibn ‘Abbas mentioned here was his legal view, and it is contrary to the view of the majority of the early and later scholars. I do not know whether he later retracted it or not. The pilgrim does not exit ihram merely by the arrival circumambulation; rather, he does not exit ihram until he stands at ‘Arafah, stones the pillars, shaves or trims, and performs the circumambulation of visitation. At that point, the two stages of release occur."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1244)."},{"num":5066,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حفصة أمِّ المؤمنين، أَنَّهَا قَالَتْ لِرَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا شَأْنُ النَّاسِ حَلُّوا وَلَمْ تَحْلِلْ أَنْتَ مِنْ عُمْرَتِكَ؟ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي لَبَّدْتُ رَأْسِي وَقَلَّدْتُ هَدْيِي فَلا أَحِلُّ حَتَّى أَنْحَرَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحجّ (180) عن نافع، عن عبدالله بن عمر، عن حفصة، فذكرته. ورواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1566)، ومسلم في الحج (1229: 176) كلاهما من طريق مالك، به، مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أنّ القارن الذي ساق الهدي لا يتحلل حتى ينحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (180), al-Bukhari (1566), and Muslim (1229:176).","chapter_en":"The one combining both rites who brought a sacrificial animal does not exit ihram until he slaughters","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":69,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hafsah, the Mother of the Believers, said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Why is it that the people exited ihram while you did not exit from your lesser pilgrimage?” He said: “I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: ( وَأَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلَّهِ فَإِنْ أُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ وَلَا تَحْلِقُوا رُءُوسَكُمْ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ الْهَدْيُ مَحِلَّهُ ) [سورة البقرة: ١٩٦].","قال ابن كثير في تفسيره (١/٥٣٨):  قوله: ( وَلَا تَحْلِقُوا رُءُوسَكُمْ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ الْهَدْيُ مَحِلَّهُ ) معطوف على قوله: ( وَأَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلَّهِ ) وليس معطوفًا على قوله: ( فَإِنْ أُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ ) كما زعمه ابن جرير ."],"en":["Allah Most High said: “Complete the pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage for Allah. But if you are prevented, then offer whatever sacrificial animal is easy to obtain. And do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal reaches its place of slaughter.” [Surat al-Baqarah: 196]","Ibn Kathir said in his commentary (1/538): “His statement, ‘And do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal reaches its place of slaughter,’ is connected to His statement, ‘Complete the pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage for Allah,’ and is not connected to His statement, ‘But if you are prevented, then offer whatever sacrificial animal is easy to obtain,’ as Ibn Jarir claimed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[4814,5205,5337],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (180) والبخاري (1566)، ومسلم (1229 : 176)."},{"num":5067,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبيد بن جريج أنه قال لعبدالله بن عمر: يَا أَبَا عبدالرحمن رَأَيْتُكَ تَصْنَعُ أَرْبَعًا لَمْ أَرَ أَحَدًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِكَ يَصْنَعُهَا! قَال: وَمَا هُنَّ يَا ابْنَ جُرَيْجٍ؟ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُكَ لا تَمَسُّ مِنْ الأَرْكَانِ إِلا الْيَمَانِيَّيْنِ، وَرَأَيْتُكَ تَلْبَسُ النِّعَالَ السِّبْتِيَّةَ، وَرَأَيْتُكَ تَصْبُغُ بِالصُّفْرَةِ، وَرَأَيْتُكَ إِذَا كُنْتَ بِمَكَّةَ أَهَلَّ النَّاسُ إِذَا رَأَوْا الهلالَ وَلَمْ تُهْلِلْ أَنْتَ حَتَّى يَكُونَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ. فَقَالَ عبدالله بْنُ عُمَرَ: أَمَّا الأَرْكَانُ فَإِنِّي لَمْ أَرَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمَسُّ إِلا الْيَمَانِيَّيْنِ، وَأَمَّا النِّعَالُ السِّبْتِيَّةُ فَإِنِّي رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَلْبَسُ النِّعَالَ الَّتِي لَيْسَ فِيهَا شَعَرٌ وَيَتَوَضَّأُ فِيهَا فَأَنَا أُحِبُّ أَنْ أَلْبَسَهَا، وَأَمَّا الصُّفْرَةُ فَإِنِّي رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَصْبُغُ بِهَا فَأَنَا أُحِبُّ أَنْ أَصْبُغَ بِهَا. وَأَمَّا الإِهْلالُ فَإِنِّي لَمْ أَرَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُهِلُّ حَتَّى تَنْبَعِثَ بِهِ رَاحِلَتُه."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (31) عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبريّ، عن عبيد بن جريج، به، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إهلال المكّي والمتمتع بالحج في يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (31), al-Bukhari (166), and Muslim (1187).","chapter_en":"The resident of Mecca and the one performing tamattu‘ enter ihram for pilgrimage on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":70,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ubayd ibn Jurayj said to ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar: “Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, I have seen you do four things that I have not seen any of your companions doing.” He said: “What are they, Ibn Jurayj?” He said: “I saw that you do not touch any of the corners except the two Yemeni corners. I saw that you wear leather sandals without hair. I saw that you dye with yellow coloring. And I saw that when you were in Mecca, the people entered ihram when they saw the new moon, while you did not enter ihram until the Day of Tarwiyah.” ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: “As for the corners, I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch any except the two Yemeni corners. As for the leather sandals without hair, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wear sandals that had no hair on them and make ablution in them, so I like to wear them. As for the yellow coloring, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye with it, so I like to dye with it. And as for entering ihram, I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enter ihram until his mount set out with him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “the Day of Tarwiyah,” means the eighth day of Dhu al-Hijjah. It was called the Day of Tarwiyah because they used to water their camels on that day and take enough water themselves, since those places at that time had neither wells nor springs. See al-Fath (3/507)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[4972,15336],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (31) والبخاري (166)، ومسلم (1187)."},{"num":5068,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، قال: صَلَّى رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ مَعَهُ بِالمَدِينَةِ الظُّهْرَ أَرْبَعًا وَالْعَصْرَ بِذِي الحُلَيْفَةِ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ بَاتَ بِهَا حَتَّى أَصْبَحَ، ثُمَّ رَكِبَ حَتَّى اسْتَوَتْ بِهِ عَلَى الْبَيْدَاءِ حَمِدَ الله وَسَبَّحَ وَكَبَّرَ، ثُمَّ أَهَلَّ بِحَجٍّ وَعُمْرَةٍ وَأَهَلَّ النَّاسُ بِهِمَا، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا أَمَرَ النَّاسَ فَحَلُّوا حَتَّى كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ أَهَلُّوا بِالحَجِّ. قَالَ: وَنَحَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَدَنَاتٍ بِيَدِهِ قِيَامًا، وَذَبَحَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالمَدِينَةِ كَبْشَيْنِ أَمْلَحَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1551)، ومسلم في الحج (690) كلاهما من طريق أيوب، عن أبي قلابة، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إهلال المكّي والمتمتع بالحج في يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1551) and Muslim (690). This is the wording of al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"The resident of Mecca and the one performing tamattu‘ enter ihram for pilgrimage on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":70,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer with us in Madinah as four units, and the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two units. Then he stayed there overnight until morning. Then he mounted, and when his mount rose with him upon al-Bayda’, he praised Allah, glorified Him, and magnified Him, then entered ihram for pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage, and the people entered ihram for both with him. When we arrived, he ordered the people, and they exited ihram until the Day of Tarwiyah, when they entered ihram for pilgrimage. He said: The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered sacrificial camels with his own hand while they were standing, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered two white rams marked with black in Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1551)، ومسلم (690). واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":5069,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: ... فَقَالَ لهُمْ (يعني النبيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ): أَحِلُّوا مِنْ إِحْرَامِكُمْ بِطَوَافِ الْبَيْتِ وَبَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالمَرْوَةِ وَقَصِّرُوا ثُمَّ أَقِيمُوا حَلالا حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ فَأَهِلُّوا بِالحَجِّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1568) ومسلم في الحج (1216) كلاهما من حديث أبي نعيم، حدّثنا أبو شهاب، قال: قدمت متمتِّعا مَكَّةَ بِعمرة فدخلنا قبل التَّروية بثلاثة أيَّام فقال لي أناس من أهل مكَّة تصير الآن حجَّتُك مكِّيّة فدخلت على عطاء أستفتيه فقال حدّثني جابر بن عبدالله رضي اللَّه عنهما أنّه حجّ مع النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم... الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إهلال المكّي والمتمتع بالحج في يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1568) and Muslim (1216).","chapter_en":"The resident of Mecca and the one performing tamattu‘ enter ihram for pilgrimage on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":70,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: … Then he said to them — meaning the Prophet ﷺ —: “Exit from your ihram by circumambulating the House and going between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and shorten your hair, then remain in a lawful state until, when the Day of Tarwiyah comes, enter ihram for pilgrimage.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1568)، ومسلم (1216)."},{"num":5070,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: ...فلما كان يوم التروية توجّهوا إلى منى، فأهلُّوا بالحجّ....الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره بطوله في حجة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إهلال المكّي والمتمتع بالحج في يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218). In another narration by him (1213): “Then we entered ihram on the Day of Tarwiyah.”","chapter_en":"The resident of Mecca and the one performing tamattu‘ enter ihram for pilgrimage on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":70,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: … Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came, they headed toward Mina and entered ihram for pilgrimage … the hadith."]},"buhuth":{"en":["And in another narration by him (1214): “The Prophet ﷺ ordered us, after we had exited ihram, to enter ihram when we set out for Mina.” He said: “So we entered ihram from al-Abtah.”","And in another narration by him (1216:142): “Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came, and we had put Mecca behind our backs, we entered ihram for pilgrimage.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218). وفي رواية له muslim(1213): (( ثم أهللنا يوم التروية ))."},{"num":5071,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدريّ، قال: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَصْرُخُ بِالحَجِّ صُرَاخًا، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا مَكَّةَ أَمَرَنَا أَنْ نَجْعَلَهَا عُمْرَةً إِلا مَنْ سَاقَ الهَدْيَ فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ وَرُحْنَا إِلَى مِنًى أَهْلَلْنَا بِالحَجِّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1247) عن عبيدالله بن عمر القواريريّ، حدّثنا عبد الأعلى بن عبد الأعلى، حدّثنا داود (هو ابن أبي هند)، عن أبي نضرة (هو المنذر بن مالك بن قطعة العبدي)، عن أبي سعيد، قال (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إهلال المكّي والمتمتع بالحج في يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1247).","chapter_en":"The resident of Mecca and the one performing tamattu‘ enter ihram for pilgrimage on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":70,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loudly proclaiming pilgrimage openly. Then when we arrived in Mecca, he ordered us to make it a lesser pilgrimage except for the one who had brought a sacrificial animal. Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came, we went on to Mina and entered ihram for pilgrimage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[4896],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1247)."},{"num":5072,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد العزيز بن رُفيع، قال: سَأَلْتُ أَنَسَ بْنَ مَالِكٍ، قُلْتُ: أَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ شَيْءٍ عَقَلْتَهُ عَنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَيْنَ صَلَّى الظُّهْرَ يَوْمَ التَّرْوِيَةِ؟ قَالَ: بِمِنًى. قُلْتُ: فَأَيْنَ صَلَّى الْعَصْرَ يَوْمَ النَّفْرِ؟ قَال: بِالأَبْطَحِ. ثُمَّ قَالَ افْعَلْ مَا يَفْعَلُ أُمَرَاؤُكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1653)، ومسلم في الحج (1309) كلاهما عن إسحاق بن يوسف الأزرق، حدّثنا سفيان (هو الثوريّ)، عن عبد العزيز بن رفيع، به، ولفظهما سواء إلاّ أنه وقع عند البخاريّ زيادة لفظة (العصر) في قوله: أين صلّى الظّهر والعصر يوم التروية.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب أداء الصلوات الخمس بمنى يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1653) and Muslim (1309).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of performing the five prayers in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":72,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Rafi‘ said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, and I said: Tell me about something you understood from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Where did he pray the noon prayer on the Day of Tarwiyah? He said: In Mina. I said: Then where did he pray the afternoon prayer on the day of departure? He said: At al-Abtah. Then he said: Do as your leaders do."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1653)، ومسلم (1309)."},{"num":5073,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله، قال: ...فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ تَوَجَّهُوا إِلَى مِنًى فَأَهَلُّوا بِالحَجِّ وَرَكِبَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَصَلَّى بِهَا الظُّهْرَ وَالْعَصْرَ وَالمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ وَالْفَجْرَ...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب أداء الصلوات الخمس بمنى يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of performing the five prayers in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":72,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: … Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came, they headed to Mina and entered into pilgrimage, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted and prayed there the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, the night prayer, and the dawn prayer … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5074,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: صَلَّى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الظُّهْرَ يَوْمَ التَّرْوِيَةِ وَالْفَجْرَ يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ بِمِنًى."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1911) ـ واللفظ له ـ، والترمذي (880) كلاهما من حديث الأعمش، عن الحكم، عن مقسم، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب أداء الصلوات الخمس بمنى يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1911), and this is his wording, and al-Tirmidhi (880).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of performing the five prayers in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":72,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer on the Day of Tarwiyah and the dawn prayer on the Day of ‘Arafah in Mina."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1911) - واللفظ له -، والترمذي (880)."},{"num":5075,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر، أَنَّهُ كَانَ يُحِبُّ إِذَا اسْتَطَاعَ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ الظُّهْرَ بِمِنًى مِنْ يَوْمِ التَّرْوِيَةِ وَذَلِكَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَلَّى الظُّهْرَ بِمِنًى."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6131) عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم بن سعد، ثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، ثني نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب أداء الصلوات الخمس بمنى يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (6131).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of performing the five prayers in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":72,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar used to like, whenever he was able, to pray the noon prayer in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah, and that was because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Mina."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6131)."},{"num":5076,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن الزُّبَيْرِ قَالَ: مِنْ سنّة الْحَجِّ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ الْإِمَامُ الظُّهْرَ وَالْعَصْرَ وَالْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ الْآخِرَةَ وَالصُّبْحَ بِمِنًى...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة (2800) عن يوسف بن موسى، ثنا جرير، عن يحيى، عن القاسم بن محمد، عن عبدالله بن الزبير، قال (فذكره). وسيأتي بتمامه في باب بماذا يحصل التّحلل الأول.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب أداء الصلوات الخمس بمنى يوم التروية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2800).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of performing the five prayers in Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":72,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said: It is from the practice of pilgrimage that the leader prays the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, the late evening prayer, and the dawn prayer in Mina … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة (2800)."},{"num":5077,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله قَالَ: صَلَّيْتُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِنًى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَأَبِي بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ، وَمَعَ عُثْمَانَ صَدْرًا مِنْ إِمَارَتِهِ ثُمَّ أَتَمَّهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في تقصير الصلاة (1082)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين (694) كلاهما من حديث عبيدالله، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1082) and Muslim (694).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in Mina as two units, and with Abu Bakr and ‘Umar, and with ‘Uthman during the early part of his rule, then he completed them as four."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1082)، ومسلم (694)."},{"num":5078,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر، قال: صَلَّى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِنًى صَلاةَ المُسَافِرِ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ وَعُثْمَانُ ثَمَانِيَ سِنِينَ أَوْ قَالَ سِتَّ سِنِينَ.","قَالَ حَفْصٌ: وَكَانَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ يُصَلِّي بِمِنًى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ يَأْتِي فِرَاشَهُ، فَقُلْتُ: أَيْ عَمِّ لَوْ صَلَّيْتَ بَعْدَهَا رَكْعَتَيْنِ. قَال: لَوْ فَعَلْتُ لأَتْمَمْتُ الصَّلاةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في صلاة المسافرين (694: 18) عن عبيدالله ابن معاذ، حدّثنا أبي، حدّثنا شعبة، عن خُبيب بن عبدالرحمن سمع حفص بن عاصم، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (694:18).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ prayed in Mina the prayer of a traveler, and so did Abu Bakr, ‘Umar, and ‘Uthman for eight years — or he said six years. Hafs said: Ibn ‘Umar used to pray two units in Mina, then come to his resting place. So I said: Uncle, if only you prayed two units after that. He said: If I did that, I would have completed the prayer."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (694 : 18)."},{"num":5079,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حَارِثَةَ بْنِ وَهْبٍ، قَالَ:  صَلَّيْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِنًى آمَنَ مَا كَانَ النَّاسُ وَأَكْثَرَهُ رَكْعَتَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في تقصير الصلاة (1083)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين (696) كلاهما من وجهين عن أبي إسحاق قال ـ في رواية أحدهما ـ سمعت حارثة بن وهب، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1083) and Muslim (696).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Harithah ibn Wahb said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Mina, at a time when the people were most secure and most numerous, as two units."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1083)، ومسلم (696)."},{"num":5080,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالرحمن بن يزيد قال: صَلَّى بِنَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ بِمِنًى أَرْبَعَ رَكَعَاتٍ، فَقِيلَ ذَلِكَ لِعبدالله بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ فَاسْتَرْجَعَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: صَلَّيْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِنًى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَصَلَّيْتُ مَعَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ بِمِنًى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَصَلَّيْتُ مَعَ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ بِمِنًى رَكْعَتَيْنِ فَلَيْتَ حَظِّي مِنْ أَرْبَعِ رَكَعَاتٍ رَكْعَتَانِ مُتَقَبَّلَتَانِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في تقصير الصلاة (1084)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين (695) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدّثنا عبد الواحد، عن الأعمش، قال: حدّثنا إبراهيم، قال: سمعت عبدالرحمن بن يزيد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1084) and Muslim (695).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid said: ‘Uthman ibn ‘Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, led us in Mina in four units. That was mentioned to ‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said the words of return to Allah, then said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Mina as two units, and I prayed with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, in Mina as two units, and I prayed with ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, in Mina as two units. If only my share from four units were two accepted ones."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1084)، ومسلم (695)."},{"num":5081,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة قالت: الصَّلاةُ أَوَّلُ مَا فُرِضَتْ رَكْعَتَيْنِ فَأُقِرَّتْ صَلاةُ السَّفَرِ وَأُتِمَّتْ صَلاةُ الحَضَرِ.","قَالَ الزُّهْرِيُّ فَقُلْتُ لِعُرْوَةَ: مَا بَالُ عَائِشَةَ تُتِمُّ؟ قَال: تَأَوَّلَتْ مَا تَأَوَّلَ عُثْمَانُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في تقصير الصلاة (1090)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين (685: 3) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن الزّهريّ، عن عروة، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1090) and Muslim (685:3).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: Prayer was first made obligatory as two units. Then the prayer of travel remained as it was, while the prayer of residence was completed. Al-Zuhri said: I said to ‘Urwah: Then why did ‘A’ishah pray it complete? He said: She interpreted it as ‘Uthman interpreted it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1090)، ومسلم (685 : 3)."},{"num":5082,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبّاد بن عبدالله بن الزُّبَيْرِ، قَالَ: لَمَّا قَدِمَ عَلَيْنَا مُعَاوِيَةُ حاجّاً قَدِمْنَا مَعَهُ مكّة، قَالَ: فَصَلَّى بِنَا الظُّهْرَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ إِلَى دَارِ النَّدْوَةِ. قَالَ: وَكَانَ عُثْمَانُ حِينَ أتمّ الصَّلَاةَ إِذَا قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ صلّى بِهَا الظُّهْرَ وَالْعَصْرَ وَالْعِشَاءَ الْآخِرَةَ أَرْبَعًا أَرْبَعًا، فَإِذَا خَرَجَ إِلَى مِنًى وَعَرَفَاتٍ قَصَرَ الصَّلَاةَ، فَإِذَا فَرَغَ مِنَ الْحَجِّ وَأَقَامَ بِمِنًى أَتَمَّ الصَّلَاةَ حَتَّى يَخْرُجَ مِنْ مَكَّةَ، فَلَمَّا صلّى بِنَا الظُّهْرَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ نَهَضَ إِلَيْهِ مَرْوَانُ بْنُ الْحَكَمِ وعَمْرُو بْنُ عُثْمَانَ فَقَالَا لَهُ: مَا عابَ أحدٌ ابنَ عمِّك بِأَقْبَحِ مَا عبْتَه بِهِ! فَقَالَ لَهُمَا: وَمَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَ: فَقَالَا لَهُ: أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أنّه أتّم الصَّلَاةَ بِمَكَّةَ؟ قَالَ: فَقَالَ لَهُمَا: وَيْحَكُمَا! وَهَلْ كَانَ غَيْرُ مَا صَنَعْتُ قَدْ صَلَّيْتُهُمَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَعَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا. قَالَا: فإنّ ابنَ عمِّك قَدْ كَانَ أتَمّها وإنّ خِلَافَكَ إِيَّاهُ لَهُ عَيْبٌ! قَالَ: فَخَرَجَ مُعَاوِيَةُ إِلَى الْعَصْرِ فَصَلَّاهَا بِنَا أَرْبَعًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16857)، والطبراني في الكبير (19/333) كلاهما من حديث يعقوب بن إبراهيم، حدّثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدّثنا يحيى بن عباد بن عبدالله بن الزبير، عن أبيه عباد، فذكره. واللفظ لأحمد ولفظ الطبرانيّ مختصر.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (16857) and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (19/333). This is the wording of Ahmad.","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abbad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said: When Mu‘awiyah came to us as a pilgrim, we arrived with him in Mecca. He said: He led us in the noon prayer as two units, then went to Dar al-Nadwah. He said: When ‘Uthman would complete the prayer, whenever he came to Mecca he would pray the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, and the late evening prayer there as four each. Then when he went out to Mina and ‘Arafat, he would shorten the prayer. Then when he finished the pilgrimage and stayed in Mina, he would complete the prayer until he departed from Mecca. So when Mu‘awiyah led us in the noon prayer as two units, Marwan ibn al-Hakam and ‘Amr ibn ‘Uthman got up and said to him: No one has found greater fault with your cousin than the way you have faulted him. He said to them: What is that? They said: Did you not know that he completed the prayer in Mecca? He said to them: Shame on you both. Was anything done other than what I have done? I prayed them this way with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and with Abu Bakr and ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. They said: But your cousin did do that, and your going against him will be counted as a criticism of him. He said: Then Mu‘awiyah went out for the afternoon prayer and led us in it as four units."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16857)، والطبراني في الكبير (19/333). واللفظ لأحمد."},{"num":5083,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ، بْنِ مَالِكٍ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: صَلَّيْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِنًى، رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَمَعَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَمَعَ عُمَرَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَمَعَ عُثْمَانَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ صَدْرًا مِنْ إِمَارَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائيّ (1447) عن قتيبة، حدّثنا الليث، عن بكير بن عبدالله، عن محمد بن عبدالله بن أبي سليم، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (1447) and Imam Ahmad (12464).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Mina, and with Abu Bakr and ‘Umar as two units, and with ‘Uthman as two units during the early part of his rule."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (1447)، والإمام أحمد (12464)."},{"num":5084,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي جُحَيْفَةَ، قَالَ: صَلَّيْتُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم بِمِنًى الظُّهْرَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ لَمْ نَزَلْ نُصَلِّي رَكْعَتَيْنِ حَتَّى رَجَعَ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (8165)، والطبرانيّ في الكبير (22/102) كلاهما من حديث وكيع، ثنا سفيان، وابن أبي ليلى، عن عون ابن أبي جحيفة، عن أبيه، فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah (2/448) and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (22/102).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Juhayfah said: I prayed the noon prayer with the Prophet ﷺ in Mina as two units, and he continued praying two units until he returned to Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (8165)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/102)."},{"num":5085,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عِمْرَانَ بْنِ حُصَيْنٍ عَنْ صَلاَةِ الْمُسَافِرِ فَقَالَ: حَجَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَصَلَّى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَحَجَجْتُ مَعَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ فَصَلَّى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَمَعَ عُمَرَ فَصَلَّى رَكْعَتَيْنِ، وَمَعَ عُثْمَانَ سِتَّ سِنِينَ مِنْ خِلاَفَتِهِ أَوْ ثَمَانِيَ سِنِينَ فَصَلَّى رَكْعَتَيْنِ ـ ثُمَّ إنّ عُثْمَانَ صلّى بعد ذَلِكَ أَرْبَعًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (545) ـ واللفظ له ـ، وأبو داود (1229) مختصراً، والإمام أحمد (19865)، وأبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (2/450) في سياق أطول من هذا ـ كلّهم من طريق علي بن جدعان، عن أبي نضرة، أنّ فتى سأل عمران بن حصين، عن صــلاة رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال (فذكره).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الصلاة بمنى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (545), and this is his wording, Abu Dawud (1229), and Imam Ahmad (19865).","chapter_en":"Shortening the prayer in Mina","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":73,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Imran ibn Husayn, speaking about the prayer of the traveler, said: I performed pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he prayed two units, and I performed pilgrimage with Abu Bakr and he prayed two units, and with ‘Umar and he prayed two units, and with ‘Uthman for six years of his caliphate, or eight years, and he prayed two units. Then after that, ‘Uthman prayed four."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (545) - واللفظ له -، وأبو داود (1229)، والإمام أحمد (19865)."},{"num":5086,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قَالَ: فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ التَّرْوِيَةِ تَوَجَّهُوا إِلَى مِنًى، فَأَهَلُّوا بِالْحَجِّ، وَرَكِبَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَصَلَّى بِهَا الظُّهْرَ وَالْعَصْرَ وَالْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ وَالْفَجْرَ، ثُمَّ مَكَثَ قَلِيلًا حَتَّى طَلَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ، وَأَمَرَ بِقُبَّةٍ مِنْ شَعَرٍ تُضْرَبُ لَهُ بِنَمِرَةَ، فَسَارَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلَا تَشُكُّ قُرَيْشٌ إِلَّا أَنَّهُ وَاقِفٌ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ كَمَا كَانَتْ قُرَيْشٌ تَصْنَعُ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَأَجَازَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى أَتَى عَرَفَةَ، فَوَجَدَ الْقُبَّةَ قَدْ ضُرِبَتْ لَهُ بِنَمِرَةَ، فَنَزَلَ بِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر بطوله في حجّة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الخروج من منى إلى نمرة إذا طلعت الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of leaving Mina for Namirah after sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":74,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came, they headed to Mina and entered into pilgrimage. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted and prayed there the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, the night prayer, and the dawn prayer. Then he stayed a little until the sun rose, and he ordered that a tent of hair be set up for him at Namirah. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proceeded, while Quraysh had no doubt that he would stop at the Sacred Monument, as Quraysh used to do in the pre-Islamic period. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed on until he came to ‘Arafah and found the tent set up for him at Namirah, so he stayed there."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “Namirah,” refers to a place beside ‘Arafat and not part of ‘Arafat. As for the wording, “until he came to ‘Arafah and found the tent set up for him at Namirah,” this is figurative speech, and what is meant is that he came near ‘Arafah. Sharh Muslim."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5087,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: غَدَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ مِنًى حِينَ صَلَّى الصُّبْحَ صَبِيحَةَ يَوْمِ عَرَفَةَ حَتَّى أَتَى عَرَفَةَ، فَنَزَلَ بِنَمِرَةَ وَهِيَ مَنْزِلُ الإِمَامِ الَّذِي يَنْزِلُ بِهِ بِعَرَفَةَ، حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ عِنْدَ صَلاَةِ الظُّهْرِ رَاحَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُهَجِّرًا، فَجَمَعَ بَيْنَ الظُّهْرِ وَالْعَصْرِ ثُمَّ خَطَبَ النَّاسَ ثُمَّ رَاحَ فَوَقَفَ عَلَى الْمَوْقِفِ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1913) عن أحمد وهو في مسنده ahmad(6130) عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم، حدّثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدثني نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الخروج من منى إلى نمرة إذا طلعت الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1913) and Ahmad (6130).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of leaving Mina for Namirah after sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":74,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Mina after praying the dawn prayer on the morning of the Day of ‘Arafah, until he came to ‘Arafah. He stayed at Namirah, which is the place where the leader stays at ‘Arafah. Then when it was time for the noon prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out early in the heat of midday, and he combined the noon and afternoon prayers, then addressed the people, then went on and stood at the standing place in ‘Arafah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1913)، وأحمد (6130)."},{"num":5088,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ الثَّقَفِيِّ، أَنَّهُ سَأَلَ أَنَسَ بْنَ مَالِكٍ وَهُمَا غَادِيَانِ مِنْ مِنًى إِلَى عَرَفَةَ: كَيْفَ كُنْتُمْ تَصْنَعُونَ فِي هَذَا الْيَوْمِ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ فَقَالَ كَانَ يُهِلُّ مِنَّا الْمُهِلُّ فَلاَ يُنْكِرُ عَلَيْهِ، وَيُكَبِّرُ مِنَّا الْمُكَبِّرُ فَلاَ يُنْكِرُ عَلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (43) عن محمد بن أبي بكر الثقفيّ، بالإسناد.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التلبية والتكبير عند الخروج من منى إلى عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (43), al-Bukhari (1659), and Muslim (1285).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of reciting the talbiyah and saying the takbir when leaving Mina for ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":75,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi asked Anas ibn Malik, while the two of them were going from Mina to ‘Arafah: How did you used to act on this day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: The one among us who recited the talbiyah would do so and no one objected to him, and the one among us who said the takbir would do so and no one objected to him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11130],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (43)، والبخاري (1659)، ومسلم (1285)."},{"num":5089,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ، قَالَ: غَدَوْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ مِنى إِلَى عَرَفَاتٍ، مِنَّا الْمُلَبِّي، ومِنَّا الْمُكَبِّرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1284) من طريق يحيى بن سعيد (هو الأنصاريّ)، عن عبدالله بن أبي سلمة (هو الماجشون)، عن عبدالله بن عبدالله بن عمر، عن أبيه، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التلبية والتكبير عند الخروج من منى إلى عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1284).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of reciting the talbiyah and saying the takbir when leaving Mina for ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":75,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Mina to ‘Arafat. Some of us were reciting the talbiyah and some of us were saying the takbir."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated it with the wording: “We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the morning of ‘Arafah. Some of us were saying the takbir and some of us were reciting the talbiyah. As for us, we were saying the takbir.”","He said: I said: By Allah, it is strange about you — why did you not say to him: What did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing?"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11131],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1284)."},{"num":5090,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَالِمِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: كَتَبَ عَبْدُ الْمَلِكِ بْنُ مَرْوَانَ إِلَى الْحَجَّاجِ بْنِ يُوسُفَ: أَنْ لاَ تُخَالِفَ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ فِي شَىْءٍ مِنْ أَمْرِ الْحَجِّ. قَالَ: فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ عَرَفَةَ، جَاءَهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ حِينَ زَالَتِ الشَّمْسُ وَأَنَا مَعَهُ، فَصَاحَ بِهِ عِنْدَ سُرَادِقِهِ: أَيْنَ هَذَا؟ فَخَرَجَ عَلَيْهِ الْحَجَّاجُ وَعَلَيْهِ مِلْحَفَةٌ مُعَصْفَرَةٌ، فَقَالَ: مَا لَكَ يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ فَقَالَ: الرَّوَاحَ إِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ السُّنَّةَ. فَقَالَ: أَهَذِهِ السَّاعَةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنْظِرْنِي حَتَّى أُفِيضَ عَلَىَّ مَاءً، ثُمَّ أَخْرُجَ. فَنَزَلَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ حَتَّى خَرَجَ الْحَجَّاجُ فَسَارَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ أَبِي، فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: إِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ أَنْ تُصِيبَ السُّنَّةَ الْيَوْمَ فَاقْصُرِ الْخُطْبَةَ وَعَجِّلِ الصَّلاَةَ. - قَالَ: - فَجَعَلَ يَنْظُرُ إِلَى عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ كَيْمَا يَسْمَعَ ذَلِكَ مِنْهُ، فَلَمَّا رَأَى ذَلِكَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ قَالَ: صَدَقَ سَالِمٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الحج (194) عن ابن شهاب، عن سالم، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قصر الخطبة وتعجيل الصلاة يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (194) and al-Bukhari (1660).","chapter_en":"Shortening the sermon and hastening the prayer on the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":76,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salim ibn ‘Abd Allah said: ‘Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan wrote to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf telling him not to oppose ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar in anything related to pilgrimage. He said: Then when it was the Day of ‘Arafah, ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar came to him after the sun had passed its zenith, and I was with him, and he called out to him at the entrance of his tent: Where is this man? Al-Hajjaj came out to him wearing a saffron-colored wrap, and said: What is it, Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman? He said: It is time to depart, if you want the Sunnah. He said: At this hour? He said: Yes. He said: Then give me time until I pour water over myself, then I will come out. So ‘Abd Allah got down and waited until al-Hajjaj came out. Then he walked between me and my father, and I said to him: If you want to attain the Sunnah today, then shorten the sermon and hasten the prayer. He began looking toward ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar so that he could hear that from him. When ‘Abd Allah saw that, he said: Salim has spoken the truth."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (194)، والبخاري (1660)."},{"num":5091,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: فخطب الناس وقال (فذكر خطبته صلى الله عليه وسلم)... ثم أذّن، ثم أقام فصلّى الظهر، ثم أقام فصلّى العصر، ولم يصلِّ بينهما شيئاً...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر الحديث بطوله في حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين الصلاتين في عرفة بأذان وإقامتين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Combining the two prayers in ‘Arafah with one call to prayer and two calls to commence prayer","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":77,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: Then he addressed the people and said — and he mentioned the Prophet’s sermon ﷺ — … then the call to prayer was made, then the call to commence prayer was made, and he prayed the noon prayer. Then the call to commence prayer was made again, and he prayed the afternoon prayer, and he did not pray anything between them … the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5092,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا كَانَتْ قُرَيْشٌ وَمَنْ دَانَ دِينَهَا يَقِفُونَ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ، وَكَانُوا يُسَمَّوْنَ الْحُمْسَ، وَكَانَ سَائِرُ الْعَرَبِ يَقِفُونَ بِعَرَفَاتٍ، فَلَمَّا جَاءَ الإِسْلاَمُ أَمَرَ اللَّهُ نَبِيَّهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ عَرَفَاتٍ، ثُمَّ يَقِفَ بِهَا، ثُمَّ يُفِيضَ مِنْهَا، فَذَلِكَ قَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 199]}."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4520)، ومسلم في الحج (1219) كلاهما من طريق أبي معاوية محمد بن خازم، حدثنا هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4520) and Muslim (1219).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: Quraysh and those who followed their religion used to stand at Muzdalifah, and they were called al-Hums, while the rest of the Arabs used to stand at ‘Arafat. Then when Islam came, Allah commanded His Prophet ﷺ to go to ‘Arafat and stand there, then depart from there. That is the meaning of His statement, Most High: “Then depart from where the people depart.” [al-Baqarah: 199]"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: (ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ) [سورة البقرة: ١٩٩]."],"en":["Allah Most High said: “Then depart from where the people depart, and seek forgiveness from Allah. Surely Allah is Ever-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” [Surat al-Baqarah: 199]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11983],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4520)، ومسلم (1219)."},{"num":5093,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ:  كَانَتِ الْعَرَبُ تَطُوفُ بِالْبَيْتِ عُرَاةً إِلَّا الْحُمْسَ، وَالْحُمْسُ قُرَيْشٌ وَمَا وَلَدَتْ، كَانُوا يَطُوفُونَ عُرَاةً، إِلَّا أَنْ تُعْطِيَهُمُ الْحُمْسُ ثِيَابًا، فَيُعْطِي الرِّجَالُ الرِّجَالَ، وَالنِّسَاءُ النِّسَاءَ، وَكَانَتِ الْحُمْسُ لَا يَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ وَكَانَ النَّاسُ كُلُّهُمْ يَبْلُغُونَ عَرَفَاتٍ.","قَالَ هِشَامٌ: فَحَدَّثَنِي أَبِي عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رضي الله عنها قَالَتْ: الْحُمْسُ هُمُ الَّذِينَ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عزوجل فِيهِمْ: ﴿ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 199].199]. قَالَتْ: كَانَ النَّاسُ يُفِيضُونَ مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ، وَكَانَ الْحُمْسُ يُفِيضُونَ مِنَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ يَقُولُونَ لَا نُفِيضُ إِلَّا مِنَ الْحَرَمِ، فَلَمَّا نَزَلَتْ: أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حيث أفاض الناس رَجَعُوا إِلَى عَرَفَاتٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1665) من حديث علي بن مسهر، ومسلم في الحج (1219: 152) من حديث أسامة ـ كلاهما عن هشام، عن أبيه، فذكره،","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1665) and Muslim (1219:152), and this is the wording of Muslim. The wording of al-Bukhari is close to it, and contains: “So they went on to ‘Arafat,” meaning that they were commanded to go to ‘Arafat, stand there, and then depart from it.","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Urwah said: The Arabs used to circumambulate the House naked, except for al-Hums — and al-Hums were Quraysh and their offspring. They used to circumambulate clothed only if al-Hums gave them clothes: men would give men, and women would give women. Al-Hums would not go beyond Muzdalifah, while all the other people would go as far as ‘Arafat. Hisham said: My father told me from ‘A’ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: Al-Hums are the ones concerning whom Allah revealed: “Then depart from where the people depart.” She said: The people used to depart from ‘Arafat, while al-Hums used to depart from Muzdalifah, saying: We do not depart except from the Sacred Precinct. Then when “Then depart from where the people depart” was revealed, they returned to ‘Arafat."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Hums is pronounced with a dammah on the letter ha’, a sukun on the letter mim, followed by sin.","Its explanation, as Ibrahim al-Harbi narrated in “Gharib al-Hadith” through Ibn Jurayj from Mujahid, is: “Al-Hums were Quraysh and those tribes that took the same path as Quraysh, such as al-Aws, al-Khazraj, Khuza‘ah, Thaqif, Ghazwan, Banu ‘Amir ibn Sa‘sa‘ah, and Banu Kinanah except Banu Bakr. In Arabic, al-ahmas means severe or strict. They were called that because they imposed strictness upon themselves. When they entered into pilgrimage or the lesser pilgrimage, they would not eat meat, nor use wool or hair coverings. When they arrived in Mecca, they would remove the clothes they had been wearing.”","Ibrahim also narrated through ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn ‘Imran al-Madani: “They were called Hums in relation to the Ka‘bah because it was darkish in color, its stones being white inclining toward blackness.” Abu ‘Ubaydah Ma‘mar ibn al-Muthanna said: “Tahammusa means to be strict; from it comes the phrase ‘the battle became fierce’ when it intensified.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1665)، ومسلم (1219 : 152)، واللفظ لمسلم. ولفظ البخاري قريب منه، وفيه: (( فدفعوا إلى عرفات )) أي أمروا أن يتوجهوا إلى عرفات ليقفوا بها ثم يفيضوا منها."},{"num":5094,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جُبَيْرِ بْنِ مُطْعِمٍ، قَالَ:  أَضْلَلْتُ بَعِيرًا لِي، فَذَهَبْتُ أَطْلُبُهُ يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ، فَرَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَاقِفًا مَعَ النَّاسِ بِعَرَفَةَ، فَقُلْتُ: وَاللهِ، إِنَّ هَذَا لَمِنَ الْحُمْسِ، فَمَا شَأْنُهُ هَا هُنَا؟ وَكَانَتْ قُرَيْشٌ تُعَدُّ مِنَ الْحُمْسِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1664)، ومسلم في الحج (1220) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، حدثنا عمرو (هو ابن دينار)، حدثنا محمد بن جبير بن مطعم، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1664) and Muslim (1220).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: I lost a camel of mine, so I went looking for it on the Day of ‘Arafah, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the people at ‘Arafah. So I said: By Allah, this man is certainly one of al-Hums, so what is he doing here? Quraysh were counted among al-Hums."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The correct understanding here is that the story of Jubayr ibn Mut‘im with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took place before Islam. Jubayr embraced Islam on the day of the Conquest, and his going to ‘Arafah was to look for his lost camel, not to stand there for pilgrimage.","This is confirmed by what Ibn Khuzaymah narrated in his Sahih, as in the following hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1664)، ومسلم (1220)."},{"num":5095,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جُبَيْرِ بْنِ مُطْعِمٍ قَالَ: كَانَتْ قُرَيْشٌ إِنَّمَا تَدْفَعُ مِنَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ، وَيَقُولُونَ: نَحْنُ الْحُمْسُ، فَلَا نَخْرُجُ مِنَ الْحَرَمِ، وَقَدْ تَرَكُوا الْمَوْقِفَ عَلَى عَرَفَةَ. قَالَ: فَرَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ يَقِفُ مَعَ النَّاسِ بِعَرَفَةَ عَلَى جَمَلٍ لَهُ، ثُمَّ يُصْبِحُ مَعَ قَوْمِهِ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ فَيَقِفُ مَعَهُمْ يَدْفَعُ إِذَا دَفَعُوا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (2823) عن نصر بن علي، أخبرنا وهب بن جرير، ثنا أبي، عن محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني عبدالله بن أبي بكر، عن عثمان ابن أبي سليمان، عن عمه نافع بن جبير، عن أبيه جبير بن مطعم، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2823). He also narrated it (3057) through another chain containing: “I certainly saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before revelation came to him, standing on a camel of his at ‘Arafat with the people, departing with them from there, and that was nothing but guidance granted by Allah.”","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: Quraysh used to depart only from Muzdalifah and would say: We are al-Hums, so we do not go outside the Sacred Precinct. They had abandoned the standing place at ‘Arafah. He said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period standing with the people at ‘Arafah on a camel of his. Then in the morning he would be with his people at Muzdalifah, standing with them and departing when they departed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “before revelation came to him,” means before the revelation of the verse: “Then depart from where the people depart.” So the Prophet ﷺ used to stand at ‘Arafat before this verse was revealed. In it is evidence for the statement, “and that was nothing but guidance granted by Allah,” meaning that Allah, Glorified and Exalted, confirmed the Prophet ﷺ’s action.","Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: “When I embraced Islam, I came to know that Allah had guided him to that.” This is how Ishaq ibn Rahuyah narrated it: Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: “I lost a donkey of mine in the pre-Islamic period and found it at ‘Arafah. There I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at ‘Arafat with the people. When I embraced Islam, I came to know that Allah had guided him to that.” See al-Fath (3/516)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (2823). ورواه أيضا ibnkhuzaymah(3057) من وجه آخر فيه: (( لقد رأيت رسول الله ﷺ قبل أن ينزل عليه، وإنه لواقف على بعير له بعرفات مع الناس، يدفع معهم منها، وما ذاك إلا توفيقا من الله ))."},{"num":5096,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: يَطَوَّفُ الرَّجُلُ بِالْبَيْتِ مَا كَانَ حَلاَلاً حَتَّى يُهِلَّ بِالْحَجِّ، فَإِذَا رَكِبَ إِلَى عَرَفَةَ فَمَنْ تَيَسَّرَ لَهُ هَدِيَّةٌ مِنَ الإِبِلِ أَوِ الْبَقَرِ أَوِ الْغَنَمِ، مَا تَيَسَّرَ لَهُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ، أَىَّ ذَلِكَ شَاءَ، غَيْرَ إِنْ لَمْ يَتَيَسَّرْ لَهُ فَعَلَيْهِ ثَلاَثَةُ أَيَّامٍ فِي الْحَجِّ، وَذَلِكَ قَبْلَ يَوْمِ عَرَفَةَ، فَإِنْ كَانَ آخِرُ يَوْمٍ مِنَ الأَيَّامِ الثَّلاَثَةِ يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ فَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ لِيَنْطَلِقْ حَتَّى يَقِفَ بِعَرَفَاتٍ مِنْ صَلاَةِ الْعَصْرِ إِلَى أَنْ يَكُونَ الظَّلاَمُ، ثُمَّ لِيَدْفَعُوا مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ إِذَا أَفَاضُوا مِنْهَا حَتَّى يَبْلُغُوا جَمْعًا الَّذِي يُتَبَرَّرُ فِيهِ، ثُمَّ لِيَذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثِيرًا، أَوْ أَكْثِرُوا التَّكْبِيرَ وَالتَّهْلِيلَ قَبْلَ أَنْ تُصْبِحُوا، ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا، فَإِنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوا يُفِيضُونَ، وَقَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 199]} حَتَّى تَرْمُوا الْجَمْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في التفسير (4521) عن محمد بن أبي بكر، حدّثنا فضيل بن سليمان، حدثنا موسى بن عقبة، أخبرني كريب، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4521).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: A man may circumambulate the House while still lawful until he enters into pilgrimage. Then when he rides toward ‘Arafah, if he can obtain an offering from camels, cattle, or sheep, then whatever is easy for him of that — whichever he chooses. But if he cannot obtain one, then he must fast three days during the pilgrimage, and that must be before the Day of ‘Arafah. If the last of those three days is the Day of ‘Arafah, then there is no harm in that. Then let him proceed until he stands at ‘Arafat from the afternoon prayer until it becomes dark. Then let them depart from ‘Arafat when they depart from it, until they reach Muzdalifah where they spend the night. Then let them remember Allah much, and increase in saying the takbir and the declaration of His oneness before morning. Then depart, for the people used to depart, and Allah Most High said: “Then depart from where the people depart, and seek forgiveness from Allah. Surely Allah is Ever-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” [al-Baqarah: 199] — until you stone the pillar."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4521)."},{"num":5097,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ أَبِي يَعْمَرَ الدِّيلِيِّ، قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ بِعَرَفَةَ فَجَاءَ نَاسٌ - أَوْ نَفَرٌ - مِنْ أَهْلِ نَجْدٍ فَأَمَرُوا رَجُلاً فَنَادَى رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَيْفَ الْحَجُّ فَأَمَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَجُلاً، فَنَادَى: الْحَجُّ الْحَجُّ يَوْمُ عَرَفَةَ مَنْ جَاءَ قَبْلَ صَلاَةِ الصُّبْحِ مِنْ لَيْلَةِ جَمْعٍ فَتَمَّ حَجُّهُ أَيَّامُ مِنًى ثَلاَثَةٌ: ﴿فَمَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ فَلاَ إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ وَمَنْ تَأَخَّرَ فَلاَ إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ﴾. [سورة البقرة: 203]. قَالَ: ثُمَّ أَرْدَفَ رَجُلاً خَلْفَهُ فَجَعَلَ يُنَادِي بِذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1949)، والترمذي (889)، والنسائي (210، 3047)، وابن ماجه (3015) كلّهم من حديث سفيان الثوريّ، عن بكير بن عطاء، عن عبدالرحمن بن يعمر الدّيليّ، فذكره واللفظ لأبي داود.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1949), al-Tirmidhi (889), al-Nasa’i (3047, 3010), and Ibn Majah (3015), and this is the wording of Abu Dawud.","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya‘mar al-Dayli said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at ‘Arafah. Then some people, or a group from Najd, came and told a man to call out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: How is pilgrimage performed? So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man, and he called out: “Pilgrimage is the Day of ‘Arafah. Whoever arrives before the dawn prayer on the night of Muzdalifah, his pilgrimage is complete. The days of Mina are three: ‘Whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.’” He said: Then he seated a man behind him, and he continued calling this out."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1949)، والترمذي (889)، والنسائي (3047، 3010)، وابن ماجه (3015)، واللفظ لأبي داود."},{"num":5098,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عُرْوَةُ بْنُ مُضَرِّسٍ الطَّائِيُّ، قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْمَوْقِفِ - يَعْنِي بِجَمْعٍ قُلْتُ: جِئْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مِنْ جَبَلِ طَيِّئٍ أَكْلَلْتُ مَطِيَّتِي وَأَتْعَبْتُ نَفْسِي، وَاللَّهِ مَا تَرَكْتُ مِنْ جَبَلٍ إِلاَّ وَقَفْتُ عَلَيْهِ! فَهَلْ لِي مِنْ حَجٍّ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ أَدْرَكَ مَعَنَا هَذِهِ الصَّلاَةَ، وَأَتَى عَرَفَاتٍ قَبْلَ ذَلِكَ لَيْلاً أَوْ نَهَارًا فَقَدْ تَمَّ حَجُّهُ وَقَضَى تَفَثَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1950)، والترمذيّ (891)، والنسائيّ (3039)، وابن ماجه (3016) كلّهم من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، حدّثنا عامر الشعبيّ، عن عروة بن مضرس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1950), al-Tirmidhi (891), al-Nasa’i (3039), and Ibn Majah (3016).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Ta’i said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the standing place — meaning at Muzdalifah — and said: I have come, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Mount Tayy’, I have exhausted my riding animal and worn myself out. By Allah, I did not leave any hill but that I stood upon it. So do I have a pilgrimage? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever joins us in this prayer, and had come to ‘Arafat before that, by night or by day, then his pilgrimage is complete and he has completed his rites of cleansing.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1950)، والترمذي (891)، والنسائي (3039)، وابن ماجه (3016)."},{"num":5099,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : مَنْ أَدْرَكَ عَرَفَاتٍ فَوَقَفَ بِهَا وَالْمُزْدَلِفَةَ فَقَدْ تَمَّ حَجُّهُ، وَمَنْ فَاتَهُ عَرَفَاتٌ فَقَدْ فَاتَهُ الْحَجُّ فَلْيَحِلَّ بِعُمْرَةٍ وَعَلَيْهِ الْحَجُّ مِنْ قَابِلٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الدارقطنيّ (2519) من طريق ابن أبي ليلى، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Daraqutni (2519) and al-Bayhaqi (5/174).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches ‘Arafat and stands there, and reaches Muzdalifah, then his pilgrimage is complete. And whoever misses ‘Arafat has missed the pilgrimage, so let him exit the state of consecration with an ‘umrah, and he must perform pilgrimage the following year.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الدارقطني (2519)، والبيهقي (5/174)."},{"num":5100,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ أَدْرَكَ عَرَفَةَ قَبْلَ طُلُوعِ الْفَجْرِ فَقَدْ أَدْرَكَ الْحَجَّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط – مجمع البحرين (1759) –وعنه أبو نعيم في الحلية (740)- عن محمد بن أحمد بن أبي خيثمي، حدثنا عبدالله بن عبدالمؤمن الواسطي، حدثنا عبيد بن عقيل، عن عمر بن ذر، عن عطاء بن أبي رباح، عن ابن عباس قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Awsat — Majma‘ al-Bahrayn (1759), and Abu Nu‘aym narrated it from him in al-Hilyah (5/116).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches ‘Arafah before dawn rises has reached the pilgrimage.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (1759)، وعنه أبو نعيم في الحلية (740)."},{"num":5101,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : الحجُّ عَرَفَاتٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط –مجمع البحرين (1757) عن محمد بن الحسين أبو حصين، حدثنا عبدالرحمن بن يونس الرقي، حدثنا عبدالسلام بن حرب، عن خصيف، عن مجاهد، عن ابن عباس قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب وجوب الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Awsat — Majma‘ al-Bahrayn (1757).","chapter_en":"The obligation of standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":78,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The pilgrimage is ‘Arafah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (1757)."},{"num":5102,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: نَحَرْتُ ههنا وَمِنًى كلُّها مَنْحر، فَانْحَرُوا فِي رِحَالِكُمْ، وَوَقَفْتُ ههنا وَعَرَفَةُ كلُّها مَوْقِفٌ، وَوَقَفْتُ ههنا وجَمْعٌ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218: 149) عن عمر بن حفص ابن غياث، حدّثنا أبي، عن جعفر (وهو ابن محمد بن علي بن الحسين بن علي ابن أبي طالب)، حدّثني أبي، عن جابر، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنّ عرفة كلّها موقف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218:149).","chapter_en":"What has been narrated that all of ‘Arafah is a place of standing","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":79,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I sacrificed here, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, so sacrifice in your camps. And I stood here, and all of ‘Arafah is a place of standing. And I stood here, and all of Muzdalifah is a place of standing.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218 : 149)."},{"num":5103,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: وَقَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِعَرَفَةَ فَقَالَ: هَذِهِ عَرَفَةُ وَهَذَا هُوَ الْمَوْقِفُ وَعَرَفَةُ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ. ثُمَّ أَفَاضَ حِينَ غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ وَأَرْدَفَ أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ، وَجَعَلَ يُشِيرُ بِيَدِهِ عَلَى هَيْئَتِهِ وَالنَّاسُ يَضْرِبُونَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالاً يَلْتَفِتُ إِلَيْهِمْ وَيَقُولُ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ! عَلَيْكُمُ السَّكِينَةَ. ثُمَّ أَتَى جَمْعًا فَصَلَّى بِهِمُ الصَّلاَتَيْنِ جَمِيعًا فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحَ أَتَى قُزَحَ فَوَقَفَ عَلَيْهِ، وَقَالَ: هَذَا قُزَحُ وَهُوَ الْمَوْقِفُ وَجَمْعٌ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ. ثُمَّ أَفَاضَ حَتَّى انْتَهَى إِلَى وَادِي مُحَسِّرٍ فَقَرَعَ نَاقَتَهُ فَخَبَّتْ حَتَّى جَاوَزَ الْوَادِيَ فَوَقَفَ وَأَرْدَفَ الْفَضْلَ، ثُمَّ أَتَى الْجَمْرَةَ فَرَمَاهَا، ثُمَّ أَتَى الْمَنْحَرَ، فَقَالَ: هَذَا الْمَنْحَرُ وَمِنًى كُلُّهَا مَنْحَرٌ. وَاسْتَفْتَتْهُ جَارِيَةٌ شَابَّةٌ مِنْ خَثْعَمٍ فَقَالَتْ إِنَّ أَبِي شَيْخٌ كَبِيرٌ قَدْ أَدْرَكَتْهُ فَرِيضَةُ اللَّهِ فِي الْحَجِّ أَفَيُجْزِئُ أَنْ أَحُجَّ عَنْهُ قَالَ حُجِّي عَنْ أَبِيكِ. قَالَ وَلَوَى عُنُقَ الْفَضْلِ فَقَالَ الْعَبَّاسُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ لِمَ لَوَيْتَ عُنُقَ ابْنِ عَمِّكَ قَالَ رَأَيْتُ شَابًّا وَشَابَّةً فَلَمْ آمَنِ الشَّيْطَانَ عَلَيْهِمَا. ثُمَّ أَتَاهُ رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنِّي أَفَضْتُ قَبْلَ أَنْ أَحْلِقَ. قَالَ احْلِقْ أَوْ قَصِّرْ وَلاَ حَرَجَ.","قَالَ: وَجَاءَ آخَرُ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ، إِنِّي ذَبَحْتُ قَبْلَ أَنْ أَرْمِيَ، قَالَ: ارْمِ وَلَا حَرَجَ. قَالَ: ثُمَّ أَتَى الْبَيْتَ فَطَافَ بِهِ ثُمَّ أَتَى زَمْزَمَ فَقَالَ: يَا بَنِي عبدالمطلب، لَوْلَا أَنْ يَغْلِبَكُمُ النَّاسُ عَنْهُ لَنَزَعْتُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (885)، وأبو داود (1922، 1935)، وابن ماجه (3010) كلّهم من حديث سفيان، عن عبدالرحمن بن الحارث بن عياش بن أبي ربيعة، عن زيد بن علي، عن أبيه، عن عبيدالله بن أبي رافع، عن علي بن أبي طالب، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنّ عرفة كلّها موقف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (885) and Abu Dawud (1935, 1922). Al-Tirmidhi said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"What has been narrated that all of ‘Arafah is a place of standing","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":79,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at ‘Arafah and said: “This is ‘Arafah, and this is the standing place, and all of ‘Arafah is a standing place.” Then he departed when the sun had set, and he had Usamah ibn Zayd ride behind him. He kept gesturing with his hand calmly while the people were rushing right and left, turning to them and saying: “O people, remain calm.” Then he came to Muzdalifah and led them in the two prayers together. When morning came, he went to Quzah and stood upon it, and said: “This is Quzah, and it is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.” Then he departed until he reached the valley of Muhassir, and he urged his she-camel on so that it hastened until it crossed the valley. Then he stopped and had al-Fadl ride behind him. Then he came to the pillar and stoned it, then he came to the place of sacrifice and said: “This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.” A young woman from Khath‘am asked him for a ruling and said: My father is an old man upon whom the obligation of pilgrimage has come — will it suffice if I perform pilgrimage on his behalf? He said: “Perform pilgrimage on behalf of your father.” He said: Then he turned al-Fadl’s neck away, so al-‘Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, why did you turn your cousin’s neck away? He said: “I saw a young man and a young woman, and I did not feel safe from Satan concerning them.” Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I departed before shaving. He said: “Shave or shorten, and there is no harm.” Another came and said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I sacrificed before stoning. He said: “Stone, and there is no harm.” Then he came to the House and circumambulated it, then he came to Zamzam and said: “O sons of ‘Abd al-Muttalib, were it not that the people might overpower you and drive you away from it, I would have drawn water.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (885)، وأبو داود (1935، 1922)، قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5104,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: قال رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: عرفةُ كُلُّها موقفٌ، وارْفعُوْا عن بطنِ عُرنة، والمزدلفةُ كلُّها موقفٌ، وارْفعُوْا عن بطنِ مُحَسّر، وشِعَابُ منىً كلُّها منحرٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطحاوي في شرح مشكل الآثار (1194) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم بن يونس البغدادي، قال: ثنا أبو الأشعث أحمد بن المقدام العجلي، قال: ثنا ابن عيينة، عن زياد بن سعد، عن أبي الزبير، عن أبي معبد، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنّ عرفة كلّها موقف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tahawi in Sharh Mushkil al-Athar (1194).","chapter_en":"What has been narrated that all of ‘Arafah is a place of standing","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":79,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of ‘Arafah is a standing place, but keep away from the bottom of ‘Uranah. All of Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from the bottom of Muhassir. And all the mountain passes of Mina are places of sacrifice.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطحاوي في شرح مشكل الآثار (1194)."},{"num":5105,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يَزِيدَ بْنِ شيبان، قَالَ: كُنَّا وُقُوفًا بِعَرَفَةَ مَكَانًا بَعِيدًا مِنَ الْمَوْقِفِ، فَأَتَانَا ابْنُ مِرْبَعٍ الأَنْصَارِيُّ، فَقَالَ: إِنِّي رَسُولُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَيْكُمْ يَقُولُ: كُونُوا عَلَى مَشَاعِرِكُمْ، فَإِنَّكُمْ عَلَى إِرْثٍ مِنْ إِرْثِ أَبِيكُمْ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1919)، والترمذي (883)، والنسائي (3014)، وابن ماجه (3011) كلّهم من حديث سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو ابن دينار، عن عمرو بن عبدالله بن صفوان، عن يزيد بن شيبان، فذكره ولفظهم متقارب.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تنبيه الحجاج على عدم الوقوف خارج حدود عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1919), al-Tirmidhi (883), al-Nasa’i (3014), and Ibn Majah (3011).","chapter_en":"Warning the pilgrims against standing outside the boundaries of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":80,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazid ibn Shayban said: We were standing in ‘Arafah at a place far from the standing place, then Ibn Mirba‘ al-Ansari came to us and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you. He says: “Remain at your sacred sites, for you are upon an inheritance from the inheritance of your father Ibrahim, peace be upon him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1919)، والترمذي (883)، والنسائي (3014)، وابن ماجه (3011)."},{"num":5106,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ارْفَعُوا عَنْ بَطْنِ عُرَنَةَ، وَارْفَعُوا عَنْ بَطْنِ مُحَسِّرٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (2816)، والحاكم (1697) وعنه البيهقيّ (9461) كلّهم من حديث محمد بن كثير، ثنا سفيان بن عيينة، عن زياد بن سعد، عن أبي الزبير، عن أبي معبد، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تنبيه الحجاج على عدم الوقوف خارج حدود عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2816), al-Hakim (1/462), and from him al-Bayhaqi (5/115).","chapter_en":"Warning the pilgrims against standing outside the boundaries of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":80,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep away from the bottom of ‘Uranah. Keep away from the bottom of Muhassir.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (2816)، والحاكم (1697)، وعنه البيهقي (9461)."},{"num":5107,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَا مِنْ يومٍ أَكْثَرَ مِنْ أَنْ يُعْتق اللهُ فِيهِ عَبْدًا مِنَ النَّارِ مِنْ يَوْمِ عَرَفَةَ، وَإِنَّهُ لَيَدْنُو ثُمَّ يُبَاهِي بِهِمُ الْمَلَائِكَةَ فَيَقُولُ مَا أَرَادَ هَؤُلَاءِ؟."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1348) من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني مخرمة بن بكير، عن أبيه، قــــــال: سمعت يونس بن يوسف يقول: عن ابن المسيب، قـــــال: قــــــالت عائشة (فذكرته).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1348).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no day on which Allah frees more servants from the Fire than the Day of ‘Arafah. He draws near, then boasts of them before the angels and says: What do these people want?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[529,10719],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1348)."},{"num":5108,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن طارق بن شهاب: أنّ أُناساً من اليهود قالوا: لو نزلت هذه الآية فينا لاتخذنا ذلك اليوم عيداً! فقال عمر أيَّةُ آيةٍ؟ فقالوا: ﴿الْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ وَأَتْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِي وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ الْإِسْلَامَ دِينًا﴾ [المائدة: 3]. فقال عمر: إنّي لأعلمُ أيّ مكان أُنزلتْ؛ أُنزلتْ ورسولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ واقف بعرفة."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازيّ (4407)، ومسلم في التفسير (3017) كلاهما من طريق سفيان الثوريّ، عن قيس بن مسلم، عن طارق بن شهاب، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4407) and Muslim (3017).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Tariq ibn Shihab said: Some Jews said: If this verse had been revealed to us, we would have taken that day as a festival. ‘Umar said: Which verse? They said: “Today I have perfected for you your religion, completed My favor upon you, and approved Islam for you as your religion.” [Surat al-Ma’idah: 3] So ‘Umar said: I certainly know the place where it was revealed. It was revealed while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing at ‘Arafah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10720],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4407)، ومسلم (3017)."},{"num":5109,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أَفْضَلُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ مِنْ أَيَّامِ عَشْرِ ذِي الْحِجَّةِ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، هُنَّ أَفْضَلُ أَمْ عِدَّتُهُنَّ جِهَادًا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: هُنَّ أَفْضَلُ مِنْ عِدَّتِهِنَّ جِهَادًا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، وَمَا مِنْ يوْمٍ أَفْضَلُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ مِنْ يوْمِ عَرَفَةَ، يَنْزِلُ اللَّهُ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى إِلَى السَّمَاءِ الدُّنْيَا فَيُبَاهِي بِأَهْلِ الأَرْضِ أَهْلَ السَّمَاءِ، فَيَقُولُ: انْظُرُوا إِلَى عِبَادِي جاؤوا شُعْثًا غُبْرًا حاجين، جَاؤُوا مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٍ يَرْجُونَ رَحْمَتِي، وَلَمْ يَرَوْا عَذَابِي، فَلَمْ يُرَ يَوْمٌ أَكْثَرُ عِتْقًا مِنَ النَّارِ مِنْ يوْمِ عَرَفَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (3853) من طريق محمد بن مروان العقيليّ، حدّثنا هشام -هو الدّستوائيّ -، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (3853), Abu Ya‘la (2090), and al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1128).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are no days more virtuous before Allah than the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah.” A man said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, are they better, or an equal number of days of striving in the path of Allah? He said: “They are better than an equal number of days of striving in the path of Allah. And there is no day more virtuous before Allah than the Day of ‘Arafah. Allah descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of the people of the earth before the people of heaven, saying: Look at My servants, disheveled, dusty, and exposed to the sun. They have come from every distant mountain path, hoping for My mercy though they have not seen My punishment. So there is no day on which more people are freed from the Fire than the Day of ‘Arafah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (3853)، وأبو يعلى (2090)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1128)."},{"num":5110,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ يُبَاهِي الْمَلَائِكَةَ بِأَهْلِ عَرَفَاتٍ، يَقُولُ: انْظُرُوا إِلَى عِبَادِي شُعْثًا غُبْرًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (8047) عن أبي قَطن وإسماعيل بن عمر، قالا: حدّثنا يونس، عن مجاهد أبي الحجّاج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (8047). It was authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2839), Ibn Hibban (3852), and al-Hakim (1/465).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasts to the angels about the people of ‘Arafat, saying: Look at My servants, disheveled and dusty.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[530,10721],"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (8047)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2839)، وابن حبان (3852)، والحاكم (1708)."},{"num":5111,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عمرو بْنِ الْعَاصِ، أنّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقُولُ: إنّ اللَّهَ عزوجل يُبَاهِي مَلَائِكَتَهُ عَشِيَّةَ عَرَفَةَ بِأَهْلِ عَرَفَةَ، فَيَقُولُ: انْظُرُوا إِلَى عِبَادِي أَتَوْنِي شُعْثاً غُبْراً."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (7089) عن أزهر بن القاسم، حدثنا المثنى -يعني ابن سعيد-، عن قتادة، عن عبدالله بن باباه، عن عبدالله بن عمرو، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (7089).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to say: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasts to His angels on the evening of ‘Arafah about the people of ‘Arafah, saying: Look at My servants; they have come to Me disheveled and dusty.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (7089)."},{"num":5112,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الأَنْصَارِيِّ فَقَالَ: إنْ شئتَ أَخْبَرْتُكَ عمَّا جئْتَ تَسْأَلُ، وإنْ شئْتَ سَأَلْتَنِي فأخْبرُكَ. فَقَالَ: لَا يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ أَخْبَرَنِي عمّا جئتُ أسألُكَ. قَالَ: جئتَ تَسْألُني عَنِ الْحَاجِّ مَا لَهُ حِينَ يَخْرُجُ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ؟ وَمَا لَهُ حِينَ يَقُومُ بِعَرَفَاتٍ؟ وَمَا لَهُ حِينَ يَرْمِي الْجِمَارَ؟ وَمَا لَهُ حِينَ يَحْلِقُ رَأْسَهُ؟ وَمَا لَهُ حِينَ يَقْضِي آخِرَ طَوَافٍ بِالْبَيْتِ. فَقَالَ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ مَا أَخْطَأْتَ مِمَّا كَانَ فِي نَفْسِي شَيْئًا! قَالَ: فإنّ لَهُ حِينَ يَخْرُجُ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ أَنَّ رَاحِلَتَهُ لَا تَخْطُو خُطْوَةً إِلَاّ كُتِبَ لَهُ بِهَا حَسَنَةٌ أَوْ حطّت عَنْهُ بِهَا خَطِيئَةٌ، فَإِذَا َوقفَ بِعَرَفَةَ فإنّ اللَّهَ عزّ وجلّ يَنْزِلُ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ الدُّنْيَا فيقــول: انْظُرُوا إِلَى عِبَادِي شُعْثاً غُبْراً اشْهَدُوا أنّي قَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَهُمْ ذُنُوبَهُمْ وَإِنْ كَانَ عَدَدَ قَطْرِ السَّمَاءِ وَرَمْلِ عَالِجٍ. وَإِذَا رَمَى الْجِمَارَ لَا يَدْرِي أحدٌ مَا لَهُ حَتَّى يُوَفَّاهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. وَإِذَا حَلَقَ رَأْسَهُ فَلَهُ بِكُلِّ شَعْرَةٍ سَقَطَتْ مِنْ رَأْسِهِ نُورٌ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. وَإِذَا قَضَى آخِرَ طَوَافِهِ بِالْبَيْتِ خَرَجَ مِنْ ذُنُوبِهِ كَيَوْمِ وَلَدَتْهُ أمُّه."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (1887)، والبيهقيّ في دلائل النبوة (6/294)، والبزار ـ كشف الأستار ـ (1082) كلّهم من حديث يحيى ابن عبدالرحمن الأرحبي، حدثني عبيدة بن الأسود، عن القاسم بن الوليد، عن سنان بن الحارث بن مصرف، عن طلحة بن مصرف، عن مجاهد، عن ابن عمر، فذكر حديثاً طويلاً، وهذا جزء منه.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (1887), al-Bayhaqi in Dala’il al-Nubuwwah (6/294), and al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1082).","chapter_en":"The virtue of the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":81,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to an Ansari man and said: “If you wish, I can tell you what you came to ask about, and if you wish, ask me and I will tell you.” He said: No, O Prophet of Allah ﷺ, tell me about what I came to ask you. He said: “You came to ask me about the pilgrim: what he receives when he leaves his house, what he receives when he stands at ‘Arafat, what he receives when he stones the pillars, what he receives when he shaves his head, and what he receives when he completes his final circumambulation of the House.” He said: O Prophet of Allah ﷺ, by the One who sent you with the truth, you did not miss anything that was in my mind. He said: “When he leaves his house, his mount does not take a single step except that Allah writes for him by it a good deed or removes from him by it a sin. When he stands at ‘Arafat, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and says: Look at My servants, disheveled and dusty. Bear witness that I have forgiven them their sins, even if they were as many as the raindrops of the sky and the sands of ‘Alij. When he stones the pillars, no one knows what reward he has until it is fully given to him on the Day of Resurrection. When he shaves his head, for every hair that falls from his head he will have a light on the Day of Resurrection. And when he completes his final circumambulation of the House, he comes out of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (1887)، والبيهقي في دلائل النبوة (6/294)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1082)."},{"num":5113,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي أَيُّوبَ، أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ قَالَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلَى كلّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، عَشْرَ مَرَّاتٍ كَانَ كَمَنْ أَعْتَقَ أَرْبَعَةَ أَنْفُسٍ مِنْ وَلَدِ إِسْمَاعِيلَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ (6404)، ومسلم (2693) كلاهما من حديث عمر بن أبي زائدة، عن أبي إسحاق، عن عمرو بن ميمون، قال: من قال: لا إله إلا الله... إلخ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الترغيب في قول: لا إله إلا الله وحده لا شريك له","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6404) and Muslim (2693).","chapter_en":"Encouragement to say: None has the right to be worshipped except Allah alone, with no partner","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":82,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Ayyub reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says: None has the right to be worshipped except Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, it is as if he freed four persons from the descendants of Isma‘il.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10818],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6404)، ومسلم (2693)."},{"num":5114,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَفْضَلُ مَا قُلْتُ أَنَا وَالنَّبِيُّونَ قَبْلِي عَشِيَّةَ عَرَفَةَ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ، لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ، وَهُوَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الدعاء (874) من طريق قيس بن الربيع، عن الأغر بن الصباح، عن خليفة بن حصين، عن علي رضي الله عنه، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الترغيب في قول: لا إله إلا الله وحده لا شريك له","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Du‘a’ (874).","chapter_en":"Encouragement to say: None has the right to be worshipped except Allah alone, with no partner","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":82,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of what I and the prophets before me said on the evening of ‘Arafah is: None has the right to be worshipped except Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He is over all things capable.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11132],"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الدعاء (874)."},{"num":5115,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ الْفَضْلِ بِنْتِ الْحَارِثِ، أَنَّ نَاسًا، اخْتَلَفُوا عِنْدَهَا يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ فِي صَوْمِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: هُوَ صَائِمٌ. وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: لَيْسَ بِصَائِمٍ. فَأَرْسَلَتْ إِلَيْهِ بِقَدَحِ لَبَنٍ وَهْوَ وَاقِفٌ عَلَى بَعِيرِهِ فَشَرِبَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (132) عن أبي النّضر مولى عمر بن عبيدالله، عن عُمير مولى عبدالله بن عباس، عن أم الفضل، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الفطر للحاج يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (132), al-Bukhari (1661), and Muslim (1123:110).","chapter_en":"The recommendation that the pilgrim not fast on the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":83,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith reported that some people disputed in her presence on the Day of ‘Arafah about whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fasting. Some said: He is fasting. Others said: He is not fasting. So she sent to him a cup of milk while he was standing on his riding animal, and he drank it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5119],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (132)، والبخاري (1661)، ومسلم (110 : 1123)."},{"num":5116,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَيْمُونَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا أَنَّ النَّاسَ، شَكُّوا فِي صِيَامِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ، فَأَرْسَلَتْ إِلَيْهِ بِحِلاَبٍ وَهْوَ وَاقِفٌ فِي الْمَوْقِفِ، فَشَرِبَ مِنْهُ، وَالنَّاسُ يَنْظُرُونَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الصوم (1989)، ومسلم في الصيام (1124) كلاهما من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني عمرو (هو ابن الحارث)، عن بكير (هو ابن عبدالله بن الأشج)، عن كريب مولى ابن عباس، عن ميمونة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الفطر للحاج يوم عرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1989) and Muslim (1124).","chapter_en":"The recommendation that the pilgrim not fast on the Day of ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":83,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The people doubted whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fasting on the Day of ‘Arafah, so I sent him a vessel of milk while he was standing at the place of standing, and he drank from it while the people were watching."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[4499],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1989)، ومسلم (1124)."},{"num":5117,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: ثُمَّ رَكِبَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى أَتَى الْمَوْقِفَ، فَجَعَلَ بَطْنَ نَاقَتِهِ الْقَصْوَاءِ إِلَى الصَّخَرَاتِ، وَجَعَلَ حَبْل الْمُشَاةِ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، وَاسْتَقْبَلَ الْقِبْلَةَ... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره بطوله في حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب الدعاء في عرفة واستقبال القبلة بذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of supplication at ‘Arafah and facing the qiblah for it","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":84,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode until he came to the standing place, and he placed the belly of his she-camel al-Qaswa’ toward the rocks, and placed the path of the walkers before him, and faced the qiblah… the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5118,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُسَامَةَ بن زَيْدٍ كُنْتُ رَدِيفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِعَرَفَاتٍ، فَرَفَعَ يَدَيْهِ يَدْعُو، فَمَالَتْ بِهِ نَاقَتُهُ، فَسَقَطَ خِطَامُهَا، قَالَ: فَتَنَاوَلَ الْخِطَامَ بِإِحْدَى يَدَيْهِ، وَهُوَ رَافِعٌ يَدَهُ الْأُخْرَى."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائيّ (3011) عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم، عن هُشيم، قال: حدثنا عبد الملك، عن عطاء، قال: قال أسامة، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب رفع اليدين في الدعاء عند الوقوف بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3011) and Ahmad (21821), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2824).","chapter_en":"Raising the hands in supplication while standing at ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":85,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usamah ibn Zayd said: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at ‘Arafat, and he raised his hands in supplication. Then his she-camel leaned and its rein fell, so he took hold of the rein with one hand while the other hand remained raised."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3011)، وأحمد (21821)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2824)."},{"num":5119,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ الْفَضْلِ بِنْتِ الْحَارِثِ، أَنَّ نَاسًا، اخْتَلَفُوا عِنْدَهَا يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ فِي صَوْمِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: هُوَ صَائِمٌ. وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: لَيْسَ بِصَائِمٍ. فَأَرْسَلَتْ إِلَيْهِ بِقَدَحِ لَبَنٍ وَهْوَ وَاقِفٌ عَلَى بَعِيرِهِ فَشَرِبَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (132) عن أبي النّضر مولى عمر بن عبيدالله، عن عُمير مولى عبدالله بن عباس، عن أم الفضل، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الوقوف على الدابة ونحوها بعرفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (132), al-Bukhari (1661), and Muslim (1123:110).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of standing at ‘Arafah on a riding animal and the like","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":86,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith reported that some people disputed in her presence on the Day of ‘Arafah about whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fasting. Some said: He was fasting, and others said: He was not fasting. So she sent him a cup of milk while he was standing on his camel, and he drank."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5115],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (132)، والبخاري (1661)، ومسلم (110 : 1123)."},{"num":5120,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: فلم يزل (يعني النبيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم) واقفاً حتّى غربتْ الشّمس، وذهبت الصُّفرة قليلا حتى غاب القرْص...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره بطوله في حجة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الإفاضة من عرفات بعد غروب الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Departing from ‘Arafah after sunset","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":87,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: He — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — remained standing until the sun had set, and the yellow glow had faded somewhat, until the disk disappeared… the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5121,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ قَالَ: وَقَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِعَرَفَةَ ثُمَّ أَفَاضَ حِينَ غَابَتِ الشَّمْسُ، وَأَرْدَفَ أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1922، 1935)، والترمذي (885)، وابن ماجه (3010)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2837) ـ واللّفظ له ـ كلّهم من حديث سفيان، عن عبدالرحمن بن الحارث بن عياش، عن زيد بن علي، عن أبيه، عن عبيدالله بن أبي رافع، عن علي، فذكره في حديث طويل كما ذكره الترمذيّ ـ ومضى قريباً ـ وغيره رواه مختصراً، واللفظ هنا لابن خزيمة الذي اختصره في هذا الجزء الخاص بالإفاضة من عرفة.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الإفاضة من عرفات بعد غروب الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1935, 1922), al-Tirmidhi (885), and Ibn Majah (3010), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2837).","chapter_en":"Departing from ‘Arafah after sunset","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":87,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at ‘Arafah, then departed when the sun had set, and he had Usamah ibn Zayd ride behind him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1935، 1922)، والترمذي (885)، وابن ماجه (3010)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2837)."},{"num":5122,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ، قَالَ: كُنْتُ رِدْفَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَلَمَّا وَقَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ دَفَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1924) عن أحمد بن حنبل، حدثنا يعقوب، حدثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدثني إبراهيم بن عقبة، عن كريب مولى عبدالله بن عباس، عن أسامة، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الإفاضة من عرفات بعد غروب الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1924).","chapter_en":"Departing from ‘Arafah after sunset","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":87,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usamah said: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and when the sun had set the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1924)."},{"num":5123,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُرْوَةَ بن مضرس الطائي قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْمَوْقِفِ - يَعْنِي بِجَمْعٍ قُلْتُ: جِئْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مِنْ جَبَلِ طَيِّئٍ أَكْلَلْتُ مَطِيَّتِي وَأَتْعَبْتُ نَفْسِي، وَاللَّهِ مَا تَرَكْتُ مِنْ جَبَلٍ إِلاَّ وَقَفْتُ عَلَيْهِ! فَهَلْ لِي مِنْ حَجٍّ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ أَدْرَكَ مَعَنَا هَذِهِ الصَّلاَةَ، وَأَتَى عَرَفَاتٍ قَبْلَ ذَلِكَ لَيْلاً أَوْ نَهَارًا فَقَدْ تَمَّ حَجُّهُ وَقَضَى تَفَثَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1950)، والترمذي (891)، والنسائي (3041)، وابن ماجه (3016) كلّهم من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، حدّثنا عامر الشعبيّ، عن عروة بن مضرّس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الإفاضة من عرفات بعد غروب الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1950), al-Tirmidhi (891), al-Nasa’i (3041), and Ibn Majah (3016). Al-Tirmidhi said: “This is a Hasan Sahih hadith.”","chapter_en":"Departing from ‘Arafah after sunset","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":87,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Ta’i said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the standing place — meaning at Muzdalifah — and said: I have come, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Mount Tayy’, I have exhausted my riding animal and worn myself out. By Allah, I did not leave any hill but that I stood upon it. So do I have a pilgrimage? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever joins us in this prayer, and had come to ‘Arafat before that by night or by day, then his pilgrimage is complete and he has completed his rites.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1950)، والترمذي (891)، والنسائي (3041)، وابن ماجه (3016). قال الترمذي: (( هذا حديث حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5124,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُرْوَةَ بن الزُّبَيْرِ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: سُئل أُسَامَةُ بن زَيْدٍ وَأَنَا جَالِسٌ مَعَهُ: كَيْفَ كَانَ يَسِيرُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حجّة الْوَدَاعِ حِينَ دَفَعَ؟ قَالَ: كَانَ يَسِيرُ العَنَق، فَإِذَا وَجَدَ فَجْوَةً نصَّ.","قال مالك: قال هشام: والنَّصُّ فوق العَنَق."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (176) عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، فذكره. ورواه البخاريّ في الحج (1666) عن عبدالله بن يوسف، أخبرنا مالك، به، مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (176), al-Bukhari (1666), and Muslim (1286:283-284).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Urwah ibn al-Zubayr reported that Usamah ibn Zayd was asked while I was sitting with him: How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ travel in the Farewell Pilgrimage when he departed? He said: He moved at a moderate pace, and when he found an open space he hastened. Malik said: Hisham said: Hastening is faster than the moderate pace."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (176)، والبخاري (1666)، ومسلم (1286 : 283-284)."},{"num":5125,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّهُ دَفَعَ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ عَرَفَةَ فَسَمِعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَرَاءَهُ زَجْرًا شَدِيدًا، وَضَرْبًا وَصَوْتًا لِلإِبِلِ، فَأَشَارَ بِسَوْطِهِ إِلَيْهِمْ وَقَالَ: أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، فَإِنَّ الْبِرَّ لَيْسَ بِالإِيضَاعِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1671) عن سعيد بن أبي مريم، حدّثنا إبراهيم بن سويد، حدثني عمرو بن أبي عمرو مولى المطّلب، أخبرني سعيد بن جبير مولى والبة الكوفي، حدثني ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1671).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that he departed with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of ‘Arafah, and the Prophet ﷺ heard behind him loud rebuking, striking, and shouting at the camels. So he pointed to them with his whip and said: “O people, remain calm, for righteousness is not in rushing.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1671)."},{"num":5126,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: وَدَفَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ شَنَقَ لِلْقَصْوَاءِ الزِّمَامَ، حَتَّى إنَّ رَأْسَهَا لَيُصِيبُ مَوْرِكَ رَحْلِهِ وَيَقُولُ بِيَدِهِ الْيُمْنَى: أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، السَّكِينَةَ السَّكِينَةَ الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدنيّ، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر بطوله في صفة حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed while holding al-Qaswa’ with a shortened rein, to the point that her head almost touched the front part of his saddle, and he was saying with his right hand: “O people, calmness, calmness…” the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5127,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْفَضْلِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ وَكَانَ رَدِيفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،  أَنَّهُ قَالَ فِي عَشِيَّةِ عَرَفَةَ وَغَدَاةِ جَمْعٍ لِلنَّاسِ حِينَ دَفَعُوا: عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، وَهُْوَ كَافٌّ نَاقَتَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1282) من طريق أبي الزبير عن أبي معبد مولى ابن عباس، عن ابن عباس، عن الفضل بن عباس، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1282).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Fadl ibn ‘Abbas — who was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — reported that on the evening of ‘Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah he said to the people when they departed: “Remain calm,” while he was restraining his camel."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[5147],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1282)."},{"num":5128,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ،  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَفَاضَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ، وَأُسَامَةُ رِدْفُهُ. قَالَ أُسَامَةُ: فَمَا زَالَ يَسِيرُ عَلَى هَيْئَتِهِ حَتَّى أَتَى جَمْعًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1286: 282) من طريق يزيد بن هارون، أخبرنا عبد الملك بن أبي سليمان، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1286:282).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ‘Arafah, with Usamah riding behind him. Usamah said: He continued moving in the same calm manner until he came to Muzdalifah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1286 : 282)."},{"num":5129,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَفَاضَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ، وَرَدِيفُهُ أُسَامَةُ، فَجَعَلَ يَكْبَحُ رَاحِلَتَهُ حَتَّى أَنَّ ذِفْرَاهَا لَتَكَادُ أَنْ تَمَسَّ، وَرُبَّمَا قَالَ حَمَّادٌ: أَنْ تُصِيبَ، قَادِمَةَ الرَّحْلِ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ وَالْوَقَارِ، فَإِنَّ الْبِرَّ لَيْسَ فِي إِيضَاعِ الْإِبِلِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3018) وأحمد (21756) والبيهقي (9485) كلهم من طرق عن حماد بن سلمة، عن قيس بن سعد، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، عن أسامة بن زيد، قال: فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3018), Ahmad (21756), and al-Bayhaqi (5/119).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usamah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ‘Arafah with Usamah riding behind him. He kept restraining his mount until the area behind its ears nearly touched — or, as Hammad said, struck — the front of the saddle, and he was saying: “O people, keep calm and dignified, for righteousness is not in making the camels rush.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3018)، وأحمد (21756)، والبيهقي (9485)."},{"num":5130,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ أَرْدَفَ أُسَامَةَ، فَجَعَلَ يُعْنِقُ عَلَى نَاقَتِهِ، وَالنَّاسُ يَضْرِبُونَ الإِبِلَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالاً لاَ يَلْتَفِتُ إِلَيْهِمْ وَيَقُولُ: السَّكِينَةَ أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ. وَدَفَعَ حِينَ غَابَتِ الشَّمْسُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1922)، والترمذيّ (885) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن عبدالرحمن بن الحارث بن عياش بن أبي ربيعة، عن زيد ابن علي، عن أبيه، عن عبيدالله بن أبي رافع، عن علي بن أبي طالب، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الإفاضة من عرفات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1922) and al-Tirmidhi (885).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from ‘Arafah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":88,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: Then he had Usamah ride behind him, and he made his she-camel move at a moderate pace, while the people were driving the camels right and left. He turned toward them and said: “Calmness, O people,” and he departed when the sun had set."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1922)، والترمذي (885)."},{"num":5131,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ: أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صلّى الْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ جَمِيعًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (196) عن ابن شهاب، عن سالم بن عبدالله، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين الصلاتين بالمزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (196), Muslim (703:286), and al-Bukhari (1673).","chapter_en":"Combining the two prayers at Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":89,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha together at Muzdalifah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (196)، ومسلم (703 : 286)، والبخاري (1673)."},{"num":5132,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي أَيُّوبَ الأنصاريّ، أنّه صَلَّى مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حجّة الْوَدَاعِ الْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ جَمِيعًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحجّ (198) عن يحيى بن سعيد (هو الأنصاري)، عن عدي بن ثابت الأنصاريّ، أنّ عبدالله بن يزيد الخطمي أخبره، أنّ أبا أيوب الأنصاريّ أخبره، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين الصلاتين بالمزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (198), al-Bukhari (4414), and Muslim (1287).","chapter_en":"Combining the two prayers at Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":89,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Ayyub al-Ansari reported that he prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha together at Muzdalifah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (198)، والبخاري (4414)، ومسلم (1287)."},{"num":5133,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا أَفَاضَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ عَدَلَ إِلَى الشِّعْبِ، فَقَضَى حَاجَتَهُ. قَالَ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ: فَجَعَلْتُ أَصُبُّ عَلَيْهِ وَيَتَوَضَّأُ. فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَتُصَلِّي؟ فَقَالَ: الْمُصَلَّى أَمَامَكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الوضوء (181) ومسلم في الحج (1280) كلاهما من حديث كريب مولى ابن عباس، عن أسامة بن زيد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين الصلاتين بالمزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1681) and Muslim (1280).","chapter_en":"Combining the two prayers at Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":89,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usamah ibn Zayd reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ‘Arafah, he turned toward the mountain pass and relieved himself. Usamah ibn Zayd said: Then I poured water for him while he performed ablution. I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, will you pray now? He said: “The prayer is ahead of you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (181)، ومسلم (1280)."},{"num":5134,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: حَتَّى أَتَى الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ، فَصَلَّى بِهَا الْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ بِأَذَانٍ وَاحِدٍ وَإِقَامَتَيْنِ، وَلَمْ يسبِّح بَيْنَهُمَا شَيْئًا، ثُمَّ اضْطَجَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى طَلَعَ الْفَجْرُ... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر حديث حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: Then he came to Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha there with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and he did not glorify Allah with any voluntary prayer between them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down until dawn broke… the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5135,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: جَمَعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ الْمَغْرِبِ وَالْعِشَاءِ بِجَمْعٍ، كُلُّ وَاحِدَةٍ مِنْهُمَا بِإِقَامَةٍ، وَلَمْ يُسَبِّحْ بَيْنَهُمَا وَلاَ عَلَى إِثْرِ كُلِّ وَاحِدَةٍ مِنْهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1673) من طريق ابن أبي ذئب، عن الزهري، به، نحوه وزاد: كلُّ واحدة منهما بإقامة، ولم يسبِّح بينهما، ولا على إثر كلّ واحدة منهما.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1673) and Muslim (1288:287).","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ combined Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah, each one of them with its own commencement call, and he did not perform voluntary prayer between them nor after either of them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1673)، ومسلم (1288 : 287)."},{"num":5136,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعِيدِ بْنِ جُبَيْرٍ،  أَنَّهُ صَلَّى الْمَغْرِبَ بِجَمْعٍ وَالْعِشَاءَ بِإِقَامَةٍ، ثُمَّ حَدَّثَ عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ أَنَّهُ صَلَّى مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ، وَحَدَّثَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَنَعَ مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1288: 288) عن محمد بن المثنى، حدّثنا عبدالرحمن بن مهدي، حدثنا شعبة، عن الحكم وسلمة بن كهيل، عن سعيد بن جبير، قال: فذكره. وقال: وحدثنيه زهير بن حرب، حدثنا وكيع، حدثنا شعبة بهذا الإسناد، وقال: صلاهما بإقامة واحدة.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1288:288).","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sa‘id ibn Jubayr reported that he prayed Maghrib at Muzdalifah and ‘Isha with a commencement call, then narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that he prayed in that way, and Ibn ‘Umar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ had done the same."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1288 : 288)."},{"num":5137,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن مَالِكٍ، أنّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ صلّى بِجَمْعٍ، فَجَمَعَ بَيْنَ الصَّلاَتَيْنِ بِإِقَامَةٍ. وَقَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَعَلَ مِثْلَ هَذَا فِي هَذَا الْمَكَانِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (887)، وأبو داود (1929) كلاهما من حديث سفيان الثوري، عن أبي إسحاق، عن عبدالله بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (887) and Abu Dawud (1929), and the wording is that of al-Tirmidhi. He said: “This is a Hasan Sahih hadith.”","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn Malik reported that Ibn ‘Umar prayed at Muzdalifah and combined the two prayers with a commencement call, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do the same in this place."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (887)، وأبو داود (1929)، واللفظ للترمذي. وقال: (( هذا حديث حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5138,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: إنه صَلَّى مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ الْمَغْرِبَ وَالْعِشَاءَ بِإِقَامَةٍ إِقَامَةٍ جَمَعَ بَيْنَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1927) عن الإمام أحمد ـ وهو في المسند (6473) ـ وفيه قال (أي عبدالله بن أحمد): قرأت على أبي: حدثنا حماد بن خالد، عن ابن أبي ذئب، عن الزهري، عن سالم، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1927) and Ahmad (6473).","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar said: He prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Muzdalifah with one commencement call, combining the two together."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Abu Dawud said: Ahmad said: Waki‘ said: “He prayed each prayer with its own commencement call,” though no one else mentioned that wording."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1927)، وأحمد (6473)."},{"num":5139,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أشعث بن سُلَيْمٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: أَقْبَلْتُ مَعَ ابْنِ عُمَرَ مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ إِلَى الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ فَلَمْ يَكُنْ يَفْتُرُ مِنَ التَّكْبِيرِ وَالتَّهْلِيلِ حَتَّى أَتَيْنَا الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ، فَأَذَّنَ وَأَقَامَ أَوْ أَمَرَ إِنْسَانًا فَأَذَّنَ وَأَقَامَ فَصَلَّى بِنَا الْمَغْرِبَ ثَلاَثَ رَكَعَاتٍ، ثُمَّ الْتَفَتَ إِلَيْنَا فَقَالَ: الصَّلاَةُ فَصَلَّى بِنَا الْعِشَاءَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ دَعَا بِعَشَائِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1933) عن مسدد، حدثنا أبو الأحوص، حدثنا أشعث بن سليم، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجمع بين صلاتي المغرب والعشاء في مزدلفة بأذان واحد وإقامتين، ولا يتنفّل بينهما ولا على إثرهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1933).","chapter_en":"Combining Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one call to prayer and two commencement calls, and not offering voluntary prayer between them or immediately after them","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":90,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ash‘ath ibn Sulaym, from his father, said: I came with Ibn ‘Umar from ‘Arafat to Muzdalifah, and he did not cease making takbir and tahlil until we reached Muzdalifah. Then he gave the call to prayer and the commencement call — or he ordered someone to do so — and led us in Maghrib with three units. Then he turned to us and said: The prayer. Then he led us in ‘Isha with two units, and then he called for his evening meal."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1933)."},{"num":5140,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، أَنَّهُ سَمِعَهُ يَقُولُ دَفَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ عَرَفَةَ حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ بِالشِّعْبِ نَزَلَ فَبَالَ، ثُمَّ تَوَضَّأَ وَلَمْ يُسْبِغِ الْوُضُوءَ. فَقُلْتُ الصَّلاَةَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. فَقَالَ: الصَّلاَةُ أَمَامَكَ. فَرَكِبَ، فَلَمَّا جَاءَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ نَزَلَ فَتَوَضَّأَ، فَأَسْبَغَ الْوُضُوءَ، ثُمَّ أُقِيمَتِ الصَّلاَةُ فَصَلَّى الْمَغْرِبَ، ثُمَّ أَنَاخَ كُلُّ إِنْسَانٍ بَعِيرَهُ فِي مَنْزِلِهِ، ثُمَّ أُقِيمَتِ الْعِشَاءُ فَصَلَّى وَلَمْ يُصَلِّ بَيْنَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحجّ (197) عن موسى بن عقبة، عن كريب مولى ابن عباس، عن أسامة بن زيد، به، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من قال: يجمع بينهما بإقامتين فقط بدون أذان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (197), al-Bukhārī (1672), and Muslim (1280:276).","chapter_en":"Those who said that the two prayers are combined with two iqāmahs only, without an adhān","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":91,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ‘Arafah, and when he reached the mountain pass he stopped, urinated, and performed ablution, but he did not do it thoroughly. I said to him, “The prayer, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “The prayer is ahead of you.” Then he rode on. When he came to Muzdalifah, he dismounted and performed ablution thoroughly. Then the iqāmah was given and he prayed Maghrib. After that, each person made his camel kneel at his place. Then the iqāmah for ‘Ishā’ was given, and he prayed it, and he did not pray anything between them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (197)، والبخاري (1672)، ومسلم (276 : 1280)."},{"num":5141,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي إسحق قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عبدالرحمن بْنَ يَزِيدَ يَقُولُ: حجّ عبدالله رَضِيَ اللَّهِ عَنْهُ، فَأَتَيْنَا الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ حِينَ الأَذَانِ بِالْعَتَمَةِ أَوْ قَرِيبًا مِنْ ذَلِكَ فَأَمَرَ رَجُلاً فَأَذَّنَ وَأَقَامَ، ثُمَّ صَلَّى الْمَغْرِبَ وَصَلَّى بَعْدَهَا رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ دَعَا بِعَشَائِهِ فَتَعَشَّى ثُمَّ أَمَرَ - أُرَى - فَأَذَّنَ وَأَقَامَ.","قَالَ عَمْرٌو: لاَ أَعْلَمُ الشَّكَّ إِلاَّ مِنْ زُهَيْرٍ ـ ثُمَّ صَلَّى الْعِشَاءَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ فَلَمَّا طَلَعَ الْفَجْرُ قَالَ: إِنَّ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم كَانَ لاَ يُصَلِّي هَذِهِ السَّاعَةَ إِلاَّ هَذِهِ الصَّلاَةَ فِي هَذَا الْمَكَانِ مِنْ هَذَا الْيَوْمِ .","قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: هُمَا صَلاَتَانِ تُحَوَّلاَنِ عَنْ وقتها صَلاَةُ الْمَغْرِبِ بَعْدَ مَا يَأْتِي النَّاسُ الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ، وَالْفَجْرُ حِينَ يَبْزُغُ الْفَجْرُ. قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النبيصلى الله عليه وسلم يَفْعَلُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1675) عن عمرو بن خالد، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا أبو إسحاق، قال (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أذَّن وأقام لكلّ واحدة منهما","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1675).","chapter_en":"Those who gave an adhān and an iqāmah for each of the two prayers","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":92,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Isḥāq said: I heard ‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd say: ‘Abdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, performed Hajj, and we came to Muzdalifah around the time of the call for ‘Ishā’, or close to that. He ordered a man, who then gave the adhān and iqāmah, and then he prayed Maghrib. After it, he prayed two rak‘ahs, then he called for his supper and ate. Then he ordered — I think — and another adhān and iqāmah were given.","‘Amr said: I do not know that the uncertainty came from anyone except Zuhayr. Then he prayed ‘Ishā’ as two rak‘ahs. When dawn came, he said: The Prophet ﷺ would not pray at this hour except this prayer, in this place, on this day. Then ‘Abdullāh said: These are two prayers shifted from their normal times: Maghrib after the people come to Muzdalifah, and Fajr when dawn first breaks. He said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ do this."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1675)."},{"num":5142,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: مَا رَأَيْتُ النبيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صلّى صَلاَةً بِغَيْرِ مِيقَاتِهَا إلاّ صَلاَتَيْنِ: جَمَعَ بَيْنَ الْمَغْرِبِ وَالْعِشَاءِ، وَصَلَّى الْفَجْرَ قَبْلَ مِيقَاتِهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1682)، ومسلم في الحج (1289) كلاهما من طريق الأعمش، حدثني عمارة (هو ابن عمير التيميّ)، عن عبدالرحمن بن يزيد (النخعي)، عن عبدالله، فذكره، ولفظهما متقارب.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب صلاة الصبح يوم النحر بالمزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1682) and Muslim (1289).","chapter_en":"The Fajr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice at Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":93,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Mas‘ūd said: I did not see the Prophet ﷺ pray any prayer outside its usual time except two prayers: he combined Maghrib and ‘Ishā’, and he prayed Fajr before its usual time."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement in the hadith, “He prayed Fajr before its usual time,” does not mean that he prayed it before dawn had entered. Rather, it means that he prayed it earlier than the normal time at which it was usually prayed in residence. See: Fatḥ al-Bārī (3/525)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1682)، ومسلم (1289)."},{"num":5143,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: ثم ركب (يعني النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم) القصواء حتى أتى المشعر الحرام، فاستقبل القبلة، فدعاه وكبّره وهلّله، ووحّده، فلم يزل واقفاً حتى أسفر جداً... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره في الحديث الطويل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المشعر الحرام والوقوف به للدعاء والذكر بعد صلاة الصبح إلى أن يُسفر الفجر جدًّا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Going to al-Mash‘ar al-Ḥarām and standing there for supplication and remembrance after Fajr until the morning becomes very bright","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":94,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ‘Abdullāh said: Then he — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — mounted al-Qaṣwā’ until he came to al-Mash‘ar al-Ḥarām. He faced the qiblah, supplicated to Allah, magnified Him, uttered the tahlil, affirmed His oneness, and he remained standing until the morning became very bright… the hadith."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى: ( فَإِذَا أَفَضْتُم مِّنْ عَرَفَاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ عِندَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ ) [البقرة: ١٩٨]."],"en":["Allah the Most High said: “Then when you depart from ‘Arafāt, remember Allah at al-Mash‘ar al-Ḥarām.” [Al-Baqarah: 198]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5144,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَمْرِو بْنِ مَيْمُونٍ يَقُولُ: شَهِدْتُ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ صَلَّى بِجَمْعٍ الصُّبْحَ، ثُمَّ وَقَفَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ الْمُشْرِكِينَ كَانُوا لاَ يُفِيضُونَ حَتَّى تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ، وَيَقُولُونَ: أَشْرِقْ ثَبِيرُ. وَأَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَالَفَهُمْ، ثُمَّ أَفَاضَ قَبْلَ أَنْ تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1684) عن حجاج بن منهال، حدّثنا شعبة، عن أبي إسحاق، سمعت عمرو بن ميمون يقول (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الدفع من مزدلفة قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1684).","chapter_en":"Departing from Muzdalifah before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":95,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Amr ibn Maymūn said: I witnessed ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, pray Fajr at Jam‘, then he stood and said: The polytheists would not depart until the sun had risen, and they would say: “O Thabīr, shine!” But the Prophet ﷺ opposed them, and so he departed before the sun rose."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “Ashriq Thabīr,” means: O mountain, enter into the sunrise. “Thabīr” — with the thā’ fatḥah and the bā’ kasrah — is a mountain at Muzdalifah on the left side of the one going to Minā. It is also said that it is the greatest of the mountains of Makkah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1684)."},{"num":5145,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: فلم يزلْ (يعني النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم) واقفاً حتى أسفر جداً، فدفع قبل أن تطلع الشمس، وأردف الفضل بن عبّاس...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الدفع من مزدلفة قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Departing from Muzdalifah before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":95,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir said: He — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — continued standing until the morning became very bright, then he departed before the sun rose, and he had al-Faḍl ibn ‘Abbās ride behind him… the hadith."]},"buhuth":{"en":["It is from the Sunnah that the pilgrim depart from Muzdalifah before sunrise. Ṭāwūs said: The people of Jāhiliyyah used to depart from ‘Arafah before sunset, and from Muzdalifah after sunrise. So Allah delayed this and brought forward that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5146,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَفَ بِجَمْعٍ، فَلَمَّا أَضَاءَ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ قَبْلَ أَنْ تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ، أَفَاضَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (3020) عن أبي داود، عن زمعة، عن سلمة بن وهرام، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الدفع من مزدلفة قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan due to supporting chains: Narrated by Aḥmad (3020, 2051) and al-Tirmidhī (895). Al-Tirmidhī said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"Departing from Muzdalifah before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":95,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at Jam‘, and when everything became bright before the sun rose, he departed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (3020)، والترمذي (895)، وأحمد (2051). قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5147,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْفَضْلِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ وَكَانَ رَدِيفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،  أَنَّهُ قَالَ فِي عَشِيَّةِ عَرَفَةَ وَغَدَاةِ جَمْعٍ لِلنَّاسِ حِينَ دَفَعُوا: عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، وَهُْوَ كَافٌّ نَاقَتَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1282) من طريق أبي الزبير، عن أبي معبد مولى ابن عباس، عن ابن عباس، عن الفضل بن عباس، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الدفع من المزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1282).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":96,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Faḍl ibn ‘Abbās — and he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — said that on the evening of ‘Arafah and the morning of Jam‘, when the people departed, he said: “Remain calm,” while restraining his camel."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[5127],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1282)."},{"num":5148,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: إِنَّمَا كَانَ بَدْءُ الْإِيضَاعِ مِنْ قِبَلِ أَهْلِ الْبَادِيَةِ، كَانُوا يَقِفُونَ حَافَتَيِ النَّاسِ حَتَّى يُعَلِّقُوا الْعِصِيَّ وَالْجِعَابَ وَالْقِعَابَ، فَإِذَا نَفَرُوا، تَقَعْقَعَتْ تِلْكَ، فَنَفَرُوا بِالنَّاسِ، قَالَ: وَلَقَدْ رُئِيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَإِنَّ ذِفْرَىْ نَاقَتِهِ لَيَمَسُّ حَارِكَهَا، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ بِيَدِهِ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2193) وابن خزيمة (2863) والحاكم (1/465) وعنه البيقهي (5/126) كلهم من حديث حماد بن زيد، عن كثير بن شنظير، عن عطاء بن أبي رباح، عن ابن عباس، فذكره. واللفظ لأحمد. قال الحاكم: صحيح على شرط البخاي.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب السير في هدوء عند الدفع من المزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (2193), Ibn Khuzaymah (2863), and al-Ḥākim (1/465).","chapter_en":"Moving calmly when departing from Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":96,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbās said: The beginning of rushing came from the desert people. They would stand along the two sides of the people until they hung up the sticks, quivers, and bowls. When they set off, those things rattled, and so they caused the people to rush. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was seen while the area behind his she-camel’s ear nearly touched her withers, and he was saying with his hand: “O people, remain calm. O people, remain calm.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “al-īḍā‘,” means urging the camel and the like to move quickly."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2193)، وابن خزيمة (2863)، والحاكم (1/465)."},{"num":5149,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عبدالله، قَالَ: حَتَّى أَتَى بَطْنَ محسِّر، فحرَّك قَلِيلًا، ثُمَّ سَلَكَ الطَّرِيقَ الْوُسْطَى."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكر بطوله في صفة حجة النبيّ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الإسراع في المشي وتحريك الراكب دابته ونحوها في وادي محسِّر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Hastening on foot, and the rider urging his mount and the like in Wādī Muḥassir","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":97,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir said: When he came to the bottom of Muḥassir, he hastened a little, then took the middle road."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “the bottom of Muḥassir,” with the mīm ḍammah, the ḥā’ fatḥah, and the sīn with shaddah and kasrah, was named so because the elephant of the People of the Elephant grew exhausted and wearied there. Sharḥ al-Nawawī (8/189)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5150,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ، قَالَ: وَقَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ... وَجَمْعٌ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ. ثُمَّ أَفَاضَ حَتَّى انْتَهَى إِلَى وَادِي مُحَسِّرٍ فَقَرَعَ نَاقَتَهُ، فَخَبَّتْ حَتَّى جَاوَزَ الْوَادِيَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (885) في حديث طويل من حديث سفيان، عن عبدالرحمن بن الحارث بن عياش بن أبي ربيعة، عن زيد بن علي، عن أبيه، عن عبيدالله بن أبي رافع، عن علي بن أبي طالب، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الإسراع في المشي وتحريك الراكب دابته ونحوها في وادي محسِّر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (885). Al-Tirmidhī said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"Hastening on foot, and the rider urging his mount and the like in Wādī Muḥassir","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":97,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib said: When the Prophet ﷺ departed from Jam‘ and reached Wādī Muḥassir, he urged his she-camel, and it moved briskly until it passed the valley."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (885). قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح )).","voc":["tirmidhi",885]},{"num":5151,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّهُ قَالَ: رَدِفْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ، فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الشِّعْبَ الأَيْسَرَ الَّذِي دُونَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ أَنَاخَ، فَبَالَ ثُمَّ جَاءَ فَصَبَبْتُ عَلَيْهِ الْوَضُوءَ، فَتَوَضَّأَ وُضُوءًا خَفِيفًا. فَقُلْتُ: الصَّلاَةَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: الصَّلاَةُ أَمَامَكَ. فَرَكِبَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى أَتَى الْمُزْدَلِفَةَ، فَصَلَّى، ثُمَّ رَدِفَ الْفَضْلُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَدَاةَ جَمْعٍ.","قَالَ كُرَيْبٌ: فَأَخْبَرَنِي عبدالله بْنُ عَبَّاسٍ رضى الله عنهما، عَنِ الْفَضْلِ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم لَمْ يَزَلْ يُلَبِّي حَتَّى بَلَغَ الْجَمْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1669)، ومسلم في الحج (1280) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن محمد بن أبي حرملة، عن كريب مولى ابن عباس، عن أسامة بن زيد، فذكره. ولفظهما متقارب.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التلبية عند الدفع من المزدلفة إلى أن يرمي جمرة العقبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1669) and Muslim (1280).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of continuing the talbiyah when departing from Muzdalifah until stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":98,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd said: I rode behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ‘Arafāt. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the left pass below Muzdalifah, he made his camel kneel, urinated, then came back and I poured water for his ablution, and he made a light ablution. I said: “The prayer, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “The prayer is ahead of you.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode until he came to Muzdalifah and prayed. Then al-Faḍl rode behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the morning of Jam‘. Kurayb said: Then ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, informed me from al-Faḍl that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued making the talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1669)، ومسلم (1280)."},{"num":5152,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالرحمن بن يَزِيدَ، أنّ عبدالله لبَّى حِينَ أَفَاضَ مِنْ جَمْعٍ، فَقِيلَ: أَعْرَابِيٌّ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ عبدالله: أَنَسِيَ النّاسُ أمْ ضلُّوا؟ سَمِعْتُ الَّذِي أُنزلتْ عَلَيْهِ سُورَةُ الْبَقَرَةِ يَقُولُ فِي هَذَا الْمَكَانِ: لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1283) من طرق عن حصين، عن كثير بن مدرك الأشجعيّ، عن عبدالرحمن بن يزيد، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التلبية عند الدفع من المزدلفة إلى أن يرمي جمرة العقبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1283).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of continuing the talbiyah when departing from Muzdalifah until stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":98,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd reported that ‘Abdullāh made the talbiyah when he departed from Jam‘, so it was said: “Is this a Bedouin?” ‘Abdullāh replied: “Have the people forgotten, or have they gone astray? I heard the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed saying in this place: ‘Labbayka Allāhumma labbayk.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1283)."},{"num":5153,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالرحمن بن مُعَاذٍ التيمي قَالَ: خَطَبَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ بِمِنًى ففُتحتْ أَسْمَاعُنَا حتّى كنّا نَسْمَعُ مَا يَقُولُ وَنَحْنُ فِي مَنَازِلِنَا فَطَفِقَ يُعَلِّمُهُمْ مَنَاسِكَهُمْ حتّى بَلَغَ الْجِمَارَ فَوَضَعَ أُصْبُعَيْهِ السَّبَّابَتَيْنِ ثُمَّ قَالَ: بِحَصَى الْخَذْفِ. ثُمَّ أَمَرَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ فَنَزَلُوا فِي مُقَدَّمِ الْمَسْجِدِ، وَأَمَرَ الأَنْصَارَ فَنَزَلُوا مِنْ وَرَاءِ الْمَسْجِدِ، ثُمَّ نَزَلَ النَّاسُ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1957)، والنسائي (2996)، والإمام أحمد (16589)، والبيهقي (9608) كلّهم من حديث محمد بن إبراهيم التيميّ، عن عبدالرحمن بن معاذ التيميّ، قال (فذكر الحديث).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب نزول النبيّ المهاجرين والأنصار بمنى بعد عودته من المزدلفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1957), al-Nasā’ī (2996), Aḥmad (16589), and al-Bayhaqī (5/127).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s settling the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār in Minā after returning from Muzdalifah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":99,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Mu‘ādh al-Taymī said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us while we were in Minā, and our hearing became so open that we could hear what he was saying while we were in our camps. He began teaching them their rites until he reached the topic of the pebbles, then he placed his two index fingers together and said: “Like the pebbles used in slinging.” Then he ordered the Muhājirūn to settle in front of the mosque, and ordered the Anṣār to settle behind the mosque, and then the people settled after that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5270],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1957)، والنسائي (2996)، وأحمد (16589)، والبيهقي (9608)."},{"num":5154,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أَنَّهَا قَالَتِ:  اسْتَأْذَنَتْ سَوْدَةُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْلَةَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ تَدْفَعُ قَبْلَهُ، وَقَبْلَ حَطْمَةِ النَّاسِ، وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَةً ثَبِطَةً. يَقُولُ الْقَاسِمُ: وَالثَّبِطَةُ الثَّقِيلَةُ قَالَ: فَأَذِنَ لَهَا، فَخَرَجَتْ قَبْلَ دَفْعِهِ، وَحَبَسَنَا حَتَّى أَصْبَحْنَا، فَدَفَعْنَا بِدَفْعِهِ، وَلَأَنْ أَكُونَ اسْتَأْذَنْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَمَا اسْتَأْذَنَتْهُ سَوْدَةُ فَأَكُونَ أَدْفَعُ بِإِذْنِهِ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ مَفْرُوحٍ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحج (1681)، ومسلم في الحج (1290: 293) كلاهما من طريق أفلح بن حميد، عن القاسم بن محمد، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1681) and Muslim (1290:293), and this is the wording of Muslim.","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ā’ishah said: Sawdah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of Muzdalifah for permission to leave before him and before the crush of people — and she was a heavy woman. Al-Qāsim said: “Al-thabiṭah” means heavy. She said: So he permitted her, and she left before he did, while he kept us until morning, and we departed with his departure. And if I had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission just as Sawdah had asked him, so that I could depart by his permission, that would have been more beloved to me than something over which one rejoices greatly."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “before the ḥaṭmah of the people,” means before the crowding and crushing of people against one another."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1681)، ومسلم (1290: 293) واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5155,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَقُولُ أَنَا مِمَّنْ، قَدَّمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْلَةَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ فِي ضَعَفَةِ أَهْلِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1678)، ومسلم في الحج (1293) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، حدّثنا عبيدالله بن أبي يزيد، أنه سمع ابن عباس يقول (فذكره). واللفظ للبخاري، ولفظ مسلم قريب منه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1678) and Muslim (1293), and the wording is that of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbās said: I was among those whom the Prophet ﷺ sent ahead on the night of Muzdalifah with the weak members of his household."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1678)، ومسلم (1293)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":5156,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["أَخْبَرَنِي عَطَاءٌ، أَنَّ ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ:  بَعَثَ بِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِسَحَرٍ مِنْ جَمْعٍ فِي ثَقَلِ نَبِيِّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قُلْتُ: أَبَلَغَكَ أَنَّ ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: بَعَثَ بِي بِلَيْلٍ طَوِيلٍ؟ قَالَ: لَا، إِلَّا كَذَلِكَ بِسَحَرٍ، قُلْتُ لَهُ: فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: رَمَيْنَا الْجَمْرَةَ قَبْلَ الْفَجْرِ، وَأَيْنَ صَلَّى الْفَجْرَ؟ قَالَ: لَا، إِلَّا كَذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1294) عن عبد بن حميد، أخبرنا محمد بن بكر، أخبرنا ابن جريج، أخبرني عطاء (هو ابن أبي رباح)، أنّ ابن عباس قال (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1294).","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Aṭā’ reported from Ibn ‘Abbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me at dawn from Jam‘ with the baggage and family of the Prophet ﷺ. Ibn Jurayj said: I asked him, “Has it reached you that Ibn ‘Abbas said: He sent me in the latter part of the night?” He said: “No, only as stated: at dawn.” I asked him: “Did Ibn ‘Abbas say: We stoned the Jamrah before dawn? And where did he pray Fajr?” He said: “No, only as stated.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1294)."},{"num":5157,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ جُرَيْجٍ، أَخْبَرَنِي عَطَاءٌ، أَنَّ ابْنَ شَوَّالٍ، أَخْبَرَهُ  أَنَّهُ دَخَلَ عَلَى أُمِّ حَبِيبَةَ فَأَخْبَرَتْهُ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  بَعَثَ بِهَا مِنْ جَمْعٍ بِلَيْلٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1292) من طريق ابن جريج، أخبرني عطاء، أنّ شوّال أخبره، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1292). Muslim also narrated from Umm Ḥabībah that she said: “We used to do that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, departing in the darkness before dawn from Jam‘ to Minā.”","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sālim ibn Shawwāl — the freedman of Umm Ḥabībah — reported that he entered upon Umm Ḥabībah, and she informed him that the Prophet ﷺ had sent her from Jam‘ at night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1292). ورواه أيضا عن أم حبيبة قالت: (( كنا نفعله على عهد النبي ﷺ، نغلس من جمع إلى منى ))."},{"num":5158,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْفَضْلِ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَ ضَعَفَةَ بَنِي هَاشِمٍ أَنْ يَنْفِرُوا مِنْ جَمْعٍ بِلَيْلٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائيّ (3037) عن أبي داود قال: حدثنا أبو عاصم وعفان وسليمان، عن شعبة، عن مشاش، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس، عن الفضل، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3037), Aḥmad (1811), and Abū Ya‘lā (6734).","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Faḍl reported that the Prophet ﷺ instructed the weak among Banū Hāshim to depart from Jam‘ at night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3037)، وأحمد (1811)، وأبو يعلى (6734)."},{"num":5159,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  أَذِنَ لِضَعَفَةِ النَّاسِ مِنَ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ بِلَيْلٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (4892) والنسائي في الكبرى (4037) كلاهما من حديث عبد الرزاق، قال: أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهري، عن سالم، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة من النساء وغيرهن في الدفع من مزدلفة إلى منى في آخر الليل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (4892) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Kubrā (4037).","chapter_en":"The concession for weak women and others to depart from Muzdalifah to Minā in the latter part of the night","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":100,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Umar reported that the Prophet ﷺ gave permission to the weak among the people to leave Muzdalifah at night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (4892)، والنسائي في الكبرى (4037)."},{"num":5160,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ:  رَمَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْجَمْرَةَ يَوْمَ النَّحْرِ ضُحًى، وَأَمَّا بَعْدُ فَإِذَا زَالَتِ الشَّمْسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1299: 314) من طريق ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله يقول (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوقت المختار لرمي جمرة العقبة يوم النحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1299:314).","chapter_en":"The preferred time for stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":101,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ‘Abdullāh said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and after that, it was when the sun had passed the zenith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[5232],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1299: 314)."},{"num":5161,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ الْحُصَيْنِ، جَدَّتِهِ قَالَتْ:  حَجَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَجَّةَ الْوَدَاعِ، فَرَأَيْتُ أُسَامَةَ، وَبِلَالًا، وَأَحَدُهُمَا آخِذٌ بِخِطَامِ نَاقَةِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَالْآخَرُ رَافِعٌ ثَوْبَهُ يَسْتُرُهُ مِنَ الْحَرِّ حَتَّى رَمَى جَمْرَةَ الْعَقَبَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1298: 312) من طريق زيد بن أبي أنيسة، عن يحيى بن الحصين، عن أمّ الحصين جدّته، قالت (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوقت المختار لرمي جمرة العقبة يوم النحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1298:312).","chapter_en":"The preferred time for stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":101,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm al-Ḥuṣayn said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I saw Usāmah and Bilāl: one of them was holding the rein of the Prophet’s camel, and the other was raising his garment to shade him from the heat, until he stoned Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1298: 312)."},{"num":5162,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله مولى أسماء، قَالَ: قَالَتْ لِي أَسْمَاءُ ـ وَهِْيَ عِنْدَ دَارِ الْمُزْدَلِفَةِ ـ: هَلْ غَابَ الْقَمَرُ؟ قُلْتُ: لَا ، فَصَلَّتْ سَاعَةً، ثُمَّ قَالَتْ: يَا بُنيَّ هَلْ غَابَ الْقَمَرُ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَتِ: ارْحَلْ بِي. فَارْتَحَلْنَا حَتَّى رَمَتِ الْجَمْرَةَ، ثُمَّ صلَّتْ فِي مَنْزِلِهَا. فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: أيْ هَنَتاهْ، لَقَدْ غَلَّسْنَا! قَالَتْ: كَلَّا أيْ بُنيّ إنَّ النَّبي صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أذِن للظُعُن."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1679)، ومسلم في الحج (1291) كلاهما من طريق يحيى القطان، عن ابن جريج، قال: حدّثني عبدالله مولى أسماء. واللفظ لمسلم، ولفظ البخاريّ نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة أن يرموا في آخر الليل قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1679) and Muslim (1291), and the wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"The concession for the weak to stone in the latter part of the night before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":102,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullāh, the freedman of Asmā’, said: Asmā’ said to me while she was at the house in Muzdalifah: “Has the moon set?” I said: No. So she prayed for a while, then said: “My son, has the moon set?” I said: Yes. She said: “Then saddle up for me.” So we set out until she stoned the Jamrah, then she prayed in her lodging. I said to her: “O my aunt, we have come very early in darkness!” She said: “No, my son. The Prophet ﷺ gave permission to the women.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1679)، ومسلم (1291)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5163,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ شِهَابٍ، أَنَّ سَالِمَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَخْبَرَهُ،  أَنَّ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ كَانَ يُقَدِّمُ ضَعَفَةَ أَهْلِهِ، فَيَقِفُونَ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ بِالْمُزْدَلِفَةِ بِاللَّيْلِ، فَيَذْكُرُونَ اللهَ مَا بَدَا لَهُمْ، ثُمَّ يَدْفَعُونَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَقِفَ الْإِمَامُ، وَقَبْلَ أَنْ يَدْفَعَ، فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَقْدَمُ مِنًى لِصَلَاةِ الْفَجْرِ، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَقْدَمُ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ، فَإِذَا قَدِمُوا رَمَوُا الْجَمْرَةَ، وَكَانَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ يَقُولُ: أَرْخَصَ فِي أُولَئِكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1676)، ومسلم في الحج (1295) كلاهما من طريق يونس (هو ابن يزيد الأيلي)، عن ابن شهاب الزهريّ، به. واللفظ لمسلم، ولفظ البخاريّ نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة أن يرموا في آخر الليل قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1676) and Muslim (1295), and the wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"The concession for the weak to stone in the latter part of the night before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":102,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Shihāb reported that Sālim ibn ‘Abdullāh informed him that ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Umar used to send forward the weak members of his family. They would stand at al-Mash‘ar al-Ḥarām in Muzdalifah during the night, remembering Allah as much as they wished, then they would depart before the imam stood there and before he departed. Some of them would arrive at Minā in time for the Fajr prayer, and some would arrive after that. When they arrived, they would stone the Jamrah. Ibn ‘Umar used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave concession to those people."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1676)، ومسلم (1295)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5164,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، يَقُولُ أَرْسَلَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي ضَعَفَةِ أَهْلِهِ، فَصَلَّيْنَا الصُّبْحَ بِمِنًى وَرَمَيْنَا الْجَمْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائيّ (3048) عن محمد بن عبدالله بن عبد الحكم، عن أشهب، أنّ داود بن عبدالرحمن حدّثهم، أنّ عمرو بن دينار حدّثه، أنّ عطاء بن أبي رباح حدّثهم أنّه سمع ابن عباس يقول (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الرخصة للضعفة أن يرموا في آخر الليل قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3048) and Aḥmad (2460).","chapter_en":"The concession for the weak to stone in the latter part of the night before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":102,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with the weak members of his household, and we prayed Fajr in Minā and stoned the Jamrah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3048)، وأحمد (2460)."},{"num":5165,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدَّمَ ضَعَفَةَ أَهْلِهِ وَقَالَ: لاَ تَرْمُوا الْجَمْرَةَ حَتَّى تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (893) من حديث وكيع، عن المسعوديّ، عن الحكم، عن مقسم، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من كره الرمي قبل طلوع الشمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (893). Al-Tirmidhī said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"Those who disliked stoning before sunrise","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":103,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Abbās reported that the Prophet ﷺ sent forward the weak members of his household and said: “Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (893). قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5166,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: سُئِلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: رَمَيْتُ بَعْدَ مَا أَمْسَيْتُ. فَقَالَ: لاَ حَرَجَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1723) عن محمد بن المثنى، حدّثنا عبد الأعلى، حدّثنا خالد، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز الرمي مساءً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1723).","chapter_en":"The permissibility of stoning in the evening","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":104,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbās said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “I stoned after evening had come,” and he said: “There is no harm.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This indicates a transfer from the preferred time of stoning to a merely permissible time. The apparent meaning of the question is that it was on the Day of Sacrifice, because the preferred time is before the sun declines. So the Prophet ﷺ removed hardship from the one who stoned in the evening, and by analogy the same applies to one who stones at night, since part of the evening belongs to the night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1723)."},{"num":5167,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْفَضْلِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ وَكَانَ رَدِيفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،  أَنَّهُ قَالَ فِي عَشِيَّةِ عَرَفَةَ وَغَدَاةِ جَمْعٍ لِلنَّاسِ حِينَ دَفَعُوا: عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، وَهُْوَ كَافٌّ نَاقَتَهُ حَتَّى دَخَلَ مُحَسِّرًا - وَهُوَ مِنْ مِنًى - قَالَ: عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَصَى الْخَذْفِ الَّذِي يُرْمَى بِهِ الْجَمْرَةُ، وَقَالَ: لَمْ يَزَلْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُلَبِّي حَتَّى رَمَى الْجَمْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1282) من طرق، عن الليث بن سعد، عن أبي الزبير عن أبي معبد مولى ابن عباس، عن ابن عبـاس، عن الفضـل بن عباس، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب التقاط الحصى لرمي الجمرات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1282).","chapter_en":"Picking up the pebbles for stoning the pillars","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":105,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Faḍl ibn ‘Abbās — and he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — said that on the evening of ‘Arafah and the morning of Jam‘, as the people departed, he said: “Remain calm,” while restraining his camel, until he entered Muḥassir — which is part of Minā — and then said: “Use the pebbles of slinging with which the Jamrah is stoned.” And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued making the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[4906],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1282)."},{"num":5168,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الْعَالِيَةِ، قَالَ: قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَدَاةَ الْعَقَبَةِ وَهُوَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ: هَاتِ الْقُطْ لِي. فَلَقَطْتُ لَهُ حَصَيَاتٍ هُنَّ حَصَى الْخَذْفِ. فَلَمَّا وَضَعْتُهُنَّ فِي يَدِهِ قَالَ: بِأَمْثَالِ هَؤُلاَءِ، وَإِيَّاكُمْ وَالْغُلُوَّ فِي الدِّينِ! فَإِنَّمَا أَهْلَكَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكُمُ الْغُلُوُّ فِي الدِّينِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائيّ (3057)، وابن ماجه (3029)، وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (2867)، وابن حبان (3871)، والحاكم (1711) كلّهم من حديث عوف بن أبي جميـلة، عن زياد بن الحصين، عن أبي العاليـة، عن ابن عباس، فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب التقاط الحصى لرمي الجمرات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3057) and Ibn Mājah (3029), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2867) and Ibn Ḥibbān (3871).","chapter_en":"Picking up the pebbles for stoning the pillars","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":105,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Abbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the morning of al-‘Aqabah while he was on his mount: “Come, pick some pebbles for me.” So I picked up for him pebbles that were like the pebbles used in slinging. When I placed them in his hand, he said: “Like these. And beware of excessiveness in religion, for those before you were only destroyed by excessiveness in religion.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3057)، وابن ماجه (3029)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2867)، وابن حبان (3871)."},{"num":5169,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، عَنِ الْفَضْلِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ وَكَانَ رَدِيفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،  أَنَّهُ قَالَ فِي عَشِيَّةِ عَرَفَةَ وَغَدَاةِ جَمْعٍ لِلنَّاسِ حِينَ دَفَعُوا: عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ، وَهُْوَ كَافٌّ نَاقَتَهُ حَتَّى دَخَلَ مُحَسِّرًا - وَهُوَ مِنْ مِنًى - قَالَ: عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَصَى الْخَذْفِ الَّذِي يُرْمَى بِهِ الْجَمْرَةُ، وَقَالَ: لَمْ يَزَلْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُلَبِّي حَتَّى رَمَى الْجَمْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1282) من طريق الليث، عن أبي الزبير، عن أبي معبد مولى ابن عباس، عن ابن عباس، عن الفضل بن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أنّ حصى الجمار مثل حصى الخذف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1282).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pebbles for stoning the pillars are like the pebbles used for slinging","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":106,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Abbas narrated from al-Fadl ibn Abbas — and he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — that he said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah, when the people set out: “Remain calm,” while he was holding back his camel, until he entered Muhassir — which is part of Mina — then he said: “Use pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging, which are used to stone the pillar.” And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the pillar."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “with pebbles of slinging,” means pebbles about the size of a broad bean. Slinging means placing the pebble between the thumb and forefinger, then flicking it with the thumb."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1282)."},{"num":5170,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَمَى الْجَمْرَةَ بِمِثْلِ حَصَى الْخَذْفِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1299) من طريق ابن جريج، أخبرنا أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أنّ حصى الجمار مثل حصى الخذف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1299).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pebbles for stoning the pillars are like the pebbles used for slinging","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":106,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ stone the pillar with pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1299)."},{"num":5171,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ جُنْدُبٍ الْأَزْدِيَّةِ، أَنَّها سَمِعَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ قَالَ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّكِينَةِ وَالْوَقَارِ، وَعَلَيْكُمْ بِمِثْلِ حَصَى الْخَذْفِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (23219) عن هشيم، أخبرنا ليث، عن عبدالله بن شداد، عن أمّ جندب، فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أنّ حصى الجمار مثل حصى الخذف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (23219), Abu Dawud (1968, 1967, 1966), and Ibn Majah (3028).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pebbles for stoning the pillars are like the pebbles used for slinging","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":106,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Jundub al-Azdiyyah narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ, when he departed, say: “O people, keep to calmness and dignity, and use pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (23219)، وأبو داود (1968، 1967، 1966)، وابن ماجه (3028)."},{"num":5172,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الهرماس بن زِيَادٍ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ - وَأَنَا رَدِيفُ أَبِي، - وَهُوَ عَلَى نَاقَتِهِ الْعَضْبَاءِ يَوْمَ الْأَضْحَى وَالنَّاسُ حَوْلَهُ، فَقُلْتُ لِأَبِي: مَا يَقُولُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: يَقُولُ: ارْمُوا الْجِمَارَ بِمِثْلِ حَصَى الْخَذْفِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 533) من طريق أبي الوليد الطيالسيّ، عن عكرمة بن عمار، حدثني الهرماس بن زياد، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أنّ حصى الجمار مثل حصى الخذف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (22/203).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pebbles for stoning the pillars are like the pebbles used for slinging","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":106,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ while I was riding behind my father, and he was on his she-camel al-‘Adba’ on the Day of Sacrifice, with the people around him. I said to my father: What is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying? He said: He is saying: “Stone the pillars with pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 533)."},{"num":5173,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالرحمن بْنِ عُثْمَانَ التَّيْمِيِّ، قَالَ: أَمَرَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم أَنْ نَرْمِيَ الْجِمَارَ بِمِثْلِ حَصَى الْخَذْفِ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الدارمي (1939) وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (675) وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (636) كلهم من حديث عثمان بن عمر، نا عثمان بن مرة، عن أبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، عن عبد الرحمن بن عثمان التيمي، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أنّ حصى الجمار مثل حصى الخذف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Darimi (1939), Ibn Abi Asim in al-Ahad wa al-Mathani (675), and Ibn Qani‘ in Mu‘jam al-Sahabah (636).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pebbles for stoning the pillars are like the pebbles used for slinging","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":106,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us in the Farewell Pilgrimage to stone the pillars with pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الدارمي (1939)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (675)، وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (636)."},{"num":5174,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْأَعْمَشِ، قَالَ:  سَمِعْتُ الْحَجَّاجَ بْنَ يُوسُفَ يَقُولُ وَهُوَ يَخْطُبُ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ: أَلِّفُوا الْقُرْآنَ كَمَا أَلَّفَهُ جِبْرِيلُ السُّورَةُ الَّتِي يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا الْبَقَرَةُ، وَالسُّورَةُ الَّتِي يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا النِّسَاءُ، وَالسُّورَةُ الَّتِي يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا آلُ عِمْرَانَ.","قَالَ: فَلَقِيتُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِقَوْلِهِ. فَسَبَّهُ وَقَالَ: حَدَّثَنِي عبدالرحمن بْنُ يَزِيدَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ مَعَ عبدالله بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، فَأَتَى جَمْرَةَ الْعَقَبَةِ فَاسْتَبْطَنَ الْوَادِي، فَاسْتَعْرَضَهَا، فَرَمَاهَا مِنْ بَطْنِ الْوَادِي بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ يُكَبِّرُ مَعَ كُلِّ حَصَاةٍ. قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: يَا أَبَا عبدالرحمن إِنَّ النَّاسَ يَرْمُونَهَا مِنْ فَوْقِهَا؟ فَقَالَ: هَذَا وَالَّذِي لَا إِلَهَ غَيْرُهُ مَقَامُ الَّذِي أُنْزِلَتْ عَلَيْهِ سُورَةُ الْبَقَرَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1750)، ومسلم في الحجّ (1296: 306) كلاهما من طريق الأعمش، به، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الجمار تُرمى بسبع حصيات يكبّر مع كلّ حصاة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1750) and Muslim (1296/306), and the wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pillars are stoned with seven pebbles, saying “Allah is the Greatest” with each pebble","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":107,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-A‘mash said: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf say while he was preaching from the pulpit: “Arrange the Qur’an as Jibril arranged it: the chapter in which the cow is mentioned, the chapter in which women are mentioned, and the chapter in which the family of Imran is mentioned.” He said: Then I met Ibrahim and informed him of what he had said, so he insulted him and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated to me that he was with Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud, and he came to Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, went into the valley, positioned himself facing it, and stoned it from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles, saying “Allah is the Greatest” with each pebble. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, people stone it from above it. He said: By the One besides whom there is no god, this is the place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1750)، ومسلم (1296: 306)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5175,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر، قَالَ: حَتَّى أَتَى الْجَمْرَةَ الَّتِي عِنْدَ الشَّجَرَةِ، فَرَمَاهَا بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، يكبِّر مَعَ كلِّ حَصَاةٍ مِنْهَا...الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل المدني، عن جعفر بن محمّد، عن أبيه، عن جابر، فذكره في صفة حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الجمار تُرمى بسبع حصيات يكبّر مع كلّ حصاة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Clarifying that the pillars are stoned with seven pebbles, saying “Allah is the Greatest” with each pebble","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":107,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: Then he came to the pillar that was by the tree and stoned it with seven pebbles, saying “Allah is the Greatest” with each pebble from them… the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":5176,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالرحمن بن يَزِيدَ، أَنَّهُ حجّ مَعَ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ فَرَآهُ يَرْمِي الْجَمْرَةَ الْكُبْرَى بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، فَجَعَلَ الْبَيْتَ عَنْ يَسَارِهِ وَمِنًى عَنْ يَمِينِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: هَذَا مَقَامُ الَّذِي أُنزلتْ عَلَيْهِ سُورَةُ الْبَقَرَةِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1749)، ومسلم في الحج (1296: 305)كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم (هو النخعي)، عن عبدالرحمن بن يزيد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استقبال جمرة العقبة عند الرمي وجعل الكعبة عن اليسار ومنى عن اليمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1749) and Muslim (1296/305).","chapter_en":"Facing Jamrat al-‘Aqabah when stoning, with the Ka‘bah to the left and Mina to the right","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":108,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated that he performed Hajj with Ibn Mas‘ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and saw him stone the large pillar with seven pebbles. He placed the House to his left and Mina to his right, then said: This is the place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down ﷺ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1749)، ومسلم (1296: 305)."},{"num":5177,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عبدالله قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْمِي عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ يَوْمَ النَّحْرِ وَيَقُولُ: لِتَأْخُذُوا مَنَاسِكَكُمْ، فَإِنِّي لَا أَدْرِي لَعَلِّي لَا أَحُجُّ بَعْدَ حَجَّتِي هَذِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1297) من طريق عيسى بن يونس، عن ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابراً يقول (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب رمي الجمار راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1297).","chapter_en":"Stoning the pillars while riding and while walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":109,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ stoning while on his mount on the Day of Sacrifice, and he was saying: “Take your rites from me, for I do not know; perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this Hajj of mine.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[9306],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1297)."},{"num":5178,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَحْيَى بْنِ حُصَيْنٍ، عَنْ جَدَّتِهِ أُمِّ الْحُصَيْنِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُهَا تَقُولُ:  حَجَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَجَّةَ الْوَدَاعِ فَرَأَيْتُهُ حِينَ رَمَى جَمْرَةَ الْعَقَبَةِ، وَانْصَرَفَ، وَهُوَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ، وَمَعَهُ بِلَالٌ، وَأُسَامَةُ: أَحَدُهُمَا يَقُودُ بِهِ رَاحِلَتَهُ، وَالْآخَرُ رَافِعٌ ثَوْبَهُ عَلَى رَأْسِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الشَّمْسِ، قَالَتْ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَوْلًا كَثِيرًا، ثُمَّ سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: إِنْ أُمِّرَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَبْدٌ مُجَدَّعٌ (حَسِبْتُهَا قَالَتْ:) أَسْوَدُ يَقُودُكُمْ بِكِتَابِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى، فَاسْمَعُوا لَهُ وَأَطِيعُوا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1298) من طريق زيد بن أبي أنيسة، عن يحيى بن الحصين، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب رمي الجمار راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1298).","chapter_en":"Stoning the pillars while riding and while walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":109,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yahya ibn Husayn narrated from his grandmother Umm al-Husayn that she said: I heard her say: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I saw him when he stoned Jamrat al-‘Aqabah and departed while on his mount. Bilal and Usamah were with him, one of them leading his mount and the other holding up his garment over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the sun. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke many words, then I heard him say: “If a mutilated slave — I think she said: a black slave — is appointed over you and leads you by the Book of Allah, then listen to him and obey him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[5255],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1298)."},{"num":5179,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قُدَامَةَ بْنِ عبدالله، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْمِي الجماعة عَلَى نَاقَةٍ. وَفِي رِوَايَةِ: عَلَى نَاقَةٍ لَهُ صهباء لَيْسَ ضَرْبٌ وَلاَ طَرْدٌ، وَلاَ إِلَيْكَ إِلَيْكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (903)، والنسائيّ (3061)، وابن ماجه (3035)، كلّهم من حديث أيمن بن نابل، عن قدامة بن عبدالله، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب رمي الجمار راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (903), al-Nasa’i (3061), and Ibn Majah (3035). Al-Tirmidhi said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"Stoning the pillars while riding and while walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":109,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qudamah ibn Abd Allah said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ stone the pillars while on a she-camel. In another narration: on a reddish she-camel of his. There was no striking, no driving away, and no shouting, “Move aside, move aside.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (903)، والنسائي (3061)، وابن ماجه (3035). قال الترمذي: (( حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5180,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا رَمَى الْجِمَارَ مَشَى إِلَيْهَا ذَاهِبًا وَرَاجِعًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذيّ (900) عن يوسف بن عيسى، حدّثنا ابن نمير، عن عبيدالله، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب رمي الجمار راكبًا وماشيًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (900), who said: “Hasan Sahih.”","chapter_en":"Stoning the pillars while riding and while walking","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":109,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Umar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ, when he stoned the pillars, would walk to them going and returning."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (900) وقال: (( حسن صحيح ))."},{"num":5181,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَالِمِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا كَانَ يَرْمِي الْجَمْرَةَ الدُّنْيَا بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، ثُمَّ يُكَبِّرُ عَلَى إِثْرِ كُلِّ حَصَاةٍ، ثُمَّ يَتَقَدَّمُ فَيُسْهِلُ، فَيَقُومُ مُسْتَقْبِلَ الْقِبْلَةِ قِيَامًا طَوِيلاً، فَيَدْعُو وَيَرْفَعُ يَدَيْهِ، ثُمَّ يَرْمِي الْجَمْرَةَ الْوُسْطَى كَذَلِكَ، فَيَأْخُذُ ذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ فَيُسْهِلُ، وَيَقُومُ مُسْتَقْبِلَ الْقِبْلَةِ قِيَامًا طَوِيلاً، فَيَدْعُو وَيَرْفَعُ يَدَيْهِ، ثُمَّ يَرْمِي الْجَمْرَةَ ذَاتَ الْعَقَبَةِ مِنْ بَطْنِ الْوَادِي، وَلاَ يَقِفُ عِنْدَهَا، وَيَقُولُ: هَكَذَا رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَفْعَلُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1752) عن إسماعيل بن عبدالله، قال: حدثني أخي، عن سليمان، عن يونس بن يزيد، عن ابن شهاب، عن سالم بن عبدالله، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب رفع اليدين بالدعاء عند الجمرتين الدنيا والوسطى دون جمرة العقبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1752).","chapter_en":"Raising the hands in supplication at the first and middle pillars, but not at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":110,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated that Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to stone the first pillar with seven pebbles, then say “Allah is the Greatest” after each pebble. Then he would go forward to open ground and stand facing the qiblah for a long time, supplicating and raising his hands. Then he would stone the middle pillar in the same way, then go to the left side into open ground, and stand facing the qiblah for a long time, supplicating and raising his hands. Then he would stone Jamrat al-‘Aqabah from the bottom of the valley and would not stop there, and he would say: “This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11137],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1752)."},{"num":5182,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا رَمَيْتَ الْجِمَارَ، كَانَ لَكَ نُورًا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1140) عن إبراهيم بن سعيد الجوهري، ثنا سعيد بن عبد الحميد بن جعفر، ثنا ابن أبي الزناد، عن موسى بن عقبة، عن صالح مولى التؤمة، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الرمي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1140).","chapter_en":"What has been reported regarding the virtue of stoning","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":111,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you stone the pillars, it will be a light for you on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1140)."},{"num":5183,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الطُّفَيْلِ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: يَزْعُمُ قَوْمُكَ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، رَمَلَ بِالْبَيْتِ، وَأَنَّ ذَلِكَ سُنَّةٌ. فَقَالَ: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا. قُلْتُ: وَمَا صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا؟ قَالَ: صَدَقُوا، رَمَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْبَيْتِ، وَكَذَبُوا، لَيْسَ بِسُنَّةٍ، إِنَّ قُرَيْشًا قَالَتْ: زَمَنَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ: دَعُوا مُحَمَّدًا وَأَصْحَابَهُ حَتَّى يَمُوتُوا مَوْتَ النَّغَفِ، فَلَمَّا صَالَحُوهُ عَلَى أَنْ يَقْدَمُوا مِنَ العَامِ الْمُقْبِلِ، يُقِيمُوا بِمَكَّةَ ثَلاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ، فَقَدِمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَالْمُشْرِكُونَ مِنْ قِبَلِ قُعَيْقِعَانَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ: صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِأَصْحَابِهِ: ارْمُلُوا بِالْبَيْتِ ثَلاثًا، وَلَيْسَ بِسُنَّةٍ. قُلْتُ: وَيَزْعُمُ قَوْمُكَ أَنَّهُ طَافَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ عَلَى بَعِيرٍ، وَأَنَّ ذَلِكَ سُنَّةٌ. فَقَالَ: صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا. فَقُلْتُ: وَمَا صَدَقُوا وَكَذَبُوا؟ فَقَالَ: صَدَقُوا، قَدْ طَافَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ عَلَى بَعِيرٍ، وَكَذَبُوا، لَيْسَ بِسُنَّةٍ، كَانَ النَّاسُ لَا يُدْفَعُونَ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ، وَلا يُصْرَفُونَ عَنْهُ، فَطَافَ عَلَى بَعِيرٍ لِيَسْمَعُوا كَلامَهُ، وَلا تَنَالُهُ أَيْدِيهِمْ، قُلْتُ: وَيَزْعُمُ قَوْمُكَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَعَى بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ، وَأَنَّ ذَلِكَ سُنَّةٌ؟ قَالَ: صَدَقُوا، إِنَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ لَمَّا أُمِرَ بِالْمَنَاسِكِ، عَرَضَ لَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ عِنْدَ الْمَسْعَى فَسَابَقَهُ، فَسَبَقَهُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ، ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ بِهِ جِبْرِيلُ إِلَى جَمْرَةِ الْعَقَبَةِ، فَعَرَضَ لَهُ شَيْطَانٌ - قَالَ يُونُسُ: الشَّيْطَانُ - فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، حَتَّى ذَهَبَ، ثُمَّ عَرَضَ لَهُ عِنْدَ الْجَمْرَةِ الْوُسْطَى فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، قَالَ: قَدْ تَلَّهُ لِلجَبِينِ - قَالَ يُونُسُ: وَثَمَّ تَلَّهُ لِلجَبِينِ - وَعَلَى إِسْمَاعِيلَ قَمِيصٌ أَبْيَضُ، وَقَالَ: يَا أَبَتِ، إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ لِي ثَوْبٌ تُكَفِّنُنِي فِيهِ غَيْرُهُ، فَاخْلَعْهُ حَتَّى تُكَفِّنَنِي فِيهِ، فَعَالَجَهُ لِيَخْلَعَهُ، فَنُودِيَ مِنْ خَلْفِهِ: ﴿أَنْ يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا﴾ [الصافات: ١٠٥] فَالْتَفَتَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ، فَإِذَا هُوَ بِكَبْشٍ أَبْيَضَ أَقْرَنَ أَعْيَنَ.","قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا نتتبّع هذا الضَّرْبَ مِنَ الكِبَاشِ. قَالَ: ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ بِهِ جِبْرِيلُ إِلَى الْجَمْرَةِ الْقُصْوَى فَعَرَضَ لَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، حَتَّى ذَهَبَ ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ بِهِ جِبْرِيلُ إِلَى مِنًى قَالَ: هَذَا مِنًى  قَالَ يُونُسُ: هَذَا مُنَاخُ النَّاسِ ، ثُمَّ أَتَى بِهِ جَمْعًا، فَقَالَ: هَذَا الْمَشْعَرُ الْحَرَامُ، ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ بِهِ إِلَى عَرَفَةَ. فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: هَلْ تَدْرِي لِمَ سُمِّيَتْ عَرَفَةَ؟ قُلْتُ: لَا. قَالَ: إِنَّ جِبْرِيلَ قَالَ لِإِبْرَاهِيمَ: عَرَفْتَ؟  قَالَ يُونُسُ: هَلْ عَرَفْتَ؟  قَالَ: نَعَمْ .قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ فَمِنْ ثَمَّ سُمِّيَتْ عَرَفَةَ. ثُمَّ قَالَ هَلْ تَدْرِي كَيْفَ كَانَتِ التَّلْبِيَةُ؟ قُلْتُ: وَكَيْفَ كَانَتْ؟ قَالَ: إِنَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ لَمَّا أُمِرَ أَنْ يُؤَذِّنَ فِي النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ خَفَضَتْ لَهُ الْجِبَالُ رؤوسَها وَرُفِعَتْ لَهُ الْقُرَى، فَأَذَّنَ فِي النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2707)، وأبو داود الطيالسيّ (2820)، وعنه البيهقيّ (5/153 ـ 154) بطوله، وأبو داود (1885) مختصراً كلّهم من طريق حماد بن سلمة، عن أبي عاصم الغنويّ، عن أبي الطفيل، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سبب رمي الجمرات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (2707) and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi (2820).","chapter_en":"What has been reported regarding the reason for stoning the pillars","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":112,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu al-Tufayl said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal around the House and that this is a Sunnah. He said: They spoke the truth and they were mistaken. I said: What do you mean by that? He said: They spoke the truth that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal around the House, and they were mistaken in saying it is an established Sunnah. Quraysh said at the time of al-Hudaybiyah: Leave Muhammad and his companions until they die the death of infestation. Then when they made peace with him, allowing him to come the following year and stay in Makkah for three days, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while the polytheists were on the side of Qu‘ayqi‘an, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: “Perform ramal around the House for three circuits,” and it was not a permanent Sunnah. I said: And your people claim that he went between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel and that this is a Sunnah? He said: They spoke the truth and they were mistaken. I said: What do you mean? He said: They spoke the truth that he did go between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, and they were mistaken that it is a Sunnah. The people would not be pushed away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor turned back from him, so he went on a camel so they could hear his words and their hands could not reach him. I said: And your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed sa‘y between al-Safa and al-Marwah and that this is a Sunnah? He said: They spoke the truth. When Ibrahim was commanded with the rites, Satan confronted him at the place of sa‘y, so he raced him and Ibrahim outran him. Then Jibril took him to Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, and a devil appeared to him — Yunus said: Satan — so he stoned him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then he appeared to him at the middle pillar, and he stoned him with seven pebbles. He said: Then he laid him down on his forehead — Yunus said: then he laid him down on his forehead — and Isma‘il wore a white shirt and said: “My father, I have no garment other than this in which I may be shrouded, so remove it until you shroud me in it.” So he began trying to remove it, and then he was called from behind: “O Abraham, you have fulfilled the vision.” [al-Saffat 104–105] Then Ibrahim turned and saw a white horned ram with dark eyes.","Ibn Abbas said: I remember us searching for this kind of ram. Then Jibril took him to the furthest pillar, and Satan appeared to him there, so he stoned him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then Jibril took him to Mina and said: This is Mina — Yunus said: this is where the people camp — then he brought him to Muzdalifah and said: This is the Sacred Monument, then he took him to Arafah. Then Ibn Abbas said: Do you know why Arafah was named Arafah? I said: No. He said: Jibril said to Ibrahim: “Have you recognized it?” — Yunus said: “Did you recognize it?” — He said: Yes. Ibn Abbas said: That is why it was named Arafah. Then he said: Do you know how the talbiyah began? I said: How was it? He said: When Ibrahim was commanded to proclaim the pilgrimage among the people, the mountains lowered their heads for him and the towns were raised for him, so he proclaimed the pilgrimage to the people."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “al-naghaf,” with vowelization, refers to worms that are found in the noses of camels and sheep. Its singular is naghafah. Al-Nihayah (5/87)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (2707)، وأبو داود الطيالسي (2820)."},{"num":5184,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عَبَّاسٍ، أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، قَالَ: إنّ جِبْرِيلَ ذَهَبَ بِإِبْرَاهِيمَ إِلَى جَمْرَةِ الْعَقَبَةِ، فَعَرَضَ لَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ، فَسَاخَ، ثُمَّ أَتَى بِهِ الْجَمْرَةَ الْوُسْطَى، فَعَرَضَ لَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ فَسَاخَ، ثُمَّ أَتَى بِهِ الْجَمْرَةَ الْقُصْوَى فَعَرَضَ لَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَرَمَاهُ بِسَبْعِ حَصَيَاتٍ فَسَاخَ، فَلَمَّا أَرَادَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ أَنْ يَذْبَحَ ابْنَهُ إِسْحَاقَ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ: يَا أبتِ أَوْثِقْنِي لَا أَضْطَرِبُ، فَيَنْتَضِحَ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ دَمِي إِذَا ذَبَحْتَنِي فَشَدَّهُ، فَلَمَّا أَخَذَ الشَّفْرَةَ فَأَرَادَ أَنْ يَذْبَحَهُ نُودِيَ مِنْ خَلْفِهِ: ﴿أَنْ يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ (104) قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا﴾ [سورة الصافات: 104، 105] [الصّافات: 104-105]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (2794) عن يونس، أخبرنا حماد، عن عطاء بن السائب، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سبب رمي الجمرات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (2794).","chapter_en":"What has been reported regarding the reason for stoning the pillars","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":112,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril took Ibrahim to Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, and Satan appeared to him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles and he sank. Then he brought him to the middle pillar, and Satan appeared to him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles and he sank. Then he brought him to the furthest pillar, and Satan appeared to him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles and he sank. Then when Ibrahim intended to sacrifice his son Ishaq, he said to his father: ‘My father, tie me firmly so that I do not move and my blood does not splash on you when you slaughter me,’ so he tied him. Then when he took the blade and intended to slaughter him, he was called from behind: ‘O Abraham, you have fulfilled the vision.’” [al-Saffat 104–105]"]},"buhuth":{"en":["And in his saying, “Ishaq,” there is evidence that the narrator did not precisely preserve the name of the intended sacrifice, because the sound and established position held by the majority of the scholars is that the intended sacrifice was Isma‘il, peace be upon him, and the implication of the Qur’an indicates this.","I have discussed this matter in detail in my book “Studies in Judaism, Christianity, and the Religions of India”; refer to it, for you will find there what you will not find elsewhere."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (2794)."},{"num":5185,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا حَلَقَ رَأْسَهُ كَانَ أَبُو طَلْحَةَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ أَخَذَ مِنْ شَعَرِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الوضوء (171) عن محمد بن عبد الرحيم، قال: أخبرنا سعيد بن سليمان، قال: حدّثنا عبّاد، عن ابن عون، عن ابن سيرين، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (171) and Muslim (1305).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik narrated that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaved his head, Abu Talhah was the first to take some of his hair."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (171)، ومسلم (1305)."},{"num":5186,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ نَافِعٍ، أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَخْبَرَهُمْ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  حَلَقَ رَأْسَهُ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في المغازي (4410) من طريق أبي ضمرة، ومسلم في الحج (1304) من طريق يعقوب بن عبدالرحمن القاري، وحاتم بن إسماعيل، كلّهم عن موسى بن عقبة، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4410) and Muslim (1304). Ibn Khuzaymah also narrated it (2930), adding: “And they claimed that the one who shaved the Prophet ﷺ was Ma‘mar ibn Abd Allah ibn Nadlah ibn ‘Awf ibn ‘Ubayd ibn ‘Uwayj ibn ‘Adi ibn Ka‘b.”","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaved his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4410)، ومسلم (1304). ورواه ابن خزيمة (2930)، وزاد فيه: (( وزعموا أن الذي حلق النبي ﷺ معمر بن عبد الله بن نضلة بن عوف بن عبيد بن عويج بن عدي بن كعب ))."},{"num":5187,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ،  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَمَى جَمْرَةَ الْعَقَبَةِ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ إِلَى الْبُدْنِ فَنَحَرَهَا، وَالْحَجَّامُ جَالِسٌ، وَقَالَ بِيَدِهِ عَنْ رَأْسِهِ، فَحَلَقَ شِقَّهُ الْأَيْمَنَ، فَقَسَمَهُ فِيمَنْ يَلِيهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: احْلِقِ الشِّقَّ الْآخَرَ، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ أَبُو طَلْحَةَ، فَأَعْطَاهُ إِيَّاهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الحج (1305) من طرق عن هشام (هو الدّستوائيّ) عن محمد بن سيرين، عن أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1305) and al-Bukhari (171).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, then turned to the sacrificial camels and slaughtered them, while the barber was sitting. He gestured with his hand toward his head, so he shaved the right side of it and distributed it among those nearest to him. Then he said: “Shave the other side.” Then he said: “Where is Abu Talhah?” and gave it to him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (1305)، والبخاري (171)."},{"num":5188,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَعْمَرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: كُنْتُ أَرْحَلُ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ قَالَ: فَقَالَ لِي لَيْلَةً مِنَ اللَّيَالِي: يَا مَعْمَرُ، لَقَدْ وَجَدْتُ اللَّيْلَةَ فِي أَنْسَاعِي اضْطِرَابًا، قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: أَمَا وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ لَقَدْ شَدَدْتُهَا كَمَا كُنْتُ أَشُدُّهَا، وَلَكِنَّهُ أَرْخَاهَا مَنْ قَدْ كَانَ نَفَسَ عَلَيَّ مَكَانِي مِنْكَ، لِتَسْتَبْدِلَ بِي غَيْرِي، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَمَا إِنِّي غَيْرُ فَاعِلٍ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا نَحَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَدْيَهُ بِمِنًى، أَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَحْلِقَهُ، قَالَ: فَأَخَذْتُ الْمُوسَى فَقُمْتُ عَلَى رَأْسِهِ، قَالَ: فَنَظَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي وَجْهِي وَقَالَ لِي: يَا مَعْمَرُ، أَمْكَنَكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ شَحْمَةِ أُذُنِهِ، وَفِي يَدِكَ الْمُوسَى؟ قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: أَمَا وَاللهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ ذَلِكَ لَمِنْ نِعْمَةِ اللَّهِ عَلَيَّ وَمَنِّهِ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَجَلْ إِذًا أُقِرُّ لَكَ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ حَلَقْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (27249)، والطبرانيّ في الكبير (20/447 ـ 448) كلاهما من حديث ابن إسحاق، قال: حدثني يزيد بن أبي حبيب المصريّ، عن عبدالرحمن بن عقبة مولى معمر بن عبدالله بن نافع بن نضلة العدويّ، عن معمر بن عبدالله، فذكره. ولفظهما سواء إلا في أحرف.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (27249) and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (20/447–448).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ma‘mar ibn Abd Allah said: I used to saddle the mount for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: One night he said to me: “O Ma‘mar, tonight I found looseness in my straps.” I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I fastened them just as I used to fasten them, but someone who envied my place with you loosened them so that you might replace me with someone else. He said: “As for me, I will not do that.” Then when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his offering in Mina, he ordered me to shave his head. I took the razor and stood over his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked into my face and said to me: “O Ma‘mar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has enabled you to hold the lobe of his ear while the razor is in your hand?!” I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that is indeed among Allah’s blessings and favors upon me. He said: “Yes, then let it be affirmed for you.” Then I shaved the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “ansā‘ī,” is the plural of nis‘ah — with the nūn carrying kasrah and the sīn being still — and it means broad woven straps used to tie onto the rear of the camel.","His statement, “nafisa,” with the fa’ carrying kasrah, is from the expression meaning to envy someone for something when you think him worthy of it. This was mentioned by al-Sindi."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (27249)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/447-448)."},{"num":5189,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: لَمَّا أَرَادَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يَحْلِقَ الْحَجَّامُ رَأْسَهُ، أَخَذَ أَبُو طَلْحَةَ بِشَعْرِ أَحَدِ شِقَّيْ رَأْسِهِ بِيَدِهِ، فَأَخَذَ شَعَرَهُ، فَجَاءَ بِهِ إِلَى أُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، قَالَ: فَكَانَتْ أُمُّ سُلَيْمٍ تَدُوفُهُ فِي طِيبِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (12483) عن حسن (هو ابن موسى)، حدّثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت البنانيّ، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (12483).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted the barber to shave his head, Abu Talhah took in his hand the hair from one side of his head, then took it and brought it to Umm Sulaym. He said: Umm Sulaym used to mix it into her perfume."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “she mixed it into her perfume,” means that she blended it into it. It is said: he mixed it with water, meaning he moistened it with it and blended it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9511],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (12483)."},{"num":5190,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْحَلَّاقُ يَحْلِقُهُ، وَقَدْ أَطَافَ بِهِ أَصْحَابُهُ، مَا يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَقَعَ شَعَرَةٌ إِلَّا فِي يَدِ رَجُلٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (12363) عن سليمان بن حرب، حدّثنا سليمان بن المغيرة، عن ثابت، عن أنس، فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2325).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the barber was shaving him, and his companions had surrounded him, wanting that not a single hair should fall except into the hand of one of the men."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2325)."},{"num":5191,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، أَنَّ أَبَاهُ حَدَّثَهُ، أَنَّهُ شَهِدَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عِنْدَ الْمَنْحَرِ، وَرَجُلًا مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، وَهُوَ يَقْسِمُ أَضَاحِيَّ، فَلَمْ يُصِبْهُ مِنْهَا شَيْءٌ وَلَا صَاحِبَهُ، فَحَلَقَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَأْسَهُ فِي ثَوْبِهِ، فَأَعْطَاهُ، فَقَسَمَ مِنْهُ عَلَى رِجَالٍ، وَقَلَّمَ أَظْفَارَهُ، فَأَعْطَاهُ صَاحِبَهُ، قَالَ: فَإِنَّهُ لَعِنْدَنَا مَخْضُوبٌ بِالْحِنَّاءِ وَالْكَتَمِ، يَعْنِي: شَعْرَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16474، 16475)، وابن خزيمة (2931)، والحاكم (1744) كلّهم من حديث أبان العطّار، قال: حدثني يحيى ـ يعني ابن أبي كثير ـ، عن أبي سلمة، عن محمد بن عبدالله بن زيد، أنّ أباه حدّثه، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلق رسول الله ﷺ رأسه في حجّة الوداع، وتقسيم شعره بين الناس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (16475, 16474), Ibn Khuzaymah (2931), and al-Hakim (1744).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaving his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage and distributing his hair among the people","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":113,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd narrated that his father told him that he witnessed the Prophet ﷺ at the place of sacrifice, and there was a man from Quraysh while he was distributing sacrificial animals. Neither he nor his companion received any of them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaved his head into his garment and gave it to him, so he distributed some of it among men. Then he clipped his nails and gave them to his companion. He said: It is still with us dyed with henna and katam, meaning his hair."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16475، 16474)، وابن خزيمة (2931)، والحاكم (1744)."},{"num":5192,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ، أنّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ ارْحَمِ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ. قَالُوا: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ ارْحَمِ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ. قَالُوا: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحجّ (184) عن نافع، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (184), al-Bukhari (1727), and Muslim (1301/317).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, have mercy on those who shave.” They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “O Allah, have mercy on those who shave.” They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “And those who shorten.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated it with the wording: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “And those who shorten.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13333],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (184)، والبخاري (1727)، ومسلم (1301/317)."},{"num":5193,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ، قَالَ:  حَلَقَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَحَلَقَ طَائِفَةٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، وَقَصَّرَ بَعْضُهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحج (1729) من طريق جويرية بن أسماء، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1729) and Muslim (1301). It also adds: Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May Allah have mercy on those who shave,” once or twice, then he said, “and those who shorten.”","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ shaved his head, and a group of his companions shaved their heads, while some of them only shortened their hair."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1729)، ومسلم (1301). وزاد: قال عبد الله بن عمر: إن رسول الله ﷺ قال: (( رحم الله المحلقين )) مرة أو مرتين، ثم قال: (( والمقصرين ))."},{"num":5194,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، أنّ النبيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ: اللهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ فَقَالَ رجلٌ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟ فَقَالَ: اللهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ. فَقَالَ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟. قَالَ: حَتَّى قَالَهَا ثَلَاثًا، أَوْ أَرْبَعًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (4897، 6384) عن عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن أيوب، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (6384, 4897). Ibn Abi Shaybah also narrated it (14/452) through another route from Ibn Umar within the story of al-Hudaybiyah, and it explicitly states that he ﷺ said this on the Day of al-Hudaybiyah. He also said it in the Farewell Pilgrimage.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Umar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of al-Hudaybiyah: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” A man said: And those who shorten? So he said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” He said: And those who shorten? He said that after saying it three or four times, he said: “And those who shorten.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["There is no contradiction between the two reports, so there is no need to reject that he also said this on the Day of al-Hudaybiyah. Whoever denies that bases his denial on not knowing it, and lack of knowledge is not knowledge, as is said. The sound and established view held by the verifying scholars is that he first said this at al-Hudaybiyah, then repeated it during the Farewell Pilgrimage, as is also explicitly stated in the upcoming hadith of Umm al-Husayn al-Aslamiyyah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (6384، 4897). ورواه ابن أبي شيبة (14/452) من وجه آخر عن ابن عمر ضمن قصة الحديبية، وفيه تصريح بأنه ﷺ قال ذلك يوم الحديبية. كما قال ذلك أيضا في حجة الوداع."},{"num":5195,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ، قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ، قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ، قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ، قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ، قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ، قَالَ: وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاريّ في الحجّ (1728)، ومسلم في الحجّ (1302) كلاهما من طريق محمد بن فضيل، حدّثنا عُمارة بن القعقاع، عن أبي زرعة، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره. واللّفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1728) and Muslim (1302), and the wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “And those who shorten.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1728)، ومسلم (1302). واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":5196,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أمّ الْحُصَيْنِ الأسلميّة، أَنَّهَا سَمِعَتِ النّبيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حجّة الْوَدَاعِ دَعَا لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ ثَلَاثًا، وَلِلْمُقَصِّرِينَ مرّة."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحجّ (1303) من طريق شعبة، عن يحيى بن الحصين، عن جدّته، أنّها سمعت النبيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم (فذكرته).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1303).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm al-Husayn al-Aslamiyyah narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage supplicate three times for those who shaved, and once for those who shortened."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1303)."},{"num":5197,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: حَلَقَ رِجَالٌ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ وَقَصَّرَ آخَرُونَ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ :يَرْحَمُ اللَّهُ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟ قَالَ:يَرْحَمُ اللَّهُ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ قَالُوا:يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟ قَالَ:يَرْحَمُ اللَّهُ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ قَالُوا:يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟ قَالَ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ. قَالُوا: فَمَا بَالُ الْمُحَلِّقِينَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ظَاهَرْتَ لَهُمُ الرَّحْمَةَ؟قَالَ:لَمْ يشكُّوا قَالَ: فَانْصَرَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (3311)، واللّفظ له، والطّحاويّ في شرح معانيه (4057)، وابن ماجه (3045) مختصراً، كلّهم من حديث محمد بن إسحاق، حدّثني عبدالله بن أبي نجيح، عن مجاهد، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (3311), and this is his wording, also by al-Tahawi in Sharh Ma‘anihi (4057), and Ibn Majah (3045).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abdullah ibn Abbas said: Some men shaved on the Day of al-Hudaybiyah, while others shortened their hair. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “May Allah have mercy on those who shave.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: “And those who shorten.” They said: Why is it, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that you singled out those who shave with repeated mercy? He said: “Because they did not doubt.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “you singled them out with repeated mercy,” means that you gathered and repeated mercy for them.","His saying, “they did not doubt,” means that they did not act like one who doubts whether it is permissible to exit the state of consecration. The one who shortened his hair acted as though he hesitated about full completion, so he limited his release to only part of it. As for the one who shaved, there was no doubt from him; meaning he did not act like one who doubts that the more complete following is better. But the one who shortened was treated like someone uncertain in that regard, because he left what was more complete. This was mentioned by al-Sindi in his commentary on the Musnad."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (3311)، واللفظ له، والطحاوي في شرح معانيه (4057)، وابن ماجه (3045)."},{"num":5198,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَالِكِ بن رَبِيعَةَ، أنّه سَمِعَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: اللهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُحَلِّقِينَ. قَالَ: يَقُولُ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ؟ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ فِي الثَّالِثَةِ أَوْ فِي الرَّابِعَةِ: وَالْمُقَصِّرِينَ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: وَأَنَا يَوْمَئِذٍ مَحْلُوقُ الرَّأْسِ، فَمَا يَسُرُّنِي بِحَلْقِ رَأْسِي حُمْرُ النَّعَمِ أَوْ فِطْراً عَظِيمًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (17598) من حديث أوس بن عبيدالله أبي مقاتل السّلوليّ، قال: حدّثني بريد بن أبي مريم، عن أبيه مالك بن ربيعة، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ للمحلّقين بالرّحمة ثلاث مرّات وللمقصّرين مرة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (17598), al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (9/275), and in al-Awsat as cited in Majma‘ al-Bahrayn (1777).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s supplication for mercy upon those who shave three times, and upon those who shorten once","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":114,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Malik ibn Rabi‘ah narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive those who shave.” A man from the people said: And those who shorten? Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, on the third or fourth time, said: “And those who shorten.” Then he said: On that day I myself had my head shaved, and I would not have been pleased to trade my shaving for red camels or for a great wealth."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (17598)، والطبراني في الكبير (9/275)، وفي الأوسط كما في مجمع البحرين (1777)."},{"num":5199,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَيْسَ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ الْحَلْقُ إِنَّمَا عَلَى النِّسَاءِ التَّقْصِيرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود من وجهين: أحدهما (1985) عن أبي يعقوب البغداديّ ـ ثقة ـ، حدّثنا هشام بن يوسف، عن ابن جريج، عن عبد الحميد ابن جبير بن شيبة، عن صفية بنت شيبة، قالت: أخبرتني أمُّ عثمان بنت أبي سفيان، أنّ ابن عباس، قال (فذكره).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ليس على النساء حلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب الحج","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (1985), al-Daraqutni (2666), and al-Bayhaqi (5/104).","chapter_en":"Women are not required to shave their heads","part_en":"The Book of Pilgrimage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة حجّة النبي ﷺ كما رواها جابر وغيره، وما جاء فيه من الأحكام","group_en":"Sections on the description of the Prophet’s Hajj as narrated by Jābir and others, and the rulings derived from it","part_no":16,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":115,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Women are not required to shave; rather, women are only required to shorten their hair.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1985)، والدارقطني (2666)، والبيهقي (9406)."}]);